ks continues tonight. Yes, just moments ago, "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " reported that documents describing a foreign government's nuclear capabilities were recovered during the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raid on Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 Now, as we've just observed, time and time again over the past, like, seven years now, the regime media stenographers were ready to feed the cycle of leaks.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It seems to me that that this is the sort of thing that makes it more likely that ultimately we'll see a criminal charge here- -\par \par \uc2 CHRIS HAYES, MSNBC HOST: Some of the information at least, at least according to reporting sources, was basically at the upper, upper echelons of how closely held it would be by the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Classified information that being described is not and can't possibly be shielded by executive privilege. In other words, he didn't have a right to have it. He didn't have a right to have it in his beach house. The end of discussion.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The Post's" sources are people familiar with the investigation. All right. And the media then they want us to believe that the, what, the DOJ and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  are above being questioned their integrity, their bias, you can't talk about it ever. But with every leak their credibility diminishes.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , former Senior Adviser to President Trump, Founder of America First Legal, also joining me now is Victor Davis Hanson, \uc2 Hoover Institution\uc2 , Senior Fellow.\par \par \uc2 Stephen, you and I ran into each other in the elevator moments ago and you said it seems like it's Groundhog Day all over again. How many times have we been through this, and how many times has \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  gotten up there and been so, like, indignant to anyone question the integrity or the unbiased nature of the DOJ?\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER\uc2 , FORMER TRUMP SENIOR ADVISER: Well, first of all, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  stood before the American people and he said, we will speak through our filings not through leaks. And yet it's been one salacious, manipulated, fabricated leak after another.\par \par \uc2 And if he cared, which he doesn't, but if he cared at all about justice in America, he would be empaneling a grand jury tonight to investigate the leakers in his own agency, who are the ultimate perversion of justice in America.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Victor, here's what one of the authors of this "\uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " piece just admitted on MSNBC. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAROL LEONNIG, THE WASHINGTON POST REPORTER: We don't know how much, we don't know which foreign government is involved. We have some theories. But we published what we can establish with great certainty, and that is that among the record seized there were details so classified, so concerning that it was covered by this classification, material that relates to a foreign government's nuclear capacity.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. Let me just say, Victor, as someone who's been around this town way too long, I don't want to admit how long, she doesn't know anything. OK. She was given information by either someone at the White House who was fed it. And so when went through an intermediary, probably from DOJ, to the White House, then to her. But she's acting like she's Edward R. Murrow, like doing like, gumshoe reporting here.\par \par \uc2 Ain't doing anything. She's just being spoon fed information about this investigation. These are journalists? Come on.\par \par \uc2 VICTOR DAVIS HANSON, SENIOR FELLOW, \uc2 HOOVER INSTITUTION\uc2 : Yes, I mean, it's really ironic because we just - why were we leaking because we so - we had this disinterested special master that was taking charge, and they were going to adjudicate the entire files. And it was almost like they went into panic and they wanted to prejudice whatever that finding might be by polluting the well.\par \par \uc2 And then the two authors of "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " new scoop, Mr. Barrett and Leonnig, they were central in the Russian collusion hoax. He won a Pulitzer Prize for assuring the nation that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  colluded with the Russians and he was involved in the Mueller bombshells, walls are closing in stories.\par \par \uc2 And so he wrote a book called the "October Surprise" the author of this latest news story. It's telling us not to trust the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , because they leaked unfairly about \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 . So their credibility is not very good. And I think it's a pattern, Laura, we saw the January 6 die-in, die- off and then it was resurrected with a raid, and then it died off. And then we had the documents on the ground in surreal photos.\par \par \uc2 And then we went into semi fascism. And then we went into that Phantom of the Opera set and half the country is a threat to democracy. And now we're back with another psychodrama. And we're not talking about a 3 million person flowing across the border, or unsafe to walk in American streets or stagflation and inflation at the same time, all the issues that we care about. We're only going to talk about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the latest manufactured psychodrama.\par \par \uc2 And you can see it's Georgia 2020 all over again. Try to get two people that otherwise would not be elected by diverting the people from the issues.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Stephen, it would not be a night of leaks or not for the star of Russiagate appearing.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOHN BRENNAN, FORMER CIA DIRECTOR: I always raised the question in my mind, why did he select these documents among the 1,000s upon 1,000s that passed his hands? It really raises serious, serious concerns about what he was planning to do with the document or may have already done with these documents and the information in there.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: God, that man is a buffoon. I mean, does anyone think for a second? I mean, you know, President Trump well, was he hand selecting documents and placing them in boxes? Is that what we think happened here, Steve?\par \par \uc2 HANSON: Well, first of all, Brennan--\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Do you think that happened, yes or no? Don't go to the next point. I just asked you a question.\par \par \uc2 MILLER: No, but--\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Do you think that happened?\par \par \uc2 MILLER: No. But more importantly even than that point is the fact that we are the victims of a psyop like Brennan and his friends had been running for seven years. In other words, you go back to the Russia scandal, it was always one bombshell, one breaking exclusive, one huge piece of news, one earth shattering revelation after another after another. Everyone false, everyone empty, everyone built on a mountain of lies.\par \par \uc2 And we are now living through it again, in real-time, with the same corrupt beltway media pushing those lies down our throats.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: How about her saying, well, we have theories going back to Carol Leonnig, who was the repository of the latest leak tonight. We did change the whole top of this show, because it's like - but she said, well, we have our theories, but we published what we know. But she doesn't know it. She is given this information. But you see what, how it all works, and they work in tandem together. This is constantly the case with anything related to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MILLER: Yes. And if you actually read that sentence in "The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 ", it's the most tortured sentence you could possibly - that there is a document that may be referred to a thing that could have been somewhere that was something. For all we know it was a printout of a Wikipedia page.\par \par \uc2 The point is, that 