e most consequential election of our lifetimes. You assume \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was incapacitated and couldn't change much.\par \par \uc2 Well, true, he is incapacitated, but the people behind him most definitely are not. They are more ideological and more aggressive than ever. Now, it turns out among those people is our largest and most heavily armed Federal law enforcement agency. That would be the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  is not allowed to insert itself into domestic politics. That would violate the US Constitution. It is completely illegal.\par \par \uc2 But for several years, it has become increasingly clear that that is exactly what the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is doing, actively working on behalf of the Democratic Party, mocking the rule of law, subverting our democracy from within far more effectively than any foreign government ever could.\par \par \uc2 If that sounds like an overheated claim, and it definitely does sound like an overheated claim, unfortunately, you should know it's entirely true. We know that for a fact.\par \par \uc2 Here is how we know and we learned it yesterday. Weeks before the 2020 election, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  pressured social media companies to kill the story of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop. Why? Because that was a story that might have prevented \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from becoming President. That happened.\par \par \uc2 And we know this not because "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 " investigated it. They didn't bother. They didn't bring you a special report in yesterday's paper giving you the details. "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " would never do that, even if they knew it to be true and they may.\par \par \uc2 No, we know this instead, because \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  of \uc2 Facebook\uc2  blithely admitted it almost parenthetically during an interview with Joe Rogan. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE ROGAN, PODCAST HOST: There was a lot of attention on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  during the election because of the Hunter Biden laptop story. "The New York Post" --\par \par \uc2 MARK ZUCKERBERG\uc2 , CEO, \uc2 META\uc2 : Yes, we had it, too.\par \par \uc2 ROGAN: So, you guys censored that as well?\par \par \uc2 ZUCKERBERG: So, we took a different path than \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . I mean, basically the background here is the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , I think basically came to us, some folks on our team and was like, "Hey, just so you know, like, you should be on high alert. We thought there was a lot of Russian propaganda in the 2016 election. We have it on notice that basically there's about to be some kind of dump of -- that's similar to that, so just be vigilant."\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Oh, so Zuckerberg, just to be clear, you just saw it, but let's just unwind what we saw. Zuckerberg was asked, "Why did you censor the story about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop?" And he said, "some folks from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  came to us and indicated there was about to be a dump of Russian propaganda."\par \par \uc2 Now, there is some rewriting of history going on, in which some are claiming, some on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  are claiming actually, that the visit from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  had nothing to do with the Hunter Biden laptop, but the answer you just saw was in response to a question about the laptop and the censorship of it and the answer was Russian propaganda, Russian disinformation.\par \par \uc2 Neither of those terms has an agreed upon meaning. They don't actually mean anything. What's Russian propaganda? Is it true? That should be the only question that any news or information company, including \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , ever asked. Is it true? Truth is the defense. No. It's Russian propaganda. Again, a term without a meaning.\par \par \uc2 So, we wanted to know more. We reached out to \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  after that interview and he responded to us to his credit.\par \par \uc2 Zuckerberg confirmed that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  didn't put any of these warnings about Russian disinformation propaganda in writing. Of course, they didn't. Nothing in writing. And that makes sense if you're the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , you wouldn't want to put that in writing because you were, of course, lying.\par \par \uc2 At the moment, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was warning \uc2 Facebook\uc2  about a propaganda dump that obviously would include \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop, they had \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop in their possession.\par \par \uc2 So, they knew perfectly well it was authentic as anyone who looks at it does. We have looked at it and it is instantly obvious this is real and of course, we now know conclusively it is real.\par \par \uc2 So, that laptop was not censored because it was propaganda, whatever that means. By the way, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  should never be in the information control business anyway. It was censored because it might hurt \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is the government agency that pushed for it to be censored.\par \par \uc2 Has that ever happened in the United States, ever?\par \par \uc2 That is the definition of police state behavior: A government agency independently decides it's going to determine the outcome of a supposedly democratic election.\par \par \uc2 So, why is it nearly two years until we learn this? Well, it turns out \uc2 Facebook\uc2  is a very political place. The founder of \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2 , paid hundreds of millions of dollars to affect the outcome of the election. Famously, we've reported on that. And then, of course, there were Democratic Party operatives working within \uc2 Facebook\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So, on October 14th, the \uc2 Facebook\uc2  communications official and former Democratic Party operative called \uc2 Andy Stone\uc2  claimed that \uc2 Facebook\uc2  was censoring this story because of \uc2 Facebook\uc2 's "standard process to reduce the spread of misinformation" whatever that means, but that was their initial explanation.\par \par \uc2 It wasn't until