par \uc2 CARLSON: So, those are the shills who will say whatever they're told to say. Of course, no sober person would take them seriously and we missed the bigger story, too. We will admit that.\par \par \uc2 At the time, we imagined that this lie, that the laptop was Russian misinformation, was being pushed almost exclusively by Democratic partisans, but that's not true. It was much worse and much more threatening to our democracy, in fact, utterly corrosive of our democracy than that.\par \par \uc2 Again, our media attributed these claims to former Intel officials who wrote a letter about Russian disinformation, but no, it wasn't just former Intel officials spreading that lie. It was members of the \uc2 US government\uc2 , Federal bureaucrats, people who work for Federal agencies, senior \uc2 FBI\uc2  leaders who are still at the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . They lied and they knew they were lying and they never took steps to validate this claim that it was Russian propaganda or Russian disinformation.\par \par \uc2 On this show in October of 2020, we interviewed one of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's business partners, a man called Tony Bobulinski, and he verified the authenticity of that laptop.\par \par \uc2 He had firsthand information. He had texts and e-mails that were on his phone and also on the laptop.\par \par \uc2 So, we reached out to Tony Bobulinski last night and we asked him a very simple question: Did anyone from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  ever call you or your lawyer to find out since your name was all over the laptop, if those texts and e- mails were real? If they wanted to know if this was Russian disinformation, they would, of course, call you? But not one of them ever did.\par \par \uc2 They knew it wasn't Russian disinformation. They knew it wasn't propaganda, and they knew it was completely real and they lied about it. Here's what Bobulinski told us in October of 2020.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TONY BOBULINSKI, FORMER \uc2 HUNTER BIDEN\uc2  ASSOCIATE: On May 13th, that e-mail was sent from James Gilliar to me. I didn't generate that e-mail, James Gilliar generated that e-mail.\par \par \uc2 And in that email, James Gilliar goes through intimate detail of what each individual's requests were from a compensation perspective and how the equity in the enterprise would be divvied up. Very important. May 13th.\par \par \uc2 That e-mail was generated by somebody else to me. In that e-mail, there is a statement where they go through the equity. Jim Biden is referenced, as you know, 10 percent, doesn't say Biden. It says "Jim" and then it has 10 percent for the "Big Guy" held by H. I, a thousand percent sit here and know that the Big Guy is referencing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . That's crystal clear to me because I lived it.\par \par \uc2 I met with the former Vice President in person multiple times and I had been meeting and talking with \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and Jim Biden and Rob Walker and James Gilliar.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, to note the obvious, that is not some cable news mouth breather who is giving you his stupid partisan opinion about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop. That's \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's former business partner, who can prove he was \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's former business partner.\par \par \uc2 No one disputes he was \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's former business partner. His name, his e-mails or texts are all over the laptop, and yet somehow the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , the agency that sent a dozen agents to investigate a rope in a NASCAR garage, the agency that used hundreds of agents to hunt down grandmothers from the election justice protest on January 6th, that same agency couldn't spare a single agent to make a telephone call to Tony Bobulinski to ask questions about the laptop.\par \par \uc2 You claim it's propaganda, it's misinformation. Why don't you call the guy who's on it and ask him? They didn't bother.\par \par \uc2 This is what the \uc2 FBI\uc2  has become: An agency that seeks to exert control over the information that you read in the media. What is this? Well, it's terrifying and again, this isn't speculation. We just had it confirmed in public yesterday.\par \par \uc2 These are people whose main goal is to ensure that they never lose power in Washington, interfering with our elections and not simply by hiding information, resorting to force because they know they can get away with it.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's chief political opponent, right now -- Biden says he is going to run again. Trump has indicated he's running again -- will be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and so they're targeting them. Is anyone noticing this?\par \par \uc2 John Paul Mac Isaac, the computer repair shop owner who first obtained the laptop, says an \uc2 FBI\uc2  agent threatened him so he wouldn't go public with the laptop. In case you've forgotten, watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOHN PAUL MAC ISAAC, FORMER COMPUTER REPAIR SHOP OWNER: The \uc2 FBI\uc2  met with me at my home and asked me about my concerns. I voiced my concerns and they -- I then shifted and said, "Hey, can -- I just want this out of my shop. At this point, just get it out of my shop and give me a phone number I can call should somebody come looking for it or wants to harass me about it," and they're like, "Yes, we can't do that."\par \par \uc2 When they showed up, instead of bringing in a tech guy with them, they brought a subpoena and they're like, "Yes, we're just going to take everything."\par \par \uc2 I was a bit uncomfortable, a little nervous, but then excited at the same time, so I kind of cracked a joke. I said, "Don't worry, lads. When I write the book, I'll leave your names out of this," and that's when Agent Mike turned around and said, "Oh, it's in our experience that nothing ever happens to people that talk about these things."\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes, So, in a free country, no one who obeys the law is afraid of law enforcement. That's true. No one should ever be afraid of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  except people who know full well they've committed Federal crimes. Period.\par \par \uc2 But in this country, let's be honest, everybody's afraid of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  because you know exactly what happens to you if you tweak the nose of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  or if you annoy \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . You get raided. You get hauled into the street in leg irons. You get banned on social media.\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said from the White House podium last year, "We're flagging problematic posts for \uc2 Facebook\uc2 ." Oh so, it is the White House, same administration which oversees the \uc2 FBI\uc2  telling social media companies who's allowed to speak? It happened to Alex Berenson. It happened to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Now, we know what happened to "The New York Post" and the people running the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , people who did that, are still there.\par \par \uc2 This is a huge problem. This cannot be ignored any longer.\par \par \uc2 John Ratcliffe is the former director of national intelligence. He knows an awful lot about this. Mr. Ratcliffe, thanks so much for joining us tonight.\par \par \uc2 JOHN RATCLIFFE, FORMER DIRECTOR OF NATIONAL INTELLIGENCE: Hey, man. Good to see you, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: You may know enough that this wasn't shocking to you. But I think to a lot of people, this was legitimately shocking. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  shows up at our biggest news outlet, that's what literally \uc2 Facebook\uc2  is, it's a news outlet, three weeks before the election and says in effect, don't print this story, because it might hurt \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RATCLIFFE: Well, Tucker, I was actually surprised to hear \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  say that because what he related the \uc2 FBI\uc2  told him was exactly the opposite of what my conversations with the \uc2 FBI\uc2  Director himself at the time were about.\par \par \uc2 Look, we knew when Adam Schiff was in October of 2020, talking about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop as Russian disinformation, and using his platform as the Chairman of the Intelligence Committee to mislead voters about that. We knew that that that simply wasn't true, that it wasn't Russian disinformation, that there was no Intelligence, and discussions between my office the Director of National Intelligence, the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , and the Attorney General at the Department of Justice, all -- we all agreed, look, we need to counter this.\par \par \uc2 And I put out a statement and was backed up by both the Department of Justice and \uc2 FBI\uc2  that this was not Russian disinformation. So to hear that, contrary to what the \uc2 FBI\uc2  Director was saying, and the official position of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  that agents were acting in contradiction to that in dealings with \uc2 Facebook\uc2  or telling, if whistleblowers are to be believed, telling \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents to suppress information about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop and to amplify damaging information about then President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , you know, that is entirely inconsistent with what we all knew, which was and what you what you now know, and the public knows is that this wasn't Russian disinformation, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop was real.\par \par \uc2 And, you know, unfortunately, a lot of folks misled the American people about that and the American voter about that two weeks before a presidential election.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: That's election interference, is it not? I don't know what else it would be.\par \par \uc2 RATCLIFFE: Yes, it is election interference. You know, to the extent that these allegations are true that \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents were knowingly putting bad information out there, absolutely. And the troubling part about this, Tucker, is the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is the primary domestic authority for enforcing election security, for making sure that people don't interfere with the American voters and American elections, and if they're engaged