e from the left.\par \par \uc2 Amala, here's what a spokesperson from the hospital told FOX Digital, quote, "We do not provide gender affirming surgery for anyone under the age of 18. We do not provide hormone therapy to children before puberty begins. Care is individualized for each patient." But when pressed why the hospital's website previously said it offers gender-affirming hysterectomies for those between the ages of zero and 21, the spokesperson said, well, that was a flaw in the design of our website. So they scrubbed their website and now they're saying it never happened.\par \par \uc2 AMALA EKPUNOBI, PRAGERU PERSONALITY: It's really ridiculous to hear this when we've just listened to the phone call where they say and express exactly what they're willing to do to a minor under the age of 18. So I find it hard to believe that this statement states that they are not performing these hysterectomies and not performing these forms of treatment.\par \par \uc2 And like Chris says, we have data on this. This is irreversible damage that you would be committing against a minor. And the United States should be following states like -- countries like France, like Sweden, like Finland, who are looking at these forms of treatment and saying absolutely not. These are not treatment options for minors. They are harmful for them, and, in fact, we should seek out other therapeutic and other treatment options for these children.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Right. I want to move to another topic. It's actually very related. Fairfax, Virginia, where teachers are being trained to transition children's genders without parental approval according to "The Washington Examiner." A district assigned training program asks, quote, "Parent permission is required for which of the following -- a student requests that the teacher call him by his chosen name in classes, a student requests to use the locker room that corresponds with her identified gender, a student requests the use of a private bathroom, or none of the above," which as you can see is the correct answer. Chris, you know, what do you make of this, if they can do this without telling a parent?\par \par \uc2 RUFO: Virtually every major school district in the country has adopted this policy. They've done so without notifying parents, really under the radar. They can facilitate your child's sexual transition, provide your child with a new name, a new set of pronouns, all without telling you. This is a horrific encroachment on the basic rights of parents to be leading the development of their own children. And it's already leading to disastrous outcomes, including one father in Florida who said that the district secretly performed this -- facilitated this sexual transmission against his daughter, which contributed to her attempted suicide. The lawsuits are coming, parents are coming. This is a disaster waiting to happen.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Yes, they're asking kids to basically live, encouraging them to live a double life and really separate them from their parents and their family values.\par \par \uc2 Let's go to you, Amala. You were a leftwing activist at one time. What is behind this? Why are they doing this.\par \par \uc2 EKPUNOBI: I like to think that people are driven by compassion when they fall for these sorts of ideologies. I think most people truly think that they are upholding their child's beliefs and thoughts and who their child believes themselves to be, and that they are ushering in a new phase of equity and equality.\par \par \uc2 But however, it takes just a moment of looking into the research and the studies done on this form of treatment with children to find out that it's not the right thing for them, that it in fact is damaging them, and that by just blindly affirming these children, we are ignoring other psychiatric comorbidities that they could be dealing with, things like anxiety and depression that lead to the attempted suicide that Wendell Perez, who Chris referenced, had to go through with his daughter.\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Yes, well, I appreciate you both joining us today. I'm a little more cynical than you, Amala. I think there's a lot more behind this than just misguided compassion. But we'll talk about that a little further maybe in another show. OK, thank you both.\par \par \uc2 You may have noticed at the beginning of the show I introduced myself as Rachel Campos instead of Rachel Campos-Duffy. Up next, I have an announcement. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CAMPOS-DUFFY: Earlier introduced myself as Rachel Campos instead of Rachel Campos-Duffy. Don't worry. Everything is fine. Sean and I are still together. We have our podcast from "The Kitchen Table." It was just a bit of nerves. I didn't divorce Sean live on the air, so sorry Sean and the Kids.\par \par \uc2 That's it for us tonight. I'm Rachel Campos-Duffy in for Laura Ingraham. Tune in tomorrow and Sunday morning for my regular gig on FOX & FRIENDS WEEKEND from 6:00 a.m. to 10:00 a.m. eastern. Thanks for watching this special edition of THE INGRAHAM ANGLE.\par \par \uc2 "GUTFELD!" is next.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020220827ei8q00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Trump Raid Affidavit Heavily Redacted; Redacted Mar-a-Lago Raid Affidavit Released; Biden: Entire Trump Philosophy Like 'Semi-Fascism; GA Senate Race Tight With 10 Weeks Until Midterms; Markets Tank On Fears Of Rate Hike; Remembering U.S. Troops Killed In Kabul