et Journal" reporting that the Biden administration is now planning to give a dedicated name to the military mission in Ukraine. The report indicates that a general would also be appointed to lead the training and assistance effort there in addition to the service members who've been deployed to \uc2 NATO\uc2  nations in Eastern Europe. The White House has given Ukraine $13 billion, the biggest chunk of which has just been allocated this week in military assistance to that country. It's the largest since Putin invaded the country six months ago as one war rolls into another effort now underway in Ukraine. I want to thank Cheryl Rex for being with us today very much.\par \par \uc2 So how the \uc2 FBI\uc2  helped shape the way that \uc2 Facebook\uc2  handled the Hunter Biden laptop story during the 2020 election. So \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2  really spilled some information here to Joe Rogan and Joe Concha weighs in on it next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Always something interesting in these Joe Rogan interviews. Now the \uc2 Facebook\uc2  founder, \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2 , just started talking away and admitted, you know what, yes, the social media giant did limit the exposure of the Hunter Biden laptop story right before the 2020 presidential election. Following a warning from the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , he says about possible Russian propaganda that could be coming and to be worried about it and concern. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MARK ZUCKERBERG\uc2 , META FOUNDER AND CEO: So fewer people saw it than would have otherwise. So it definitely --\par \par \uc2 JOE ROGAN, AMERICAN COMMENTATOR: By what percentage?\par \par \uc2 ZUCKERBERG: I don't know off the top of my head. But it's meaningful.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: It's meaningful, actually. So let's bring in Joe Concha, media and politics columnist for the hill and Fox News contributor. Joe, you know, this is a big deal. This was 