e time? It's always like this, Raymond. Our bills are great!\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: But it's a real turnabout to try to suggest that it's Republicans who are embracing violence, Laura, after we saw the summer of rage, monuments being toppled, cities burned, Supreme Court justices targeted, pro-life clinics and churches defiled. Who's embracing violence? Come on.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That's all justifiable against the racist, outrageous domestic terrorist class.\par \par \uc2 All right, Raymond, I hear your mirror down in New Orleans, \uc2 LaToya Cantrell\uc2  is up to some interesting things. What is it, she's in some hot water?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yes, a little hot water after carjackings have increased by 400 percent since 2019. The mayor appeared in court recently, Laura, in defense of a young carjacker, not the victims.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I was in shock she wasn't there for us. She was there for the assailant and his mother. And it felt like she was supporting the crime.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Now Mayor \uc2 LaToya Cantrell\uc2  is responding. It turns out this young offender was found guilty of robbing multiple women in carjackings, Laura. But he had been through a city internship program the mayor founded in 2019. So Mayor Cantrell used her office to defend the perpetrator.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MAYOR LATOYA CANTRELL, (D) NEW ORLEANS: I didn't pick a side. That was my way of supporting this young person that was required to participate in a program that \uc2 the city of New Orleans\uc2  had created and is funding. That's supporting a young person that has made decisions that puts him on a better pathway. That's what I did.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: No, that's really not what she did. If you've got a multiple offender, Laura, who has beat up and robbed multiple women and taken their vehicles, they should