tions. These are the issues that are animating this race. If Democrats take one more cue, address crime and abortion, and I've got to tell you on election night we are going to surprise, because I'm a Democrat, we're going to surprise a lot of people. Most importantly, we're going to make the country stronger in the process. I will let the Pennsylvania race, the commonwealth play out like it should.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Marc, response to that?\par \par \uc2 THIESSEN: Inflation is still at a 40 year high. Gas prices are still $1.50 more than when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took office. This whole Biden comeback, Biden is on a roll, he's got the wind at his -- aviator Joe thing, is an inside the beltway phenomenon. Out in the country there are still people who are having to choose between gas and food. And as long as that is happening, nobody is going to be giving \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  credit for any of that.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: I will say, to your point about polls, Hugh, that while the president's approval rating is still fairly low in all of these state polls, the Senate candidates on the Democratic side are outpolling him, and that kind of tells you something as well. I have got to run there. Panel, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 HEWITT: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 FORD: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Finally tonight, a SPECIAL REPORT salute. When a San Antonio man veered off the road and rolled his car, take a look at this, a group of strangers quickly assembled a rescue effort. They flipped the vehicle back upright, broke inside, removed the guy from the smoky situation with the car. We're told the driver is OK and recovering at a hospital. I can tell you from personal experience in Montana, that good Samaritans doing that, it means everything.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow on SPECIAL REPORT, we will take you to the Iowa State Fair -- it is that time -- to see how some Trump Republicans and anti-Trump Republicans are faring with midwestern voters.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for invi