le are going to make their voices heard.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for joining us. Tucker is up next. I am not even going to do it.\par \par \uc2 WILL CAIN, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: We have a FOX News Alert.\par \par \uc2 Good evening and welcome to TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT. I am Will Cain, in for Tucker.\par \par \uc2 We begin with this FOX News Alert: A little over one hour ago, we learned that the Biden administration raided the home of the former President, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Palm Beach, Florida.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced the raid in a statement and FOX News has confirmed that the raid occurred. "These are dark times for our nation" said the former President, "As my beautiful home Mar-a-Lago in Palm Beach, Florida is currently under siege, raided, and occupied by a large group of \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents."\par \par \uc2 Trump wrote, "Nothing like this has ever happened to a President of the United States before."\par \par \uc2 Trump said the raid, which was announced amounts to "Prosecutorial misconduct, the weaponization of the justice system, and an attack by the radical left Democrats who desperately do not want me to run for President in 2024, especially based on recent polls."\par \par \uc2 Trump said agents also broke into his safe.\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  concluded his statement noting that "\uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  was allowed to delete and acid wash 33,000 e-mails after they were subpoenaed by Congress, but the DOJ did nothing about that."\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " is reporting tonight that the search is "Focused on material that Mr. Trump had brought with him to Mar-a-Lago, his private club and residence after he left the White House. Those boxes allegedly contained many pages of classified documents according to a person familiar with their contents."\par \par \uc2 "The Times" continued: "Mr. Trump delayed returning 15 boxes of material requested by officials with the National Archives for many months only doing so when there became a threat of action being taken to retrieve them."\par \par \uc2 FOX News has confirmed that per standard protocol, \uc2 FBI\uc2  Director Wray and Attorney General Garland were aware of the raid before it occurred.\par \par \uc2 However, you characterize what happened in the United States of America today, this is a defining moment, a seminal moment, a partisan moment, one that generations will look back on and ask, "Was this a moment we broke apart or we were able to come together?" And the answer to that question will be the questions we ask tonight.\par \par \uc2 Was there an evidentiary basis? Was there a legal basis? Or was this a partisan witch hunt?\par \par \uc2 To begin that conversation, let's start with FOX's Mike Emanuel who is standing by with the latest -- Mike.\par \par \uc2 MIKE EMANUEL, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CHIEF CONGRESSIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Will, good evening.\par \par \uc2 FOX News has learned from a source close to the former President that Mr. Trump was in New York City at Trump Tower. When he learned about the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raid of his Mar-a-Lago home, "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 " is reporting the Federal authorities appear to be focused on material former President Trump brought with him from the White House to his home in Palm Beach, Florida.\par \par \uc2 That published report cites a person familiar that the raid began this morning and notes the former President delayed returning those 15 boxes of material requested by officials with the National Archives for months.\par \par \uc2 FOX News is working to confirm all of those details. FOX News has confirmed the raid of former President Trump's Mar-a-Lago home with a law enforcement source familiar with the search warrant, per standard protocol Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  and \uc2 FBI\uc2  Director \uc2 Chris Wray\uc2  were aware this, have been fully briefed and will continue to be.\par \par \uc2 The former President announced the raid a short time ago, earlier this evening, calling this "Dark times for our nation" as his home in Palm Beach, Florida is being raided and "Occupied by a large group of \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump called the raid unannounced and says it was not "necessary or appropriate" and arguing that such an assault could only take place in broken third world countries. The former President says Federal authorities broke into his safe.\par \par \uc2 This search comes after numerous televised hearings on Capitol Hill looking into the events of January 6, 2021 and more questioning of former Trump administration officials by the Justice Department regarding the events after the 2020 election in the final weeks of the former President's time in office.\par \par \uc2 It's not entirely clear why today was chosen to launch the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raid, the former President calling it political targeting at the highest level, comparing this to former Secretary of State \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , but noting nothing has happened to hold her accountable -- Will.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Mike, I'd love to follow up with one question here for you. I noted you said both \uc2 FBI\uc2  Director \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  and the Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  were aware of this raid. Do we know, and you mentioned both of these potential evidentiary or legal basis for the raid. Do we know specifically was this about those confidential material, the alleged classified material that were in boxes taken to Mar-a-Lago or was this connected to the Congressional investigation around January 6?\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: We have not been able to pinpoint that just yet. We know that there was back and forth between Trump administration officials and the National Archives over 15 boxes of material. We do know that.\par \par \uc2 What we haven't confirmed just yet is whether that is the reason for the raid that happened at Mar-a-Lago today. So we are working to button that up, but that is the latest information that we've seen in terms of that "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 " report, so we wanted to provide it to our audience, and let our viewers decide for themselves what they think of that.\par \par \uc2 So not entirely clear whether this is related to the hearings on Capitol Hill, the subsequent investigation that is taking place at the Justice Department, interviewing former Trump administration officials about his final weeks in office exactly why they're doing this at this particular time.\par \par \uc2 But there's a lot going on, obviously, on Capitol Hill, and over at the Justice Department, leading to a raid of his Mar-a-Lago home today -- Will.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: And as of tonight, no comments so far from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  or the DOJ. Mike Emanuel, thank you so much for the latest.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: You heard Mike say there that this will be up to the American people, you watching to decide, was this a legal raid? Was this a raid in pursuit of justice? Or was this a partisan act to take out not just a former President, but a potential candidate for President of the United States? And, obviously, according to the latest polls, the leader of the opposition party.\par \par \uc2 In order to know the answer to that question, the DOJ and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  will need to provide and soon the evidentiary and legal basis for this, and this is a very fair statement, unprecedented action by the Department of Justice.\par \par \uc2 Let's talk about exactly what you, the viewer, what you the American should be taking away from this with \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 . He is a former senior Trump adviser, and he joins us with his reaction.\par \par \uc2 Stephen, what a day in American history. Your reaction.\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER\uc2 , FORMER WHITE HOUSE ADVISER: This is an abomination. You have the sitting President of the United States, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , through his Justice Department, through his \uc2 FBI\uc2  conducting a raid on the person who is presumed to be his opponent in the next election, and also the 45th President of the United States.\par \par \uc2 As President Trump pointed out in his statement, it is risible that this would be purportedly done in the name of document preservation from the leaks we've seen, when Hillary Clinton used an off the book server for years to conduct classified State business and at the same time, money was being funneled by the millions into \uc2 the Clinton Foundation\uc2  with the very people she was doing business with that to this day, has never been investigated, not by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , not by the \uc2 IRS\uc2 , not by anybody.\par \par \uc2 We are truly living in a situation where the \uc2 FBI\uc2  has become a Praetorian Guard from Rome, where they take it unto themselves to decide who wields power in this country.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: You know, Stephen, I can't help but notice that for all that Trump was accused, it seems that Biden is intent on embodying. It was said that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would "lock her up." That did not happen as you just pointed out with \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 . There was no raid of \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  and her classified documents, but here now under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , there is exactly that pursuit. There is the use of law enforcement to go after his political opponent.\par \par \uc2 MILLER: Let's talk about the Security State that has been after President Trump for six years when he declared his candidacy, and then when he became the nominee. They began pushing the Russian collusion hoax. Let's not forget for years of our national life, the official position of the government, of the beltway class, of the media was that he had conspired illegally with the government of Russia until that was completely and wholly debunked.\par \par \uc2 Let us not forget the Security State leak that was used to improperly and scandalously impeach him for simply trying to get to the bottom of well- known corruption in