ctions, and I think you're exactly right to point to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 How do you explain -- how do you explain the interest in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but more importantly, the lack of interest, Gerry, in potential corruption in the White House? And I'm going to use the word "potential" because allegations are designed to be investigated by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . And in this case, what we have seen and Wray said last week, well, you know, it's concerning that we haven't given that more attention.\par \par \uc2 It's a problem that you called disinformation. Not only did you decline to investigate, you explained it away as Russian disinformation.\par \par \uc2 CALLAHAN: Right. That's a great point. Think about this. I've heard a lot of guest talk about Hillary Clinton deleting e-mails, obviously, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  pointed that out. \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  went to Pedophile Island -- how many - - a couple dozen times. You don't even expect an investigation, let alone a raid.\par \par \uc2 And with \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , this always blows my mind. We don't need an investigation. It's right there in front of you. They handed it to you, \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 . We see the videos.\par \par \uc2 We know there's probably underage hookers, but we know there is crack. We know there is influence peddling. That guy was at the White House in the Rose Garden about two weeks ago for the Medal of Freedom ceremony, he doesn't even -- he's not even worried.\par \par \uc2 You know who is worried? \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2 . \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Jr., anybody in Trump's universe, they are afraid of the 6:00 AM raid where they were in their boxer shorts and CNN is across the street. I guess \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was lucky, at least he wasn't in his underwear and with, you know, a CNN camera watching him come out of Mar-a-Lago. At least he wasn't -- it didn't reach that point, but who knows what's next?\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Well, coming up shortly, we'll be talking to members of the Trump family. But we appreciate hearing from you tonight, Gerry. Thank you so much, Gerry Callahan.\par \par \uc2 CALLAHAN: Thanks, Will. Thank you, Will.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: All right, this just in from FOX Digital's Brooke Singman. A source tells FOX News that \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents went to Mar-a-Lago and looked in every single office, his safe, the former President's safe, and grabbed documents and boxes without going through them on the property. So immediately left the property with those boxes.\par \par \uc2 The source said the agents took the documents to go through later once they left Mar-a-Lago. The source told FOX News: "They were not being judicious about what they took."\par \par \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 , as promised, a member of the Trump family and former senior adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  joins us now.\par \par \uc2 Lara, thank you for being on the program with us tonight. I will just start with this: Have you spoken to the former President? How is he doing? What is the attitude of the family?\par \par \uc2 LARA TRUMP, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: I have spoken to my father-in- law, and I've got to tell you, you know, he is as shocked as anybody. I think for someone, and anyone, quite frankly, who loves this country and believes in America, this should shake you to your core what has happened today.\par \par \uc2 This is a very clear demarcation in the history of America. Never before as many of your guests have already talked about, Will, have we seen something like this happen, where an unannounced raid by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is conducted on a former President of the United States?\par \par \uc2 Think about this, if this is what they're able to do to the former President of the United States, think about what they could do to you, to anybody in America. The bottom line here is that these documents that have been in question have been -- everybody has been cooperating, everybody from my father-in-law's team has been cooperating with the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , with any authority that asked for anything up until now and there was no need to make such a big scene to do something this insane, quite frankly, to a former President.\par \par \uc2 But I think everybody clearly knows, Will, what is going on here. This is about weaponizing the justice system as it has been so many times in the past against somebody who you politically do not like. They detest \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , not just on the Democrat side, but the general establishment, because he is not one of them, because he doesn't play their game.\par \par \uc2 They are terrified he is going to announce any day that he is running for President in 2024 and this is a very convenient way to just throw a little more mud on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as though they haven't already done enough.\par \par \uc2 This is the same agency, don't forget, the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , who you know, had falsified documents to get FISA warrants to conduct this entire sham Russia hoax that the country had to deal with for two years, millions of taxpayer dollars and our time that we'll never get back to find what? Absolutely nothing.\par \par \uc2 They've been trying to shove January 6 down everybody's throat in an effort to get people to care about that and think that's the most important thing in the world. That hasn't worked for them yet. So here they are heading into a midterm and heading into a presidential election season coming up where they know, they have no hope on the Democrat side. They have nothing positive to show that they've done for the American people.\par \par \uc2 So what do you do? You try to take out a guy who hasn't even announced that he is running yet, but they're terrified of him on the Democrat side, for sure, and I'm going to say it again, in the general establishment.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: Lara, you've spoken to your father-in-law, therefore, you have the most immediate information of anybody we've spoken with tonight. Does he know, do you know why his home was raided?\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: He believes it is the documents in question that, you know, everybody has been really upset about from the White House. Look, my father-in-law, as anybody knows who has been around him a lot loves to save things like newspaper clippings, magazine clippings, photographs, documents that he had every authority, Will, to take from the White House.\par \par \uc2 And, you know, again, he's been cooperating every single step of the way with the people that have questioned any of this and I know people have brought it up before but you know, look at \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , the 33,000 e- mails that she just deletes that are completely gone and nobody bats an eyelash about it.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  takes some documents that he had every right to take that every President does, didn't take antiques, you know, like \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  took out of the White House in paintings apparently, but that is what he believes and that's what you know, I think is at the bottom of all this and the reason that they raided Mar-a-Lago, quite frankly.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: All right, Lara, always good to talk to you. Thank you for giving us that firsthand perspective from inside the family tonight.\par \par \uc2 L. TRUMP: You've got it.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: All right, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  has experienced the weaponization of the justice system firsthand. He is the former White House chief strategist. He has been targeted relentlessly by the January 6 Committee.\par \par \uc2 He joins us now by phone to react to news of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raid on Mara a Lago.\par \par \uc2 Steve, happy to have you on the program. I have you by phone here tonight. What's your immediate reaction?\par \par \uc2 STEVE BANNON\uc2 , FORMER WHITE HOUSE CHIEF STRATEGIST (via phone): Well, Will, you know, I gave a speech, a keynote address at the CPAC on Friday night, I said, "We're at war." We're at a political and ideological war. And they've obviously weaponized the Justice Department.\par \par \uc2 And this had to be approved by \uc2 Ron Klain\uc2 . This had to go up to the White House to be approved. Absolutely. Anybody who is saying that didn't is a liar. This had to go up the chain of command, through \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , to \uc2 Ron Klain\uc2  at least and Wray and these guys.\par \par \uc2 But look, here's the thing. This is about pure power politics. They're absolutely scared to death about Trump. This can be Marc Elias, the guy who laid out the entire effort to steal the 2020 election or the transition period. He is tweeting right now, all the US Code of that document and they have this e-mail to make sure he can't run for Federal office again.\par \par \uc2 They're absolutely petrified Trump's going to announce in the next couple weeks, win the Republican nomination, win the White House.\par \par \uc2 Now, here is what's incumbent upon everyone, the House leaders right now need to step up and recommit -- Jim Jordan -- full investigation, I think cutting off appropriations to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to get to the bottom of this. Okay.\par \par \uc2 This is this is going to continue on. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  right now is the Gestapo. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  is the Gestapo, whether it's out in Colorado, putting a Gold Star mother like Tina Peters in chains, \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  in chains. It is absolutely I've seen obscene. This is an obscenity, and we're going to have to fight fire with fire.\par \par \uc2 The way to do it is win election, win them overwhelmingly and then use the appropriations process to choke down the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and shut down the Justice Department and get to the bottom of who approved this. This is so outrageous. It needs to be investigate.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: You know, Steve, I want to ask you this question, Steve. You know, I'm familiar with your point of view. I'm familiar with the opinions you share on "War Room." I'm familiar with how deep you fear the corruption has run within the 