on and the raid into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but for now, we turn to FOX's Shannon Bream for a legal analysis of the situation unfolding tonight.\par \par \uc2 Shannon, great to have you with me.\par \par \uc2 Let's take this from a legal perspective. As you look at what has happened and what has occurred, what's your takeaway?\par \par \uc2 SHANNON BREAM, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CHIEF LEGAL CORRESPONDENT: Well, I can't wait to see the warrant. I think everybody wants to know the underpinnings of this, as you've talked about on the show. And Will, you are a gifted lawyer, and know this just as well as anybody. You've talked us through what would happen.\par \par \uc2 I mean, this doesn't just happen overnight. You go through a Judge. There is an internal decision making process at the DOJ, at the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , in which people have to talk over the possibilities of what can happen here.\par \par \uc2 And you know, it's so rare because there's never been an indictment of a former President, a criminal indictment of a former President, and who knows whether we'll get to that place. But this is part of a case. This is part of what you would do is go get information and go get the things that you would claim are evidence.\par \par \uc2 It's interesting as what \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2  has been saying, I'd be interested to see if the DOJ and \uc2 FBI\uc2  also believe, as she said, he's been cooperating, he's been working with them. They may likely have suggested otherwise. They may believe otherwise.\par \par \uc2 Because to go to a Judge and get the underpinnings that you need for this warrant to have someone sign off on, they probably had to make some kind of allegation. I would guess that the President has not been cooperating with them, at least not in their definition of cooperation.\par \par \uc2 But it calls to mind a lot of these other raids that you've talked about, the arrest of Steve Navarro and some of the others and how -- or excuse me, \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  -- how 