s, Will.\par \par \uc2 I worked in classified information. I worked in national security cases, and I worked in front of the FISA Court. So what I would have said to you 10 years ago is that a Federal Judge had to sign off on this, and that means a Federal Judge had to be shown an affidavit that said there was probable cause to believe a crime was committed, and that evidence of that crime would be found at Mar-a-Lago, and I would have trusted that.\par \par \uc2 But after the Russia collusion hoax, the FISA warrant that was misused and gotten illegally against \uc2 Carter Page\uc2 , and the way the \uc2 FBI\uc2  treated the Hillary Clinton investigation, where they never sent a single subpoena, or served a single search warrant on \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  or her aides, her laptop or her secret server, it is very hard for me now to say that this does hold water, I hope so honestly, for the Justice Department that I served for 10 years, and the cause of justice that I've served my entire career as a prosecutor. I actually hope there is probable cause, but from what we're hearing, I don't have any faith that that's true.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: There is so little faith left. I believe among the American people for their institutions and I think you're exactly right. The burden of proof now for the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the DOJ to retain what little faith the American people have in that institution, those institutions. That is what is at stake.\par \par \uc2 Francey Hakes, thank you for being with us tonight.\par \par \uc2 HAKES: Thanks, Will.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: All right, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said tonight his Mar-a-Lago home has been under siege by \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents. Ned Ryun is CEO of American Majority and he joins us with his reaction.\par \par \uc2 Hey, Ned, I'd love for you to pick up on where Francey left off. You know, it's impossible to separate this from the last five years of allegations and investigations, from Russia collusion to the supposed, you know, Russian soldiers and bounties on American soldiers overseas to the lack of interest in \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , we have to -- we are being asked to trust an apparatus which has burned every ounce of trust.\par \par \uc2 NED RYUN, FOUNDER AND CEO, AMERICAN MAJORITY: Well, well, we need to disabuse ourselves of the notion that the DOJ and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  are actually interested in the rule of law. I mean, I would remind people, these very same institutions secured four FISA warrants off a Steele dossier they knew was bogus to target a sitting President of the United States.\par \par \uc2 I don't think they really care about much of anything, except for targeting political enemies. And again, as people have said, they are weaponizing against a political enemy who they view as an existential threat to the administrative state, and instead of viewing the DOJ and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  as rule of law, I think we need to view them as the Praetorian Guard of the administrative state and I don't think it's going to stop here, Will.\par \par \uc2 I'm afraid that they might try to indict Trump with a rigged grand jury before the midterms, I think it is a real possibility.\par \par \uc2 CAIN: We will be watching, Ned. I appreciate you jumping on here at the end of the show.\par \par \uc2 I appreciate you watching me tonight filling in for \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This story is not going away. Obviously, you'll have excellent coverage starting right now with \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 . He is up next.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document TCARL00020220809ei8800001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 George Soros\uc2  Has Been Creating Chaos For Decades; Governor DeSantis Fighting Back In Florida; Final Exam; China's Alliance With Russia Will Hurt America; Interview With Rep. \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  (R-FL)\b0\par\par\uc2 Tucker Carlson, Emily Compagno, Will Cain \par \uc2 7,637 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 August 2022\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: Tucker Carlson Tonight\par \uc2 TCARL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Chris: "Last night, Gutfeld accused you of having hair plugs. Is that true?" No, but the way things are going, I might actually have to look into getting some.\par \par \uc2 Tucker is up next and always remember, I'm Watters and this is my world.\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Good evening and welcome to TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT.\par \par \uc2 When a Hungarian financier called \uc2 George Soros\uc2  shorted the English pound 30 years ago, back in 1992, the \uc2 British government\uc2  fought back. It did everything it could to preserve the value of its national currency.\par \par \uc2 British officials raised interest rates all the way to 15 percent. \uc2 The Bank of England\uc2  then sold $40 billion of foreign currency reserves in a desperate effort to prop up the pound.\par \par \uc2 In the end, of course, it didn't work. \uc2 The Bank of England\uc2  collapsed. Total cost to the population of Great Britain? Well, that's hard to measure, but it was 