na Tech War," and a frequent guest of ours.\par \par \uc2 Gordon, thanks so much for coming on. So, we can let the military situation develop as it will, and we can read about it in the news. But underneath all of that is a huge story about the US Dollar as the global reserve currency. Tell us what you believe China would like to do about that?\par \par \uc2 GORDON CHANG, SENIOR FELLOW, GATESTONE INSTITUTE: Well, certainly China would like to replace the dollar as the global reserve currency with the renminbi. Now China is wanting to do this for decades, Tucker, and so have the Russians, but now, they're actually attacking the dollar because they think they can get away with it.\par \par \uc2 And so therefore, this is a moment of vulnerability, because certainly, if we don't have the global reserve currency, the power of the United States will be substantially diminished, as you point out.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So this is a core American interest. This is not like promoting trans-rights in Botswana, which they're also doing. This is the key to our standard of living in our economy. So why wouldn't Pelosi and the various geniuses around her keep that in mind before she left for Taipei?\par \par \uc2 CHANG: Well, probably, she doesn't think that it's within her ambit. But this is certainly within the ambit of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and with Biden's crazy spending plans, that is eventually going to end up in a much cheaper dollar. And people around the world are not going to want to keep their wealth in dollars, if they think that it's going to get less valuable.\par \par \uc2 So the President of the United States, I think, really needs to understand the ultimate long-term effects of his spending.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: You put it so simply and clearly, I appreciate that. Do you think -- so you clearly understand it and most people who spend five minutes on it can understand it. Do you think there are economists at the White House who are worried about this and are taking steps to prevent it?\par \par \uc2 CHANG: No, I don't think that they really care about this. Yes, there probably are communists in the White House or those, at least we know that they are sympathizers of the regime in Beijing, and, you know, I don't know what's in their minds.\par \par \uc2 But you know, if they wanted to undermine the core interests of the United States, which is the primacy of the dollar, they're doing a very good job of it, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So shocking and scary. Gordon Chang, thank you for that update tonight.\par \par \uc2 CHANG: Thank you, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: What's happened to our economy is the product of a theory called Modern Monetary Theory, where the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  just prints all the money it wants, that inevitably results in inflation. Of course, no one denies that. But then to fix inflation, you take money out of the system through taxation. That is the plan according to Modern Monetary Theory.\par \par \uc2 It is not a conspiracy theory. You can look it up.\par \par \uc2 So it's probably not a coincidence that the \uc2 IRS\uc2  has now gotten a lot more funding and a lot more guns. The \uc2 IRS\uc2  has its own army. They've already stockpiled five million rounds of ammunition and thousands of firearms. Why are they doing that exactly?\par \par \uc2 Why is no one noticing this? Well, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  of Florida is trying to stop it. Bless him. He joins us next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So when they start treating the \uc2 IRS\uc2  as a military agency, you should be very worried and that's exactly what the \uc2 US government\uc2  is doing.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, the \uc2 Government Accountability Office\uc2  reported that more than 2,000 IRS enforcement agents have more than 4,000 weapons, guns that kill people, remember?\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IRS\uc2  is also stockpiling more than five million rounds of ammunition. In 2020. The watchdog organization, openthebooks.com report the \uc2 IRS\uc2  has spent more than $20 million on guns and ammo between 2006 and 2019.\par \par \uc2 A few lawmakers are trying to stop this. Florida Congressman, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  is one of them. He just introduced the Disarm the IRS Act. It is sponsored by Marjorie Taylor, Paul Gosar, and Jeff Duncan. \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Congressman, thanks so much for coming on and for doing this. Why would the \uc2 IRS\uc2  need millions of dollars' worth of guns and ammo?\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 MATT GAETZ\uc2  (R-FL): Well, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is raising taxes, disarming Americans, so of course they are arming up the \uc2 IRS\uc2  like they're preparing to take Volusia.\par \par \uc2 Like you mentioned, five million rounds of ammunition, 4,500 firearms, automatic weapons, and $731,000.00 of taxpayer money spent this year to quite literally weaponize your government against you.\par \par \uc2 So, it's not really that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Democrats hate guns. They just hate law-abiding Americans having them and they take the money from the people to go and have their own little private arsenals and it is particularly egregious, from a country that militarizes its bureaucracies and then forces its grandmothers to go and fend for themselves on dangerous streets because they defund the police and have cashless bail and other hug-a-thug woke criminal justice policies. That's why I'm introducing legislation to stop it.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, God bless you. I mean, \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  has bodyguards with extended magazines. They're not against guns. They are against you having guns.\par \par \uc2 So how could anybody -- rhetorical question here -- in the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  oppose your bill? On what grounds?\par \par \uc2 GAETZ: Well, I'm hoping -- I'm hoping we get a vote on it because it will show the hypocrisy that is around gun ownership in America. And you just look at the last assault weapons ban that they passed off the floor of the Congress. They had special exemptions for the Department of Education and the Department of Agriculture and the \uc2 IRS\uc2  to have guns, so I don't know if the future is like critical race theory and tax payments at the end of a rifle, but I certainly hope not.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: It sounds like it maybe. I don't know what else to infer from this.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for fighting against it. I very much appreciate that.\par \par \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  of Florida.\par \par \uc2 GAETZ: Thank you, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, we are out of time, but we will be back every night, 8:00 PM. The show that is the sworn enemy of lying, pomposity, smugness and groupthink.\par \par \uc2 Taking a break for a week, but I'll be back in a week, nine days, something like that.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, have a wonderful time. Hope you get some time off with the ones that you love, and as a gesture of great affection we are throwing it to \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  about 40 seconds early.\par \par \uc2 Have a wonderful night.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document TCARL00020220805ei8400001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Sellout Manchin Is Angry He Is Tethered To Biden; AZ Governor GOP Primary Still Too Close To Call; Dems Head For Exit As Biden's Presidency Derails; Somehow Kamala Is More Worrisome Than Biden; Tattoos & Hoodies Can't Mask Fetterman's Elitism; NYT Friedman's Love Affair With China Exposed; Cotton Moves To Ban China From Buying U.S. Land; China Shouldn'