is - How do you expect people to have faith and confidence and trust in the integrity of the system when they can't count the ballots and every other country can? Why don't we make voting day voting day, unless you need an absentee ballot you're incapacitated.\par \par \uc2 That's it. Count the votes at night. We're done.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Somehow our parents managed to vote on Election Day, right. Except just military, but it's ridiculous. But I just had to vent on that. You had a great show and we'll try to--\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Just keep venting. I like the venting Laura Ingraham. Give it to them.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We'll vent together. All right, Sean. Thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 I'm Laura Ingraham. This is THE INGRAHAM ANGLE from just outside Minneapolis tonight. And we begin with what I just referenced, some breaking news. The GOP gubernatorial contest in Arizona between Kari Lake and Karrin Taylor Robson is still too close to call.\par \par \uc2 And any moment now, we're expecting a count of nearly 120,000 votes from Maricopa County. And that could change the outlook of the race. But we'll wait and see. We're going to bring you the latest updates as we get them.\par \par \uc2 Now, also tonight, we're going to bring you more of my exclusive investigation into what's happened here in Minneapolis in the two-plus years now since the George Floyd riots burnt much of the city to the ground. But first, runaway Democrats. That's the focus of tonight's 'Angle'.\par \par \uc2 Congratulations, dems, because in President Biden's 19th months in office, he's the equivalent of a lame duck.\par \par \uc2 Now, here's the definition, according to Oxford languages. This is an official, especially the president and the final period of office after the election of a successor or an ineffectual or unsuccessful person or thing.\par \par \uc2 OK. The primary definition might not apply. But the secondary one certainly does. Talk about ineffectual. That's \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and everyone knows it.\par \par \uc2 Now, you remember that movie, Runaway Train, right? Well, meet the runaway Democrats.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHAD HARTMAN, "THE CHAD HARTMAN SHOW" HOST: Do you want \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to run in 2024?\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 DEAN PHILLIPS\uc2  (D-MN): No, I don't. I think the country would be well served by a new generation of compelling, well-prepared, dynamic Democrats to step up.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Congressman Phillips is not alone. Here in Minnesota, you can feel the anxiety building among Democrats. Not just in the Twin Cities, but in the burbs as well.\par \par \uc2 Now another Democrat in Minnesota, \uc2 Angie Craig\uc2 , also doesn't want Biden running again. Saying, "We need new leaders in Washington".\par \par \uc2 And then in an exchange that has tongues a wagon, two New York, liberals in a hot primary also signaled the end is near for Biden.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Should President Biden run again in 2024? Mr. Nadler?\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 JERROLD NADLER\uc2  (D-NY): Too early to say. He doesn't serve the purpose of Democratic Party to deal with that until after the midterms.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Ms. Maloney.\par \par \uc2 REP. CAROLYN MALONEY (D-NY): I don't believe he's running for reelection.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Of course, the true believers then pretended to be in shock.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE SCARBOROUGH, MSNBC HOST: I just got to say, wow.\par \par \uc2 MIKA BRZEZINSKI\uc2 , MSNBC HOST: I'm really thrown off by this act.\par \par \uc2 SCARBOROUGH: That's insane, because - that's news to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BRZEZINSKI: Yes. The guy is sitting there watching these two. I would be very, very disappointed actually. I really would. I'm - that's really - it's stunning actually.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. That's just bad acting. They're not disappointed.\par \par \uc2 Now, Maloney got clobbered all day long by party leadership. So she tried to walk it back today tweeting, "I will absolutely support President Biden, if he decides to run for re-election. Biden's leadership securing historic investments for health care, climate and economic justice prove once again why he is the strong and effective leader we need right now."\par \par \uc2 Come on. But we all know the damage is already done, right? And then the climate change sell out from coal country. He added fuel to the Biden funeral pyre as well.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ANDREA MITCHELL, MSNBC HOST: Would you support \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  if he's on the ticket in 2024?\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOE MANCHIN\uc2  (D-WV): I'm not talking about the 2022 election and 2024. I have no control over those elections.\par \par \uc2 MITCHELL: You're a Democratic senator. I'm just asking if you would support your own, the leader of your own party.\par \par \uc2 MANCHIN: I'm talking about - I'm supporting this bill, Andrea.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. What he's not supporting there is a guy who has spent more time COVID positive than positive about the names of members of his own cabinet.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT, UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: I want to thank the former general, I keep calling him general, my - the guy who runs that outfit over there.\par \par \uc2 And the reason I asked Mitch to do this is because he knows how to get things done.\par \par \uc2 Now, you - I'm going to hand it over to Secretary - Mr. Secretary, I'm going to have you speak now.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Of course, the Democrats have no one to blame here but themselves. This is a mess they've created. By running a hologram septuagenarian with rapidly declining cognitive skills, then pairing him up with Willie Brown's dimwitted former flame, they box themselves in.\par \par \uc2 Now, the only thing scarier than Biden with a finger near the nuclear button is Kamala 100 yards from it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: We can move clean energy from where it is created to where it is needed. It is literally about the transportation of energy. How exciting is that?\par \par \uc2 So the devastation is real. The harm is real. The impact is real. And we are witnessing it in real time.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Democrats are anti-American radicals, but they're not total morons. They're seeing the same polls that we're seeing, the same Kamala, the same Joe we're seeing.\par \par \uc2 Check out this poll from CNN. They found that a shocking 75 percent of Democrat voters want someone other than Biden in 2024. And the latest Gallup survey has Biden's approval lower than any president at this point in his first term ever. It's a personal low of 38 percent.\par \par \uc2 Now, and despite the endless tedious January 6 hearings, and the relentless media hits, Trump is still beating Biden and Harris in a hypothetical 2024 matchup.\par \par \uc2 Now, remember, we told you this a few weeks ago. Liberals are never going to admit, never, that liberalism has failed. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has consistently pursued these left-wing policies and we know those policies have led to one disaster after another. Yet we're waiting for that honest, that self assessment, but it never comes.\par \par \uc2 They can never admit that the lockdowns lasted too long, or that the government has been too soft on crime, or that Democrats blew it on inflation. Because that would be admitting a problem with liberalism. And they're never going to do that. So the problem, they think, it has to be Biden. He's too old. He's too weak. He doesn't fight hard enough, blah, blah, blah.\par \par \uc2 So now they're thinking, maybe