re not working really but we still need a new messenger. Is this all going according to plan in other words?\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: No. Look, I mean, part of the reason I wrote 'Defeating Big Government Socialism' is their underlying belief system. For example, if you're really a hard left, if you're Buttigieg, for example, you've never done anything seriously, you bicycle around. He's happy to have the American people in pain overpaying for gasoline, because he thinks that'll drive them into electric vehicles, which they also currently can't afford.\par \par \uc2 If you look at the murder rate. I mean, the people that \uc2 George Soros\uc2  has been electing are happy to release murderers back on the street. And I just saw a New York state senator, Democratic senator who said that the men who had been put in women's prison because they were transgender, and who had now been caught raping women, shouldn't be prosecuted, because they're women too.\par \par \uc2 Now, I mean, if that's your belief system and that's the world you live in, open borders are fine. You just have a couple of million people coming in. Although even for the mayors of Washington, DC and New York, there are beginning to be so many illegal immigrants that are beginning to complain that it's literally unmanageable.\par \par \uc2 But I think if you're truly hard left, all of this is acceptable because it's for this greater mythical belief system that's almost a religion. It's a secular religion.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Newt, we just got a Fox News alert. We have the new numbers in from that razor thin GOP gubernatorial contest in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 Maricopa County just announced moments ago that Karrin Taylor Robson is now leading Kari Lake, 45.87 percent to 45.22 percent. That's a difference of 2,650 votes. Now, the county says, it's going to release updated numbers tomorrow around 10pm.\par \par \uc2 That is great for us, because our shows starts at 10 pm Eastern. But, Newt, I talked about this with Hannity. This is obscene that in the greatest country in the world we can't count our votes on Election Day and report on election night. What the heck is going on? And why is this still not fixed?\par \par \uc2 GINGRICH: Well, it's crazy. I just watched a French national election. And the French national election was with paper ballots, and they were reported that night. There's something profoundly wrong with the way we approach all this.\par \par \uc2 And I think it'll be interesting tomorrow to watch, because there are other counties that Lake was carrying by pretty good margins. And I don't think they finished reporting either. So who knows what the final number is going to be sometime tomorrow. And you're right. It is crazy that they can't just get this done.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Newt, thank you. Great to see you.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOHN FETTERMAN\uc2  (D) PENNSYLVANIA U.S. SENATE CANDIDATE: People have been trying to label me my entire life. I do not look like a typical politician. I don't even look like a typical person.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  knows Pennsylvania through and through, from York, played football in Reading, raising his family in Braddock, a steel town.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, he's a total phony. We've told you this all along that \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  is a fake populist. Now, he's playing the part through his goofy, oversized gym shorts, the goatie. But even we didn't know how bad this narrative really was.\par \par \uc2 Now, it turns out that this giant man baby was getting an allowance from his parents in excess of 50k a year. And it lasted not just for a few years, but well into his 40s. OK. It gets better. His sister took care of him too.\par \par \uc2 According to 'The Philadelphia Inquirer', he bought a swanky industrial- style loft from her for just $1. That's a good buy.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Dr. Mehmet Oz, Republican candidate for the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  in Pennsylvania. Dr. Oz, who is this guy, \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 ? Because this story keeps getting more fanciful by the day.\par \par \uc2 MEHMET OZ, PA GOP SENATE CANDIDATE: Well, Fetterman is a fraud. I'm actually in Pittsburgh now, which is close to where he's currently living, although he's not from here originally. And they know it. And they tell me all the time how much they disliked him.\par \par \uc2 He was supported by his parents until he was elected as lieutenant governor four years ago. He lived on handouts without paying his taxes correctly, by the way. And yet, he's raising taxes right now, advocating for that on the working class, after pushing for reckless spending programs and creating all this inflation. And he's a rubber stamp for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And here's the thing, he's the most radical Democratic candidate in a contested election this cycle. I'll say it again, the most radical in a contested election, yet no one knows it. And by the way, if you were to go to Doctoroz.com, and help me get the word out, it will be helpful. Because he stored up so much money that he's been telling that tale that you just showed.\par \par \uc2 I, on the other hand, I'm the son of an immigrant. I believe in the American dream because I lived it myself. I respect the needs of workers hurt by regulations and overreaching government. And the reality is \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  believes in big government and bloated bureaucracies. That's his life experience, because he's never had to actually work to make his own money because it was given to him.\par \par \uc2 I believe in the people of Pennsylvania. If you believe in the people and individualism and what you do if you work for yourself, which is what the American Dream was about. That's the deal. You work hard, you succeed, you do the right thing. You achieve things that unimaginable anywhere else on the planet.\par \par \uc2 If you believe that, c