n? No more sniffing little girls.\par \par \uc2 If you're \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and your main source of pleasure at this late stage in your life is sniffing the hair of unsuspecting, defenseless little girls and now you can't even smell it, imagine that. Let's say you're riding your bike and you see a little girl and you think, "I'd love to sniff her hair. Oh, man. No sense of smell."\par \par \uc2 So, actually the costs of COVID are a little more profound than sometimes we understand. It is kind of weird from a political perspective is that Biden got infected with COVID at exactly the moment his approval rating has reached its lowest ebb, not just with normal people, with Democrats. He's 19 percent among Hispanic voters. Red alert, anyone?\par \par \uc2 And this also comes exactly the same moment that his son faces possible felony charges, huh? And also, needless to say, at the moment that his dementia has become so obvious that no one can possibly deny it. "I'm in Israel to honor the Holocaust," he just said. Oh, it's so awful.\par \par \uc2 So, what does this mean? Well, this incites the blood instincts of others in his party. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , probably sitting in her rec room right now polishing her resume. "I could replace him."\par \par \uc2 But the real story here is the medical story. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and a whole lot other people have gotten pretty sick with COVID after getting multiple shots. What is that about exactly? How did that happen?\par \par \uc2 It's easy to just mock that this is a pandemic of the unvaccinated. That's clearly untrue, but is there a connection between getting most multiple COVID vax shots and getting sicker?\par \par \uc2 Is it possible that the vaccine actually can hurt you, especially if you keep getting boosted? Can it weaken your immune system?\par \par \uc2 Well, that looks possible. Multiple studies have looked into this.\par \par \uc2 Just last month, "The Journal of Food and Chemical Toxicology" published the findings of several mRNA researchers and we're quoting, "In this paper, we present evidence that vaccination induces a profound impairment in type one interferon signaling, which has diverse adverse consequences to human health."\par \par \uc2 Well, that seems like a headline. Did you read that in "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 ?" No, you probably didn't. Kind of weird since hundreds of millions of people got the shot.\par \par \uc2 The researchers continue that in their studies of the COVID vaccine, "We identify potential profound disturbances in regulatory control of protein synthesis and cancer surveillance. These disturbances potentially have a causal link to neurodegenerative disease, myocarditis, Bell's Palsy, liver disease, impaired adaptive immunity, impaired DNA damage response, et cetera."\par \par \uc2 So, it's possible. In fact, it's looking likely that the vaccine might suppress the immune system. This fact, the authors concluded, will "Have a wide range of consequences, not the least of which include the reactivation of latent viral infections and the reduced ability to effectively combat future infections."\par \par \uc2 Now again, we sincerely hope that's not true, but it's not just the conclusion of one scientific journal.\par \par \uc2 "The Lancet" may be the most famous scientific journal in the world, released similar findings in February. "The Lancet's" piece was entitled "Risk of infection, hospitalization and death up to nine months after a second dose of COVID-19 vaccine."\par \par \uc2 A physician called Kenji Yamamoto made this observation about the data from "The Lancet." He wrote this in a letter to "The Journal of Virology" and we're quoting: "The study showed that immune function among vaccinated individuals eight months after the administration of two doses of COVID-19 vaccine was lower than that among the unvaccinated individuals."\par \par \uc2 Now your first response, if you're a humane person to a line like that, has got to be deep sympathy because people were misled. They were forced. They were forced, medical ethics thrown out the window. People were forced to take medicine they didn't want and some of them have been hurt by it and you don't have to take this man's word for it.\par \par \uc2 Pull up "The Lancet" study yourself. You won't find anything of the text of the article saying what Kenji Yamamoto said, which is weird. Why would "The Lancet" want to hide a major finding like that? We can't say, but if you look at table three in the piece, here's what you'll find buried in the data.\par \par \uc2 Among people around the age of 80 who have been double vaccinated, that would include people like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the per capita rate of medical incidences, including hospitalizations for death, is nearly twice as high as the rate of serious incidence for the unvaccinated. This is 180 days after vaccination.\par \par \uc2 What is that? And why is no one interested?\par \par \uc2 The piece also includes a chart showing negative vaccine efficacy for all ages after eight months for all participants in the study. So again, this is sad news for a lot of Americans, but it's also a profound indictment, maybe the greatest indictment in our lifetimes of our leaders, their recklessness, their pig headedness, their dishonesty.\par \par \uc2 Given this, how is the DC government, among many others, still requiring schoolchildren -- public and private schoolchildren -- to get a COVID vaccine? That's a question that no one asked at today's White House press briefing.\par \par \uc2 How are members of the US military being dismissed without their pensions because they won't take this same vaccine, in light of these study results? Is no one paying attention? How is this allowed?\par \par \uc2 But instead, today at the White House briefing, all the questions are about the proof of life video that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's office released today. Here it is.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Hey, folks, guess you heard this morning I tested positive for COVID. But, I've been double-vaccinated and double-boosted. Symptoms are mild and I really appreciate your inquiries and concerns.\par \par \uc2 But I'm doing well, getting a lot of work done. I'm going to continue to get it done.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Here's a question. Is there a single public statement \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has made since Inauguration Day that he did not read off a teleprompter? Is there one? Find it.\par \par \uc2 So, the question they come up at today's press briefing was, after seeing that is who shot that footage? Is that person in danger?\par \par \uc2 Well, once again, the President's glass ceiling shattering publicist, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , was asked that question and she said it's totally fine because the video was taken outside and there is no risk outside that we will arrest you for paddleboarding in California.\par \par \uc2 But then an hour earlier, to make this even messier because it's inherently messy, because it's Biden-related, the White House released this picture and it shows \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , brace yourselves, indoors at his desk, no mask.\par \par \uc2 So, who shot that picture? Is that person still alive? Does that person have monkeypox?\par \par \uc2 Presumably, the White House photographer is vaccinated. That's got to be a requirement working there. But as we just saw, that may make the photographer more vulnerable to infection and in fact, and we hate to say this, it might mean the photographer is now more likely to face serious health complications.\par \par \uc2 So, underlying all of this is a really ominous fact, and that is a lot of people have been hurt by this. You hate to say it.\par \par \uc2 Germany's Ministry of Health\uc2  found that one in 5,000 Germans have suffered "serious side effects after a COVID-19 vaccine."\par \par \uc2 Now, one in 5,000 may seem like a lot or a little, but extrapolate forward to the United States, a country with our population. That would mean that in the US, if that number holds constant across countries (and why wouldn't it?) it would mean more than 100,000 Americans may have been seriously injured by the COVID vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Why does no one talk about them? Why does nobody care and what happens to them now? If \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  accomplishes a single thing as President, it will be getting more people to ask that question today and it's a fair question and to end, science is about questions. Science is questioning.\par \par \uc2 So, anyone who tells you, you're anti-science for asking a question doesn't understand what science is.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Harvey Risch is a Professor Emeritus of Epidemiology at the Yale School of Public Health, and he joins us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Doctor, thanks so much for coming on.\par \par \uc2 What worries me in all of this is not necessarily what the results are of the studies, though they seem kind of scary. But the fact that no one in charge of our public health systems is talking about it, apologizing for statements they made that were wrong, there is no accountability.\par \par \uc2 I just feel like no one's going to ever trust doctors again after this. Are you worried about that?\par \par \uc2 DR. HARVEY RISCH, PROFESSOR EMERITUS OF EPIDEMIOLOGY, YALE SCHOOL OF PUBLIC HEALTH: Well, I'm worried about the credibility of medicine, about public health, about government institutions, about Congress, people, even nobody has been forthcoming and talking honestly about any of this.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Our whole system, I never thought about this until the last few years, but it's built on trust, and everybody trusts their doctor. I always have, everybody does. People love doctors.\par \par \uc2 Doesn't the medical establishment understand that their credibility is at stake? And that's kind of existential for them and for all of us?\par \par \uc2 RISCH: Well, the problem is that doctors are more afraid of what happens if they go outside the permitted messaging, than just hiding behind, going along to get along, you know, and so their credibility loss follows because they were unwilling to stand up to the message.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: You are one of the few who's had heterodox views on this and has said so publicly, what have other professors you worked with, other physicians that you know, people who have lived in your world for some time, what have they said to you privately?\par \par \uc2 RISCH: I have lots of people who've supported what I've said, people from diverse walks of life and different academic disciplines, not just medicine, epidemiology, and science, that basically everybody has got some reason to be scared about being public, because of negative consequences to them, their economics, their family, and whatever.\par \par \uc2 So they prefer to just kind of be under the radar. And in fact, the telemedicine groups have been under the radar, but have treated more than a quarter-million of Americans with the drugs that one is not allowed to talk about, hydroxychloroquine and ivermectin, very, very successfully, overwhelmingly successful in a quarter of a million people treated that way.\par \par \uc2 And it's all sub rosa, but it's working that way.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Boy, you read accounts of the Soviet Union, Soviet science that was so ideological, that it was insane. Are you worried that that's happening in our country?\par \par \uc2 RISCH: Well, yes, and no, you know, to the degree that people believe our current insanity, I would be worried about it, but I don't know that there's a large amount of belief except for maybe 20 or 30 percent of the medical establishment and the general population that are true believers and the rest are either skeptics or know the truth, but can't really come out with it, can't be public about it.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Oh, man, I feel like we're losing a lot right now.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for your bravery and