portant problem facing the country. Jesse, that might actually be the one percent downtown.\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CO-HOST: Yes, it's true. Air safer?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I think we need the streets safer, not the air, Joe. And that's what happens when you do a shot in front of a landfill, when you have to scramble when Manchin tanks your domestic agenda. You don't give the advance team to set up a good shot.\par \par \uc2 Biden is not a green guy and never was a green guy. He was following Barack's footsteps and now he's following Bernie's footsteps. He probably couldn't explain to you the science of global warming if you asked him straight up. He doesn't know anything about it.\par \par \uc2 He is going to Massachusetts because Massachusetts had this coal plant. And they fired 200 workers from the coal plant to make wind mills now. But guess who owns the wind mill company? The Italians. So, he's picking winners and losers. None of these winners and losers are American companies. He's doing corporate welfare for the Italian companies. I don't understand why he's doing that because it's not even a green state.\par \par \uc2 I looked in to the energy sources for Massachusetts. It's like two-thirds natural gas, a couple little bit coal and a lot nuclear. Less than one percent of energy in Massachusetts comes from renewables. So, you can put wind mills up as much as you want. They're not going to be able to power that state.\par \par \uc2 He has a new poll, Quinnipiac he's at 31 percent. He is clinging for dear life here. That's why he's going up there because his base has one foot out the door.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: You have to think to yourself, Dana, if Massachusetts is such a liberal state and I said yesterday that Delaware, such a liberal state, then how come none of he's states are green? How come none of these states use solar or wind? None of them do. What's stopping the Democratic leaders