mits. We know that the vast majority want a 15-week ban put in place. But they do want people to be able to get reproductive health care.\par \par \uc2 So, when you do this, and then the story switches over to that -- and it's not only conservatives that are going to be talking about it. It's going to be moderate Democrats that are talking about it or someone like \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2 , actually, who was out there as well. But you didn't see footage of her. She was just out there talking about the cause that has mattered to her through decades of public service, talking about her record, what she was doing, and supporting the people who are rightfully upset about this.\par \par \uc2 And maybe it's a feature of having worked with some fantastic Conservative colleagues, but I always look at stories for what is going to happen to the other side when they get their hands on this. And you know, for a fact if you're voluntarily putting your hands behind your back, that people are going to seize on that. And they're not going to talk about the fact that in 26 states now it's basically illegal to get an abortion. So, that's what I think about it.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Greg, do you think --\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: It's basically illegal.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Well, is that not true?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: No, it's not.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Well, I'm --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: We're not going to do the abortion argument.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes., but we been through it.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: But he did.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: We've been through it.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: He did it.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK, do you think -- let's keep it light. Do you think maybe she had invisible handcuffs on?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes, I've seen them. I actually ordered a few on \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . But we -- you got to understand, for many people, being arrested is a new virtue signal for gaining status. There are at least two people I know at this building, or were in