ally be delayed, and that's because of a one-of-a-kind Maryland law which states that absentee ballots, those mail-in ballots, cannot be counted until two days after the primary. So we might be waiting for a bit. Bret?\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, Aishah, thank you. We'll have the numbers tonight if we get them.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, we look at how Asian-American voters apparently are in play for coming elections. The group went for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  by 44 points in 2020. But senior news correspondent Rich Edson tells us this evening many are now making a switch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 RICH EDSON, FOX NEWS STATE DEPARTMENT CORRESPONDENT: Forty-five years ago, John Lin moved from Taiwan to the United States. He went from waiting tables to starting his own commercial real estate firm.\par \par \uc2 JOHN LIN, CAPSTAR COMMERCIAL REALTY CEO: That was one of the most difficult process to train myself to be an entrepreneur.\par \par \uc2 EDSON: Lin also works on a Montgomery County, Maryland, Asian liaison group and helps Asian Americans register to vote.\par \par \uc2 LIN: I feel like people register Democrat but they don't necessarily vote for Democrat because of certain issues.\par \par \uc2 EDSON: He says issues like the economy, crime, education, and the border. Comparing President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  's 2020 exit polls with a spring midterm preview from \uc2 Pew Research\uc2  , Asian voter's support of Democrats is down 16 points. Asian voters say they will still support Democrats in the midterms by a wide margin, 28 percent. But the decline is still the largest among American ethnic groups.\par \par \uc2 Republicans blame Democrats for inflation and criticize them for supporting school admission policies that they say tend to disadvantage Asian students. The \uc2 RNC\uc2  tells FOX, quote, "\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the radical Democrats have left Asian Americans behind, so the AAPI community is returning the favor."\par \par \uc2 FENG OUYANG, ENGINEER: We came here mainly for the purpose of getting our children a better education. Are we going to advance children because of their talent, their achievement, or their level of effort, or are we advancing them because of the skin of color?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 EDSON (on camera): A \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  aide says the party has invested significantly in Asian American voter outreach ahead of the midterm elections, essential to their effort, they say, to protect and expand the Democratic majorities, especially as Asians are the fastest growing group in the United States. Bret?\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Rich, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Major League Baseball's all-star game will be held tonight at Dodger Stadium in Los Angeles. Among the stars, \uc2 Washington Nationals\uc2  outfielder Juan Soto. The 23-year-old won last night's home run derby. Did you see that? You can see the game on the FOX broadcast network, that's the big FOX. Coverage starts at 7:00 eastern time.\par \par \uc2 Up next, Ukraine's first lady meets with the Bidens to talk about her country's efforts to hold off the Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is in Iran on a trip intended to deepen ties with regional heavyweights. It's seen as part of Moscow's challenge to the U.S. and Europe during its campaign in Ukraine. Putin is scheduled to hold talks with the presidents of Iran and Turkey.\par \par \uc2 Meantime, Ukraine's first lady will address members of Congress here in Washington on Capitol Hill tomorrow. Earlier today, \uc2 Olena Zelenska\uc2  accepted the Dissident Human Rights Award in Washington on behalf of the Ukrainian people. And she met with President Biden and America's first lady. Correspondent Alexandria Hoff shows us tonight.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDRIA HOFF, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: President Biden joined the first lady in greeting