o hats in there from you. Freedom matters. And I'm going to wear it tomorrow morning when I workout.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, so it's the golf hat. This is for Bob Woodson's charity Woodson Center. So it's that. I know it's a Krav Maga hat. And then because you're very happy with the feminine side of your life, so this is when you're not sure--\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm really in touch of it. Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: This is when you're kind of malleable on how you identify. That day, you're going to wear this. OK. So, but I just think you got to protect that Irish skin of yours. You don't want to get to - you're very - you're a little orange tonight. Did you notice that? You're very tan, very tan.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I'm very tan.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. It looks good.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Mostly I go outside lately. Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Look, I told you. I knew it. I knew it. You look great and I'm glad you liked the hat.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: No, I'm wearing the hat tomorrow. I'll take a picture and send it to you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Please do, Hannity. Thanks so much and great show as always.\par \par \uc2 All right. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is INGRAHAM ANGLE from Washington tonight.\par \par \uc2 The climate con trolls. That's the focus of tonight's 'Angle'.\par \par \uc2 Now, all the enlightened people, you know who they are, they now insist that summer is no longer supposed to be hot. So any heatwave anywhere by its very existence is evidence of climate change. So they're all reading from the same playbook. With the end game more obvious by the day, the climate propaganda, it's saturating the airwaves.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JAKE TAPPER, CNN HOST: Yes, it's summer. Yes, it's supposed to be hot. But it is never been like this. Dallas and Oklahoma City reached 109 degrees today. Again, this is a global problem.\par \par \uc2 Just look at the heat map. Mexico, Central America, this heat devastation is evidence as if you need more of it, that climate change is here and is a crisis. What scientists and activists have been warning about for decades.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: We knew these temperatures were coming. We might not have known 2022, but we knew they were coming.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Was that guy a PhD? I think he writes for \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 , I don't know. But, remember, they never have to establish actual facts. It's all kind of, I don't know, just a feeling.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We're feeling it. We're literally feeling it. We are enduring the effects of climate change.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Feeling it? Of course, the truth about global warming is never as simple as they claim. So showing this really scary looking temperature map with a bunch of red on it ignores another expert analysis.\par \par \uc2 "The worst heat waves on our planet aren't happening now. They actually occurred 40 years ago. According to a review by researchers from the \uc2 University of Bristol\uc2  in the United Kingdom, we show there have been some even greater extremes in the last few decades, said Vikki Thompson, a climate scientist at the \uc2 University of Bristol\uc2  and lead author of this new paper."\par \par \uc2 And notice, by the way, that the climate controls wailing about how this is the worst heatwave ever, don't acknowledge what happened in Europe almost two decades ago. 35,000 people died, because of what, extreme heat. Yet the left and its media allies, they want strict government controls on how business operates, and eventually, on how we as free citizens live.\par \par \uc2 So it's just more fodder for liberals to call for the Senate to be abolished. As this writer for the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  argued today, because they blather on about extreme heat. How about their extreme solutions?\par \par \uc2 Like blowing up the constitution