here. And the partnership with the -- with the Arabs is essential because we need them to counter the Iranians who are -- who are on the march in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 And yes, it's going to take some time though to rebuild that trust.\par \par \uc2 HEMMER: General, thank you. Jack Keane with his analysis tonight. We'll talk again, General, thank you.\par \par \uc2 In a moment here, governors from across the country need to find bipartisan solutions but new state abortion laws might get in the way of finding common ground.\par \par \uc2 And as we head to break, we remember \uc2 Ivana Trump\uc2  this evening, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's first wife died today. She was the mother of Donald Jr., Ivanka and Eric.\par \par \uc2 An accomplished skier, she fled Eastern Europe to start a new life in the U.S. and what a life that was. Late word today, Fox confirms that she was found at the bottom of a staircase in her New York City apartment. \uc2 Ivana Trump\uc2  was 73.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HEMMER: Governors from across the country gathering in person today. The goal of these summer meeting is to work together on policy issues.\par \par \uc2 But with poor attendance in some of the nation's most pressing issues being left off the table, the focus has shifted to presidential politics.\par \par \uc2 Bryan Llenas is in Portland, Maine with details on that tonight.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: There are opportunities for us to find common ground and consensus.\par \par \uc2 BRYAN LLENAS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL NATIONAL CORRESPONDENT (voice-over): Today, the \uc2 National Governors Association\uc2  gathered in Portland, Maine for its annual summer meeting, an efforts to bring the nation's 55 governors together to focus on bipartisan solutions.\par \par \uc2 This year, just 19 governors attended on the agenda, K through 12, computer science education, and the return of travel and tourism. Not on the agenda, the elephant in the room, abortion, inflation, crime, and the governor's eyeing potential 2024 presidential runs.\par \par \uc2 Like Republican Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and Democratic California Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 . Neither attended the conference, but both are rising stars, after Newsom released a campaign ad in Florida attacking DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 GOV. GAVIN NEWSOM (D-CA): I urge all of you living in Florida to join the fight or join us in California, but we still believe in freedom.\par \par \uc2 LLENAS: The \uc2 Republican Governors Association\uc2  attacked Newsom in a video, tweeting, "Bold to invite Floridians to move to California when you're literally out of U-hauls.\par \par \uc2 Other Republican governors at the conference like Maryland Governor \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , and Arkansas Governor Asa Hutchinson both left the door open for 2024.\par \par \uc2 GOV. \uc2 LARRY HOGAN\uc2 , (R-MD): My only interest would be if I -- if I thought I was going to make a difference. And I thought we had a chance to win.\par \par \uc2 GOV. ASA HUTCHINSON (R-AR): I want to help shape the future of our party and our country and that might lead to a presidential campaign down the road.\par \par \uc2 But first, Republican leadership is focused on winning gubernatorial races this November.\par \par \uc2 GOV. DOUG DUCEY (R-AZ): We have 36 races. So, I see the opportunity to really expand this map.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LLENAS (on camera): New NGA chair Democrat governor of New Jersey, \uc2 Phil Murphy\uc2 , tells Fox News, he will 1,000 percent support President Biden as the nominee in 2024. And he says he's fully confident the party will too. Bill?\par \par \uc2 HEMMER: Well watch it together, Bryan. Thank you, Bryan Llenas in Maine tonight.\par \par \uc2 There is a new report from conservatives raising the alarm over trust in elections among Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 The authors warned, if a large percentage of Americans don't believe the process is fair, it could harm the country for years to come.\par \par \uc2 Chief Washington correspondent Mike Emanuel walks us through that report tonight.\par \par \uc2 MIKE EMANUEL, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CHIEF WASHINGTON CORRESPONDENT (voice-over): Lost, not stolen, is a new 72-page report, "making the conservative case that Trump lost and Biden won the 2020 presidential election."\par \par \uc2 Its authors find, "There is absolutely no evidence of fraud in the 2020 presidential election on the magnitude necessary to shift the result in any state, let alone the nation as a whole. In fact, there was no fraud that changed the outcome in even a single precinct.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BEN GINSBERG, LEGAL ANALYST, CNN: Once \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost all those 64 court cases, he had an obligation under our form of government and our institutions to say that to concede.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Ben Ginsberg is a leading Republican election attorney who helped \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2  in the Florida recount in 2000.\par \par \uc2 Other conservatives participating in this review, two former U.S. senators, a former chief of staff to the Senate Majority Leader and House Speaker, a former solicitor general, and three former federal appeals court judges.\par \par \uc2 THOMAS GRIFFIN, FORMER FEDERAL JUDGE: So, we will have to find out what really happened from our own vantage point, not relying on what others told us.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL (on camera): And to be clear, if you found meaningful evidence, you guys would be out there in the fight, right?\par \par \uc2 GINSBERG: If there was meaningful evidence of fraud, we would be out there in the vanguard, saying you got to fix the system, because it is crucial that people believe in elections.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Griffin, says as part of this investigation, they found the American election system works.\par \par \uc2 GRIFFIN: We don't have a great deal of confidence and a great deal of pride in our election administration system.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: But the issue is still brought up by the former president.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , FORMER PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: The election was rigged and stolen.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: And on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: We can't move on past 2020, because they don't actually know what happened.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: With midterms just four months away, these conservatives say that approach is a losing strategy for the GOP.\par \par \uc2 GINSBERG: It is going to depress Republican turnout that if voters come to think their votes don't matter, because the results are rigged, they'll stay home.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: The authors of the study say candidates should run instead on conservative ideas in response to Democrats currently being in charge, and to be forward looking about what they would do if elected. Bill.\par \par \uc2 HEMMER: Big topic, Mike. Thanks, Mike Emanuel in Washington tonight.\par \par \uc2 HEMMER (voice-over): In a moment, as Paris celebrates Bastille Day, American World War II veteran receive France's highest military honor.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HEMMER: A federal grand jury has indicted the Buffalo shooting suspect under federal hate crimes and firearms violations. The Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  announcing charges against Payton Gendron.\par \par \uc2 The indictment alleges the 19 year old willfully shot his victims because of their race He is accused of killing 10 people, all African Americans during a May 14th rampage at a grocery store.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina attorney Alex Murdaugh has been charged with murder. He's accused of killing his wife and son outside their home last year. The indictments do not include details on how police linked Murdaugh to the shootings. After 13 month investigation he has denied involvement. Murdaugh is currently jailed on fraud 