)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: People wanted to really see you get mad when Trump started lying about Hunter.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Well, you know, I would like to be able to be back in high school and just have he and I in a room.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: As a mother, how hurtful have these attacks been on Hunter for you?\par \par \uc2 JILL BIDEN, FIRST LADY OF THE UNITED STATES: I have been really hurtful. I mean--\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. That was humiliating for the media and a humiliating performance by Jill. It's embarrassing.\par \par \uc2 Jill's bad acting - we know now from Hunter's reportedly leaked text messages from the laptop from hell that the two of them had a terrible relationship. I mean, really bad. So who's smarter? The druggie, or the doctor?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JILL BIDEN: As unique as the breakfast tacos here in San Antonio.\par \par \uc2 HUNTER BIDEN, CO-FOUNDER, ROSEMONT SENECA PARTNERS: 2.07 without the bag.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think it's a tie. But it's very embarrassing. But the real humiliation for America isn't the family drama, or Joe's shuffling and stumbling? It's what he's doing to the once great economy of ours that was handed to him by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Today, we saw the biggest gain in consumer prices since 1981. And the humiliation that keeps on giving, you bet, because here's our Vice President trying to reassure the public.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: There is no question that we still have work to do. But it is important to note that these numbers do not fully reflect the recent drop in gas prices. Average national gas prices have fallen every day for nearly 30 days.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: She doesn't even looks like she believes it, right? I mean, yes, saving a few cents a gallon here and there. Time to pop up in the champagne, America. I paid $6.03 this morning in Maryland.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: When I look at this report, I don't see any relief anywhere. Even before we got to this 9.1 percent, there had been some sectors that were behaving a little bit better. I look at rents going up. I didn't see any relief in apparel.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Red, red, red. By year three of the Trump administration, remember, we had no inflation and we saw median incomes rising. But now, well, wage growth is declining at historic rates. The situation is so bad that Obama's former chief economist says, it's terrible right now.\par \par \uc2 As cataclysmic as the Biden economy is for American families, one of the most humiliating aspects of the entire charade is our open border. Now, look at this sea of humanity crossing now at Eagle Pass, Texas. A country that refuses to control its border, I mean, is it a country at all?\par \par \uc2 This dereliction of immigration enforcement is an impeachable offense. I'm going to say it again. It's an impeachable offense. It's hurting and it's changing our entire country. It allows deadly fentanyl to pour in, enriches the cartels, strains our budget. Look at what it's going to do to our health care and our schools.\par \par \uc2 And as President Trump said in 2015, they're sending their rapists, including 27-year-old Gershon Fuentes. He was just arrested for raping a 10-year-old girl in Ohio on at least two occasions. And according to an ICE source, he is here, of course, illegally.\par \par \uc2 And, of course, the humiliation for America overseas, got to get into that, because that knows no bounds. Last summer was the botched withdrawal of Afghanistan, leading to the deaths of 13 servicemembers, and a self- inflicted Afghan refugee nightmare unfolding here.\par \par \uc2 And now, we're being humiliated in Ukraine, spending more than $7 billion so far