industries and is now going hat in hand to Mohammed bin bonesaw Salman begging for oil. Total humiliation.\par \par \uc2 We could go on and on, because under Biden and Biden land, the humiliation of America never ends. But what we all need to understand is that the Biden team doesn't really feel humiliated at all. They think their low poll numbers are due to a messaging problem. You heard them out there today trying to message their way out of this.\par \par \uc2 They don't care if Hunter is compromised and making money corruptly. They certainly don't care about inflation, or if gas prices are too high. They definitely don't care about schools failing our kids, or if China is pushing us around. Those aren't points of humiliation at all to them.\par \par \uc2 In fact, at some level, they believe America deserves to be humiliated. America deserves to be brought to heel, and ultimately to bend to a new international order. But I'm wagering that the voters in November are going to show Biden's party that they don't much like being humiliated by individuals whose incompetence goes hand in hand with their anti- Americanism. And that's the 'Angle'.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now is \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , former 2020 Democratic presidential candidate and former Hawaii Congresswoman. Tulsi, the number we've approved for Ukraine weapons and aid is $70 billion. So I said seven, that's wishful thinking.\par \par \uc2 So Americans are seeing their finances hollowed out here at home as we ship billions abroad. And the war looks like it's going in the wrong direction. How do we reach any conclusion except this is the ongoing humiliation of America and our foreign policy once again?\par \par \uc2 TULSI GABBARD (D) FMR 2020 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: Well, Laura, you're bringing up such critical points here that the American people need to understand the seriousness of the situation that the Biden administration and leaders in Washington have put us in.\par \par \uc2 So we go beyond kind of the day to day battle updates of what's happening in our proxy war against Russia and Ukraine. And actually take a step back and focus on the big picture and the great threat that we face, which is the reality that this war is continuing to escalate.\par \par \uc2 President Biden himself says, he has no idea when or how it's going to end. But we know where this escalation leads. It leads us closer and closer to the brink of a nuclear war with Russia.\par \par \uc2 We just saw the other day in New York City, I'm sure you saw how they put out a PSA telling residents of New York City, Hey, here's what you do in the event of a nuclear attack. Go inside, stay inside, and stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 I almost fell out of my chair when I saw that PSA, because it's insane. They're treating this as though we're like back in the 50s and 60s when teachers are telling kids to go under your desk and you'll be protected from a nuclear attack. It's crazy.\par \par \uc2 The reality is President Biden, members of Congress, leaders in our country, the wealthy, they will have a safe place to be in the event of a nuclear war that they are behind causing, while the rest of us in America and Russia, people around the world will be decimated from this event.\par \par \uc2 And yet they treat it as though it's nothing. It's nothing to take seriously. They're even making plans on how they can continue to wage this war from an underground bunker. This is the seriousness of the threat that we face. And how crazy and disturbing it is that President Biden and people in this administration can be so nonchalant about how they are the ones who are continuing to drive this forward. Cavalier, exactly.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Tonight, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , Tulsi, is reporting that Ukrainians say, they need faster shipments of long range artillery and other sophisticated weapons to blunt Russia's steady advance. So the Pentagon now is concerned about potentially depleting our stockpiles in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 So the word depletion is just becoming too common for Americans to hear these days. Our finances are being depleted, our weapons are being depleted. Our artillery stockpiles and our oil is being depleted from the strategic petroleum reserves. Our spirit is being depleted by this administration.\par \par \uc2 GABBARD: Yes, you're completely right. And that's where this trip that President Biden is taking now. He'll soon be going to Saudi Arabia really exposes what a complete farce his whole autocracy versus democracy foreign policy is.\par \par \uc2 He's saying, Hey, we've got to go and get help to wage war against Russia. And in order to save "democracy". And I'm going to go talk to a bunch of autocratic dictators and ask them for oil and ask them for help to do it.\par \par \uc2 We see that with Saudi Arabia, an Islamist autocracy. We see that with Turkey, another guy who wants to be Caliph of his own new caliphate and Ottoman Empire who's guilty of genocide against the Kurds there. It is a sham. It is a lie that the American people need to see straight through and hold leaders accountable for that lie. And for the cost that they are bringing on to the American people and frankly, to the world, the further they escalate this war.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. Mohammed bin bonesaw is going to demand a lot for any oil that he gives us. But I bet he gives us nothing. It's going to be like the godfather. How's nothing sound to you? That's what he's going to do.\par \par \uc2 Tulsi, it's great to see you tonight as always.\par \par \uc2 And with Biden distracted abroad, fresh new face took his spot at 1600 Pennsylvania Avenue. Pretty boy Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , he swooped into meetings in the West Wing today, setting political tongues a wagon.\par \par \uc2 Fox's chief breaking news correspondent Trace Gallagher has all the details. Trace?\par \par \uc2 TRACE GALLAGHER, CHIEF BREAKING NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Hey, Laura. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  insists he has zero White House ambitions, and yet you see the video he is walking into the White House. Where he met with the First Lady, potentially also his California colleague vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and other Biden officials.\par \par \uc2 Newsom is ostensibly in town to accept an award from an education group for his work in getting kids into preschool. The education group is not to be confused with the California teachers unions, who for 18 months during the pandemic, ignored Newsom and controlled and shut down public schools at their whim.\par \par \uc2 Newsom is also being awarded for California also not being awarded for his California's public school performance, not exactly the envy of the nation. But some believe, this whole Newsom goes to Washington show is actually the first step to building a national brand and setting up a potential presidential run in 2028, or even a kind of save the party run in 2024 if needed.\par \par \uc2 Though, Newsom says, he emphatically supports a Biden re-election. And Newsom is already generating chatter by going after red state governors like \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Here's part of an ad Newsom ran in Florida on Fourth of July on Fox News. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. GAVIN NEWSOM (D-CA): I urge all of you living in Florida to join the fight, or join us in California. But we still believe in freedom, freedom of speech, freedom to choose, freedom from hate, and the freedom to love. Don't let them take your freedom.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Newsom did not talk about California high point, high crime, high taxes, high gas, high housing, and an incredibly high number of homeless people. And if Newsom is trying to generate national support, he might want to explain why California has now banned state-funded travel to 22 states, including Montana where Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  just traveled with state-funded security.\par \par \uc2 By the way, the Newsom DC trip is supposed to last for days, meaning he might still sneak in a French Laundry visit Saturday night late - late Saturday night.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Trace, he seemed very happy prancing around the White House. It was like a special spring in his step today. Thanks so much, Trace.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Yes. You bet.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And if we know the vaccines don't stop the spread of COVID, and they do not, why are soldiers and athletes still being subjected to these insane draconian mandates? Some remarkable pushback in moments.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, that was the scene in France as opposition MPs rejected a proposal from Macron to reinstate the requirement for travelers entering the country to show a proof of vaccination or negative COVID tests.\par \par \uc2 Well, we know the vaccines don't stop the spread. Even Dr. Fauci was forced to admit that. Yet mandates are still the norm in the Americas. So although the U.S. Open in New York City allows visitors without proof of vaccination, one of the best tennis players of all time, Novak Djokovic will not be able to play in the U.S. Open because of COVID requirements for the international travelers set by our government.\par \par \uc2 Canada will still not allowed professional athletes who refuse the jab from entering their country. And instead of relenting to pressure, \uc2 Philadelphia Phillies\uc2  catcher JT Realmuto spoke the truth.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JT REALMUTO, CATCHER FOR THE \uc2 PHILADELPHIA PHILLIES\uc2 : I'm a healthy 31-year- old professional athlete. I just didn't feel a need to get it. I had COVID a couple of times and super mild symptoms back when it first came out.\par \par \uc2 And when it came time to decide whether I needed a vaccine or not, talked with a couple of doctors that I knew and told them my story and just really decided I didn't think I needed it. And I wasn't going to take it just because I was told to basically, so.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: You're going to forfeit a good amount of salary.\par \par \uc2 REALMUTO: Yes. I mean, what's money when - I'm not going to let Canada tell me what I do and don't put in my body.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh gosh, he's great. But it isn't just athletes as Raymond Arroyo reported Friday night.\par \par \uc2 Roughly 40,000 National Guardsmen and 22,000 reservists who have refused the vaccine will be barred from their duties. Apparently we just have so many reservists, we don't need those people. Now, this is all allowed because of the defense authorization passed last November with broad bipartisan support. You cannot make this up.\par \par \uc2 This cannot be allowed to stand. And this show is going to start targeting any Republican who joins on to this year's defense authorization without this vaccine requirement stricken from the bill. It's high time this is done.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now Republican Florida Congressman Byron Donalds. Congressman, it seems that Republicans have difficulty with this concept. Democrats running a woke military are a threat to the United States of America, the way the Democrats are doing this. They're threatening us. And the Republicans are like, how much more money do you want? Approved, approved, approved? When is this going to end?\par \par \uc2 REP. BYRON DONALDS (R-FL): Laura, I completely agree with you. Listen, I am supportive of our military just like every member of the Republican Congress. But we have to draw the line somewhere.\par \par \uc2 Look, first the number one thing, we're going to fund the military up here on Capitol Hill. So let's not have anybody think that's not going to happen. But what we have to stop are these ridiculous woke policies in our military budget. Why would we do that?\par \par \uc2 The purpose of a military is to win conflicts and to basically defeat people on the battlefield. That's the job. No more, no less. So fund woke ideology to continue these ridiculous COVID mandates against men and women who serve our country with honor and distinction is despicable and it shouldn't be tolerated.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, the problem though, is you write, we write, the taxpayers write a check to the Pentagon, right? I mean is it really segmented off to this and that? I don't know, you tell me. But it seems to me the power of the purse has to be used at some point. Because otherwise we just say, well, we love the military. We're going to give them the money they need.\par \par \uc2 Well, if you do that, you're going to get CRT, transgenderism and vax mandates. So that's what the Republicans are funding right now.\par \par \uc2 DONALDS: Actually, we do have the power of the purse to make those distinctions and we should. And I think that's one of the issues that does exist amongst Republicans is do we do that now, or do we do it later? But for my attitude and perspectives, it's never the wrong time to do the right thing.\par \par \uc2 We should make those points right now loud and clear, so whether it's \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and with two majorities, or \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  with no majorities, he understands exactly where Republicans stand with respect to how military operations are going to be conducted in the United States.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, we also learned that with $70 billion in weaponry and other humanitarian assistance we're sending Ukraine, now there's real concern logical that we can't track the weapons. And that some of these weapons are ending up on the dark web and will be sold throughout the world and then used against American interests. How concerned are you about this, given the lack of accountability thus far?\par \par \uc2 DONALDS: I'm incredibly concerned. It's one of the reasons in the last $40 billion package I voted no on that package. And it's not because of a lack of support for Ukraine, it's because of a lack of controls on with the Biden administration about how this funding was going to go forward.\par \par \uc2 Look, this is the same administration that left $85 billion of military hardware in Afghanistan. And there's been no accounting for that where those weapons have ended up. So it's a serious problem. And we have to stop just being supportive of funding military operations without putting in the necessary controls of how those dollars are going to be spent, and how they're going to be accounted for. You can't do both things up here on Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congressman, great to see you. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 And speaking of ignorance about medical issues, the left really thought that holding hearings on abortion access post Roe was going to help them like connect with American voters. Well, instead over the past 24 hours, they've revealed themselves as not just out of touch, but frankly ghoulish.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Do you support infanticide, killing the child after he's born?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I do not agree with the basis of that question. But I do believe that abortion is healthcare. My abortion was the best decision I ever made. It was an act of self love.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: For some, abortion is liberation. There was a lot of good that comes from the people's ability to access abortion. And I want to celebrate that.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Explain what these fake health clinics are and how they promote an anti-abortion agenda.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: So someone may show up at a crisis pregnancy center believing that they are going to a place that can help facilitate access to abortion and be totally fooled.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So much for safe, legal and rare.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Mollie Hemingway, Fox News contributor and editor in chief at The Federalist. Mollie, I was watching this today. And it actually made my stomach turn. Because these women I know, you know so many of them at these pregnancy centers are just the most selfless. They're incredible. They're angels helping women in need. Women who are - clearly have no one to help them. And this is how they're portrayed.\par \par \uc2 MOLLIE HEMINGWAY, EDITOR-IN-CHIEF, THE FEDERALIST: It's just amazing that at this moment. And yes, Democrats clearly thought that holding hearings on abortion would help them politically.\par \par \uc2 What they didn't calculate was that they would be revealing just how radical their positions are. Their position is that they support abortion for any reason whatsoever through all nine months of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 If your child is a girl, and you don't want to have a girl, they think it should be ok to kill that child at nine months into a pregnancy. Having to defend that type of position is so radical and so toxic, I think, to the American public. But they're taking an issue where they might have had a little bit of political play, and they're actually turning off American voters.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, all the polls are showing it's absolutely helping them not at all, which you and I predicted a couple of weeks back. It wasn't going to help them at all.\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: I think they thought about the suburban districts where there are these wealthy white women who are easily persuadable that they nabbed in recent elections. And I do think that that might help them in some of those districts.\par \par \uc2 What they neglected to think about were the dozens of districts where you're having these very large Hispanic populations that are completely turned off, not just by the radical abortion policies, but the attacks on Roman Catholic churches and other Christian churches, the arson attempts and other things at these maternal care centers, attacks on federal judges. Those things don't play as well outside the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  newsroom and outside the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  newsroom as Democrats need them.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, to your point, Rhode Island's David Cicilline delivered, what I think is a straight up lie at today's House Judiciary Committee.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. DAVID CICILLINE (D-RI): The notion that anyone is suggesting that abortion should happen up until the birth date is an absurdity and deeply offensive to women who are making important health care decisions every single day.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, the Women's Health Protection Act with Cicilline and almost every Democrat voting for would have allowed that, Mollie.\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: Yes, nearly every single Democrat voted for something that would have prohibited people from being allowed to have any protection of any kind at any stage in a pregnancy in any state. It's a really radical piece of legislation. It's officially what they believe. And again, polling shows that the vast number of Americans support at least some restriction on abortion. And of course, the entire world supports at least some restriction on abortion.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Remember when New York had that standing ovation in Albany in the state legislature for basically abortion on demand up until birth, and they got up and they stood and gave it a standing ovation. Ghoulish.\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: It is ghoulish, and it is horrible. All abortion ends a human life violently in the womb. So no matter what your position on abortion should be, it is never to be celebrated.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Again, safe, legal and rare used to be what the Democrats believed. Mollie, thank you so much. Great to see you tonight.\par \par \uc2 OK, here's a clue for tonight's "Wit's End" segment, and I will reveal the answer at the end of the show. What's the latest way the Democrats are trying to stick it to the uber rich? Tweet me your guesses @IngrahamAngle, we'll see if you get it right.\par \par \uc2 But up next, liberals are protesting the Roe decision via medical procedures. You won't believe this one. And the Emmy nominations reveal where we are as a culture, the good and the bad. "Seen and Unseen" with Raymond Arroyo is next. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's time for our "Seen and Unseen" segment where we expose the cultural stories of the day. And for that we turn to FOX News contributor Raymond Arroyo. All right, Raymond, the president is in Israel tonight.\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND ARROYO, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Yes, but, Laura, the change of location has not helped the primary difficulty here. This is the president asking, where do I go, just before he left for Israel yesterday. And after landing in Tel Aviv, he still didn't know where he was supposed to go.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: What am I doing now?\par \par \uc2 Later today, I will once more return to the hallowed ground of Yad Vashem to keep alive the truth and honor of the holocaust -- horror of the holocaust.\par \par \uc2 And so I hope that we pay attention to one another.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Laura, at least we can be thankful he didn't compare the Israelis to matzoh ball soup or falafel. So this is a big improvement over recent days. But they move him around like a wax work at Madame Tussauds. While the international alliance collapses in the Middle East, falls to pieces. Meanwhile, Putin is about to meet with Iran just as Joe leaves the Middle East. Good luck to that foreign policy.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Raymond, is this a staffing problem? Are they not tell him where he is supposed to go, or does he forget? It is a long trip, and maybe he is just a little tired. Maybe he only can work a few hours a day.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Let's hope so.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And back home, Raymond, Kamala was taking care of the major issues facing the country, I understand, and it is tonight's "Harris Rerun Rerun."\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Rerun.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , (D) VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Together we are expanding access to transportation. It seems like maybe it's a small issue. It's a big issue. You need to get to go and need to be able to get where you need to go to do the work and get home.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And go.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Laura, this could turn out to be one of the great American drinking games, games where people drink in America every time she repeats something, the drinking games could happen in America. I'm looking forward to that. We should start that here.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: She is struggling there, Raymond.\par \par \uc2 Let's move on to the nominees for T.V.'s highest honors which were just announced, I understand. What did they tell us?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: For starters, the most-watched scripted drama on television, "Yellowstone" got no nominations at all.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Of course, of course.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Nothing, Laura. But you will be happy to know Lizzo got a nod for best competition show. It's called "Lizzo's Watch Out for the Big Girls." I'm not sure what this plus-size competition is since I have never watched it, but it might have something to do with who has the most resilient Lycra. We will update you on that. But --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They're having a lot of fun. They're having a lot of fun there on that show it looks like.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I guess.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: "Yellowstone," of course they stiff-armed "Yellowstone," the best show, the absolute best show. And it has conservative kind of general sort of sentiment, old west. They hate the old west.\par \par \uc2 Dave Chappelle also got a nod, Raymond, for his "Closer" comedy special which is pretty remarkable given all his controversies.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: What's really remarkable, Laura, is the nominee for outstanding narrator, it went to the new Jack Hanna, the David Attenborough of our generation, because when you think nature, this is the only man you think of.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: This sloth has an entire micro kingdom living in his further.\par \par \uc2 BARACK OBAMA\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT: Wild spaces are where we can connect with ourselves, our families, and something greater than us.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: They may as well have called this category, Laura, outstanding narration by someone elected president from 2009-2017. Come on, you know who is going to win this one.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Didn't he already win an Emmy, an Oscar? Didn't he win every award? Of course, the Nobel Peace Prize for being in office for five minutes. You remember that?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He won pretty much everything. What else?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: He has got just about everything and the Nobel.\par \par \uc2 Finally, there is a new trend of turning to medical procedures to protest the Supreme Court's abortion decision, and not only women are doing it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: More men are taking action themselves in the aftermath of Roe v. Wade, turning to vasectomies.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I've always thought about this decision. The Supreme Court did push me to finally do it.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: For Figueroa (ph) this is also about easing the burden on women who have had their constitutional right to abortion taken away.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I feel for a lot of men, especially for myself, that this is a way where they are trying to protect their girlfriends, they're trying to protect their partners.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, my God.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Oh, please, he's protecting himself. Give me a break. How do you like sterility as protest. And that's what we are seeing here, Laura. The most disturbing thing women apparently, according to "Newsweek," last week the \uc2 Google\uc2  searches for "female sterility" was through the roof, sterilization of females. So this is really, and what you saw here is the media, it's a propaganda push for sterility rather than motherhood, fatherhood, love together to build a family, or taking care of mothers in need. That's what we should be showing through the media, not pushing people to stop their reproduction. And not all these vasectomies, by the way, can be reversed. Just word to the wise, fellows.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I hate to cut this segment short on the --\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Careful there.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Raymond, first of all, he looks like, what is the senator's name from Georgia? The young guy? Ossoff. He looks like Ossoff. Doesn't he.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yes, he does.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That kid, he looks like if pajama boy meets Ossoff. I'm not sure what got in his mind, but he is going to regret that decision. Raymond, great to see you.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: It's not his mind you have to worry about.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Very good. We've got to cut this. All right, Raymond, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Is Pennsylvania Democratic Senate candidate \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  healthy enough to run? We have some new video that raises serious doubts. Plus the woman looking to take out Gretchen witless Whitmer has some good news about the Michigan's governor's race in moments. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: In tonight's "Retaking America" segment, we take a closer look at the Pennsylvania Senate race, and specifically the health of Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 . This race is of interest not just because it could help determine the balance of the Senate, but because of Fetterman's absence on the campaign trail. Just two days before his May primary he sadly suffered a stroke and underwent surgery to get a pacemaker due to an irregular heart rhythm. Weeks after that we learned of another health issue that he hadn't revealed was back in 2017. Fetterman was diagnosed with a decreased heart pump. His cardiologist at the time, Ramesh Chandra, prescribed medications along with improved diet and exercise, and asked him to follow up again in the following months. Instead, she didn't see him for five years. And after he had his stroke, that is when she did see him. And this past week in his campaign touted what was supposedly his big return to the trail, which is actually more of a just thank you to his staffers.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOHN FETTERMAN\uc2 , (D) PENNSYLVANIA SENATE CANDIDATE: I am feeling so great. And we will be back on the trail soon.\par \par \uc2 It eerily almost was at the end of my life. We know what is at stake in this race right now. We need to make sure that we bring Josh (ph) and send me to D.C.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We are glad that Fetterman seems to be somewhat recovering and we are rooting for him to be healthy, of course. But we couldn't help but notice that this appearance wasn't incredibly encouraging. It should raise serious questions about his ability not just to run, but to serve if he were to win.\par \par \uc2 In the 2020 Biden's campaign unveiled what we know it was just a basement strategy. They kept him hidden from view, limited his events and his interviews. It obviously worked as we never got a full picture of what was his obvious decline. The media didn't cover it. And likewise, Fetterman's absence from the trail right now because the media is not interested in it, it's not hurting him. He leads Dr. Oz by nine points in the latest poll. So the media ran cover for Biden and you see what they got the country. They cannot do the same to the people of Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 And as for Dr. Oz, this isn't too sensitive for him to discuss. As a former cardiothoracic surgeon, he knows all too well the limitations that Fetterman faces. The people of Pennsylvania need to know that they will have not just a good steward of policy but someone who can fully participate in the representation that the state deserves.\par \par \uc2 And now to Michigan, where we are less than three weeks away from the Republican primary there to decide who is going to take on Governor Gretchen witless Whitmer in November. The latest poll shows businesswoman Tudor Dixon surging from a two-point lead to an 11-point lead over her competitors in just a two-week span. However, when head-to-head against Whitmer, Dixon is down 11 points, leading some to claim that the red wave may be a mirage.\par \par \uc2 Tudor Dixon joins me now. Tudor, obviously it's very early. There is not a one-to-one matchup here, but how much stock do you put in that poll given the fact that the primary hasn't even been sorted out yet?\par \par \uc2 TUDOR DIXON, (R) MICHIGAN GUBERNATORIAL CANDIDATE: I think it is a great sign. I think them putting that out there means that they are definitely afraid of what this matchup could bring. And you know what, it's interesting because we are hearing people say this could be the epic race in the middle of the country, having two women battle out, the conservative mom. And she is, I guess, referring to herself these days as the far left birthing parent.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Is she really saying that? She's not saying that. Is that a joke?\par \par \uc2 DIXON: No, when I started this race, when I started this race. We were fighting for fairness in girls' sports. And then a few weeks ago she came out and she started to erase women, and we were "menstruating people." It's like the last thing I want to be called as a menstruating person. And then last week, the teachers' union, which we know the teachers' union she is bought and paid for by, came out and said we are going to take "moms" out of anything written, and we are going to replace it with "birthing parents." And she is on board with that.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK, well, the damage that her policies did to the children of Michigan and, obviously, to the parents of the children in Michigan, just in the COVID closures, that is reason enough for her to be booted out of office. Just that. Forget all the other stuff she's down.\par \par \uc2 But I should also add, Tudor, that just today she signed an executive order refusing to extradite women coming to Michigan seeking abortions, saying in her press release that "As states pursue extreme abortion bans and prosecute those seeking and providing abortion care, Michigan will refuse to cooperate with the criminalization of women's health." Your response?\par \par \uc2 DIXON: Let's look at what she has gone to the president to try to do, because she said over the weekend that she went to President Biden and asked him to work with Canada to try to open abortion clinics for women in Michigan. But lets remember what she has not done. She has not gone to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and asked him to do something to increase energy independence in this country, to decrease gas prices. In fact, this is a woman who is running to shut down another pipeline in Michigan. So while she is concerned about whether or not we can get rid of babies, we can't afford gas, and she is doing nothing there.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: A vote for \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  is a vote to keep gas prices high in Michigan. Is it not?\par \par \uc2 DIXON: Absolutely, because we have a pipeline here that she is actively trying to shut down, because we know Democrats love to shut down pipelines. And this would increase the cost of gas in our state, not only would it increase the cost of gas, it would increase the cost of jet fuel and it would be more difficult to do business here. She is bad for business, and she is bad for students.\par \par \uc2 Tudor, we're going to be watching this very closely, and we really appreciate your joining us tonight. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 And our "Wit's End" segment is next. Remember, here's the clue -- what is the latest way the Democrats are trying to stick it to the uber rich, stick it to the uber rich? Tweet me your answers @IngrahamAngle. We're going to see if you get it right, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What's the latest way the Democrats are trying to stick it to the uber rich. Lori tweeted, "By forces them to buy electric cars." Bobbie wrote, "Raise taxes on limousines or caviar?" And John guessed, "Tariffs on imported foie gras?" Here is the big reveal.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It's time to eat the rich. We've got Bill Gates. We've got Jack Ma, \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg\uc2 , \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 , and the most popular, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . Let's go, baby.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Tastes good.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Protesting capitalism by practicing capitalism, I'll take it.\par \par \uc2 New trucker hat, this is really cool, red, white, and blue. Freedom Matters, go to LauraIngraham.com. Proceeds go to the Woodson Center this month.\par \par \uc2 And "GUTFELD!" is next.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020220714ei7d00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Economic Indicators Are Getting Even Worse; Rapist In Biden's Abortion Story Concerning A 10-Year-Old Child Is An Illegal Immigrant; Adam Schiff's Capitol Hill Power Grab; All Cops And Adults Have Duty To Rush In And Save Kids When They Are Crying For Help\b0\par\par\uc2 Tucker Carlson, Trace Gallagher \par \uc2 7,500 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 July 2022\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: Tucker Carlson Tonight\par \uc2 TCARL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: "Jesse, you seem like a busy person? How did you read two books on a weekend?" I didn't. I read two books in a week and then I talked about it after the weekend was over.\par \par \uc2 That's all for us tonight. DVR the show.\par \par \uc2 Tucker is up next. Always remember, I am Watters, and this is my world.\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: Good evening and welcome to Tucker Carlson tech.\par \par \uc2 When we say "Good evening," we mean it, and tonight, we want to send a special, as they say on talk radio, shout out to our most loyal and faithful viewers. We love you. We appreciate you.\par \par \uc2 In fact, we think of you as all little tacos and your children as taquitos and not just tacos and taquitos, but also enchiladas and chalupas and everything else on the \uc2 Taco Bell\uc2  menu. That's how we think of you.\par \par \uc2 So, the good news is America at this stage is getting a lot more amusing. The bad news is it's also getting a little scary.\par \par \uc2 So today, in the second category, the government announced that inflation has once again set a year-over-year record. But now, we're used to this. If you buy anything, you already knew it was happening. Boy, did you.\par \par \uc2 But there were parts of today's Labor Department report that were not expected by anyone. In fact, they were bizarre. They seemed to defy the most basic rules of economics, but first, here are the raw numbers. This is from a FOX News report today.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CAROLINE SHIVELY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Inflation cranked up a whopping 9.1 percent in June, the highest yearly jump since 1981.\par \par \uc2 The Consumer Price Index, released Wednesday morning, showed the price of necessities far outpacing raises. The price of gas is up almost 60 percent year-over-year. Rent went up 5.6 percent over last June and food at home and dining out, increasing 10.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 If you break it down to just groceries, the annual jump was 12.2 percent. That includes eggs up 33 percent and butter up 26 percent.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, the biggest annual spike in inflation in more than 40 years. That's the headline. But if anything, it understates what's actually going on. The reality of it is worse than that.\par \par \uc2 During the Carter years, when inflation famously hit 14.6 percent, wages were still going up. As Pew put it in a recent analysis, "During the high inflation years of the 1970s and early 1980s, average wages commonly jumped seven, eight, even nine percent year-over-year" and that makes sense.\par \par \uc2 There's more money in circulation. It's worth less, but there's more of it. But that is not what is happening right now and that's the weird thing.\par \par \uc2 According to the Labor Department report today, "Real average hourly earnings decreased 3.6 percent, seasonally adjusted from June 2021 to June 2022. The change in real average hourly earnings, combined with a decrease of 0.9 percent of the average workweek, resulted in a 4.4 percent decrease in real average weekly earnings over this period."\par \par \uc2 Four point four percent average decrease in earnings. This is what economic disaster looks like.\par \par \uc2 Americans are making less money at exactly the moment when everything they buy from gas to groceries is more expensive and not just a little more expensive, a lot more expensive. Here's the big picture.\par \par \uc2 The average American household income this year is about $87,000.00. Today's inflation numbers means the average household is losing nearly $8,000.00 a year just from inflation. By the way, that's using the government's cooked numbers, the 9.1 percent inflation number, which is derived from the intentionally deceptive Consumer Price Index (CPI), so the real number is actually higher than that.\par \par \uc2 Rising inflation with falling wages. This is very bad, and as we said, it's also very weird. How weird? Well, here's one measure of the strangeness. The price of gas is now much cheaper in Mexico than it is in the United States, and that's why so many Californians are now driving across the border to fill their cars.\par \par \uc2 Now, why is this happening? That does not make sense. Oil price is set on the international market.\par \par \uc2 But apart from a few outlier websites like ZeroHedge, which not coincidentally the left is always trying to shut down and censor, no one seems to be asking that question.\par \par \uc2 We do know that gas prices in Mexico are so cheap that the Mexican government is encouraging more Americans to cross the border to refuel their cars.\par \par \uc2 "Right now," said the President of Mexico this week, "A gallon of regular cost $4.78 average on your side of the border, while in Mexico, it cost $3.12." So, you have to ask yourself, if we're paying more for gas because of Putin's price hike, why isn't Mexico paying more for gas because of Putin, too? Why is inflation up when wages are down?\par \par \uc2 This doesn't make any sense. So, if you want to answer those questions, you really have to look at government spending.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Mexico's government did not follow the Biden administration's lead in sending the Strategic Petroleum Reserve to China. They did not do that. Instead, here's what Mexico did. They spent $2 billion in subsidies to keep gas prices lower for consumers.\par \par \uc2 In other words, the government of Mexico in the middle of a drug war is taking better care of its citizens than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is taking care of his citizens and that is shameful, but it doesn't mean \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is ignoring the needy.\par \par \uc2 In the very same month, the gas prices shot beyond the reach of people, people aren't taking trips because of gas prices. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , in the name of democracy, signed a $40 billion aid package, not for you or any other American, but for Ukraine and that money, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says, is just the beginning. It's part of our unlimited commitment to funding Ukraine's corrupt and authoritarian government. Here's Biden.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: "For as long as it takes." Does it mean indefinite support from the United States for Ukraine or will there come a time when you have to say to President Zelenskyy that the United States cannot support his country any longer? Thank you.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (D), PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: We are going to support Ukraine as long as it takes. We are going to stick with Ukraine and all of the allies will stick with Ukraine as long as it takes.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: The war has pushed prices up. It could go as high as $200.00 a barrel, some analysts think. How long is it fair to expect American drivers and drivers around the world to pay that premium for this war?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: As long as it takes. Russia cannot, in fact, defeat Ukraine and move beyond Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Future generations will look at that tape and many tapes like it with their jaws open. "As long as it takes. Whatever the cost