istance; now, the head of \uc2 USAID\uc2 , that would be \uc2 Samantha Power\uc2  -- she's never left, she's still here, amazingly, after wrecking the world -- she has announced we're sending $4 billion more to Ukraine to pay off that country's budget deficit.\par \par \uc2 Wouldn't that be nice if \uc2 Samantha Power\uc2  decided to pay off our budget deficit, if anyone decided to help us? But no, no one would ever do that.\par \par \uc2 So, your tax dollars are now paying the salaries of Ukrainian government bureaucrats. In all, your Congress has approved more than $50 billion for Ukraine. That includes $7 billion in food assistance and healthcare (healthcare), along with $9 billion for economic support, whatever that means. There's also $2 billion for refugee assistance.\par \par \uc2 So, just as we did in Iraq and Afghanistan and I don't know, half a dozen other countries, we're sending bales of $100.00 bills into a war zone and hoping they find the right pockets.\par \par \uc2 Again, this is nuts. And yet leaders of both parties agree we have to keep doing it, much more of it.\par \par \uc2 Dozens of Democrats in Congress just signed a letter pushing the administration, as if they needed to be pushed, toward the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , a total of $650 billion in new funding because Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 And on top of all of that, Congressman \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  just proposed an amendment to the National Defense Authorization Act calling for another hundred million for, "Ukrainian military pilots and associated personnel." Kinzinger is the guy who thought the ghost of Kiev was real.\par \par \uc2 Now all of this is necessary. It's mandatory. We must, according to members of both parties, because we must defend democracy. Now we're not picking on Senator Kevin Cramer of North Dakota, a Republican State, but we want to show you this tape.\par \par \uc2 He just sat for an interview with Charlie Kirk and explained that we have to send an unlimited amount of money to Ukraine. Why? To "Fight back against communist intrusion for the cause of freedom because \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is evil." Watch.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE KIRK, FOUNDER, TURNING POINT U.S.A.: What amount of money is too much to send to Ukraine because we just did $1.7 billion more? Where is the line because we're up near $56 billion now?\par \par \uc2 SEN. KEVIN CRAMER (R-ND): Sure. Well, I don't know that the line is a dollar amount, Charlie. I think each request or each requirement, each demand, each circumstance requires its own discovery, if you will.\par \par \uc2 I don't think we should do a whole bunch necessarily at one time. I think that we should do smaller tranches just for the purpose of renegotiating, you know, reassessing.\par \par \uc2 The price of letting Ukraine fall to Russia, to the United States taxpayer and to the cause of liberty, I think is very, very high.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes. Fighting the communist menace. These people never update their talking points.\par \par \uc2 Senator Cramer invokes the cause of liberty and that's a phrase we strongly support. That's an idea we strongly support. That's why we're in favor of unfettered free speech. That's why we oppose vaccine mandates.\par \par \uc2 But you have to ask yourself, what does the cause of liberty have to do with Ukraine? Well, very little.\par \par \uc2 Last February, the Ukrainian government shut down opposition media. Then they arrested the leader of the main opposition party.\par \par \uc2 Now, President Zelenskyy has decided to combine all television stations in Ukraine into a state-owned propaganda ministry in order to combat "misinformation."\par \par \uc2 Now, what is that? Well, I'll tell you what, it's not. It's not the profile of a free country. Not even close. The cause of liberty. May those words burn in your mouth. "Oh, but we have to," they tell us," because Putin is worse. He's the worst person in the world." He's a communist, says Senator Cramer, who plans to conquer the globe.\par \par \uc2 You don't have to like \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  to see how absurd this is. Putin is a communist now. Really? How communist is \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 ? Is \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  more or less communist than, say, Sandy Cortez? More or less communist than say \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's domestic policy team? Is he more committed atheist than they are?\par \par \uc2 Is Putin throwing Americans in jail for attending political rallies at the Capitol? Is he trying to confiscate the rifles from your bedroom? Is he sterilizing children in the name of trans-liberation? Whatever his many faults, no, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is not doing any of that.\par \par \uc2 As for his apparently limitless international ambitions, ask yourself, is \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  recolonizing Africa right now? Is \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  trying to build military bases in the Caribbean and South America? No, he's not, but another country is. That would be China, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's patron.\par \par \uc2 Putin wants Crimea. He may succeed in getting it, but it is China that is on its way to controlling the world. Here's a graphic we saw today that illustrates the point.\par \par \uc2 These are the relative sizes of the players in the global economy. The numbers are from the \uc2 IMF\uc2 . As you can see, the world is completely dominated by the economic power of China and the United States. As of today, our two economies roughly equal in size, though thanks to COVID, China is quickly pulling ahead.\par \par \uc2 That is a problem. In fact, that is the biggest problem in the world by far. Nothing comes close because the Chinese Empire will not be like our empire at all.\par \par \uc2 So, where is Russia in this? How does it fit in? Well, get your reading glasses, because Russia is a footnote. It's not irrelevant, but it's close to irrelevant.\par \par \uc2 Russia's economy is smaller than Italy's. The Italians, in other words, are in a better position to take over the world than \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is.\par \par \uc2 This entire conversation is insane. Anyone who takes it seriously is a fool, and anyone who doesn't see the red flags is probably dishonest.\par \par \uc2 The most dishonest, the most power-hungry people in the United States are the very ones yelling the loudest for a war with Russia. That would be \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . That would be \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 . That would be \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 . That would be Adam Schiff.\par \par \uc2 These are the people telling you that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is a war criminal bent on world domination. Why are they saying that? Why are you suggesting \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's going to take over Europe? That's not true, but why are they saying it?\par \par \uc2 Well, there's a reason, a reason that has precisely nothing to do with saving lives or making Ukraine a better country. Again, red flag, anyone?\par \par \uc2 And yet somehow Republicans don't see it. They don't seem curious about why the worst people in America are for an endless war with Russia.\par \par \uc2 In fact, apart from \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  and a few other Republicans in Congress, they are all in. Whatever \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wants in Ukraine they support.\par \par \uc2 Here, for example, is \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  with his little friend Richard Blumenthal, that would be Connecticut's most famous Vietnam War hero. Here they are together.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. RICHARD BLUMENTHAL (D-CT): This picture ought to tell you something about America right now. There's bipartisan support to defeat Putin, to call him out as a pariah and a war criminal.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 LINDSEY GRAHAM\uc2  (R-SC): When we get back, we're going to try to get the Senate, as a whole, to pass the resolution, hopefully leading the way for the administration to label Russia as a state sponsor of terrorism in the category of Iran, Syria and North Korea.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Defeat Putin. Will that improve your life? Is it improving the lives of the Ukrainians right now? No, it's not.\par \par \uc2 And yet every person who has been on the wrong side of every foreign policy decision going back 40 years is on the same page and that, of course, would include \uc2 John Bolton\uc2 , the former national security adviser, who by the way just admitted on national television that he has personally engineered coups in foreign countries.\par \par \uc2 Wait, we're not for democracy? Apparently not. \uc2 John Bolton\uc2  isn't. But wasn't democracy the whole point? Were those coups state-sponsored terror? No one's asking. No one's calling \uc2 John Bolton\uc2  a war criminal. Instead, here's what they're saying.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JIM CRAMER\uc2 , CNBC NEW HOST: Biden studiously avoids doing the one thing, though, that could really bring down the price of crude. He needs to arm the Ukrainians to the teeth so they can quickly beat Russia and put the war to bed.\par \par \uc2 Can we make Ukraine safe for agriculture? Sure, but we might have to set up a no-fly zone in the western part of the country, which Biden doesn't want to do. He doesn't want to create a no-fly zone because that's American fighter planes firing at Russian ones and it's a hop, skip and a jump from there, nuclear war. I understand that.\par \par \uc2 By the way, I think there's a very good argument for that, but a no-fly zone is, while extremely risky, it is the best way to get food inflation under control.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Wait, what? I tuned in to find out whether I should buy \uc2 Cisco\uc2  on the dip and you're a foreign policy expert now? The American economy is in serious trouble. It's heading south faster than anyone anticipated.\par \par \uc2 But instead, you flip on CNBC and the geniuses are talking about World War III, and they're not the only ones.\par \par \uc2 So, if you want to know how big this has become, how ominous this is, in the absence of attention from the rest of us, we've kind of slept walked up to this point, you should see this.\par \par \uc2 This is from the City of New York, our largest city. This is a public service announcement reminding the eight million residents of New York they could soon be nuked.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: So, there's been a nuclear attack. Don't ask me how or why. Just know that the big one has hit. Okay, so what do we do?\par \par \uc2 Step one: Get inside fast. You, your friends, your family, get inside. Stay inside. Shut all doors and windows.\par \par \uc2 Have a basement? Head there. If you were outside after the blast, get clean immediately. Remove and bag all outer clothing to keep radioactive dust or ash away from your body.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: What? Now, if you were drinking beer and that came on TV, you'd think maybe she was giving you advice on what to do if your basement floods or if there was a heat wave. Then you get to the part where she says "radioactive dust" and you snap to it. Radioactive dust? You're suggesting that someone might lob a nuclear weapon into our largest city? What?\par \par \uc2 Why the chirpy tone? What the hell are you talking about?\par \par \uc2 How do we get so close to nuclear war that the city of New York is telling me to wash the radioactive dust off my pants? This is total lunacy. This is crazy. Why are we doing this? Because Putin's bad and he's going to take over Belgium?\par \par \uc2 Because nobody has said anything and because the Republican Party has collaborated with the nutcases in the Biden administration, we have reached the point where some chirpy lady on TV is telling you to prepare for the deaths of tens of millions of Americans. Wake up.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: To the polling, again in the good news column, looking pretty bad, pretty much across the board for old \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . But Biden has a response for the haters.\par \par \uc2 FOX's Trace Gallagher has a story for us tonight. Hey, Trace.\par \par \uc2 TRACE GALLAGHER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT: Hey, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 Whether it's accusing border agents of whipping Haitian migrants or calling White House correspondent stupid SOB, President Biden has a history of getting angry, agitated, and hopping over the facts to get to the politics.\par \par \uc2 This was at the White House congressional picnic when the President was asked about a majority of Democrats opposed to him running again. The soundbite is 22 seconds, but well worth the watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 QUESTION: Mr. President, what's your message to Democrats who don't want you to run again?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: They want me to run.\par \par \uc2 QUESTION: Two-thirds say they don't.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Read the polls. Read the polls, Jack. You guys are all the same. We've got poll that showed that 92 percent of Democrats if I run would vote for me.\par \par \uc2 QUESTION: A majority of Democrats say they don't want you to run again in 2024.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: No, 92 percent said if I did, they'd vote for me.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: Well, they are both talking about the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 /Siena College Poll, but the 92 percent number that the President cherry picked is only referring to Democratic support in a hypothetical rematch with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The reporter there was correct that overall 64 percent of Democrats think somebody else should run in 2024. And it gets worse, 94 percent of Democrats under the age of 30 want a different nominee altogether. And only 13 percent of Americans believe the country is on the right track, Jack -- Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Trace Gallagher for us. If someone is going to shoot your dog, if he didn't, would you vote for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ? Ninety-two percent say yes. It's so good.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for that.\par \par \uc2 GALLAGHER: You bet.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, you've probably heard a lot, if you watch TV, and we don't recommend that until 8:00 PM, but whatever. If you have you've heard a lot about a 10-year-old girl who was raped in Ohio and then supposedly had to flee to Indiana to seek an abortion.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has told that story a lot. Every other media outlet, of course, repeated it. It wasn't true in its details. We are learning the actual truth and it turns out the headline here is someone raped a 10-year-old.\par \par \uc2 The headline is not, "Oh, she couldn't have an abortion." Someone raped a 10-year-old and now, we know who did, and we'll tell you after the break.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: To \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , other human beings only exist to the extent they can be used for partisan ends, so it shouldn't surprise you that on Friday, he used the story of a 10-year-old rape victim to push for more abortion.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the laws in Ohio forced a 10-year-old rape victim to flee to Indiana to get that abortion, and the White House never vetted the facts of this story.\par \par \uc2 As the President of the United States, saying things that no one checked, but the facts didn't make any sense. On Monday, for example, the Attorney General of Ohio said there would not be a reason for this child to flee to Ohio in the first place. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DAVE YOST, ATTORNEY GENERAL OF OHIO: Ohio's heartbeat law has a medical emergency exception broader than just the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 This young girl if she exists, and if this horrible thing actually happened to her, it breaks my heart to think about it. She did not have to leave Ohio to find treatment.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So the obvious headline here was not about abortion. It