t at a time of great national peril.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, in 2022 under the democrat majority, we have arrived at that time of great national peril.\par \par \uc2 When the Supreme Court draft opinion overturning Roe leaked in May, we began to report on the increasing number of left-wing attacks on churches and other institutions across America.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: This past weekend, a pregnancy crisis center in Washington, DC's Capitol Hill neighborhood was vandalized with red paint, eggs and a message reading, 'Jane says revenge'.\par \par \uc2 In Amherst, New York, yesterday more acts of terror. CompassCare Pregnancy Services clinic had its windows broken, it was graffitied and set on fire.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And it hasn't stopped. In Washington state, a church had two glass doors broken with rocks, the wall spray painted and an employee who was assaulted. In Chippewa County, Wisconsin, four Catholic churches were hit with graffiti. In Kansas, a church was also vandalized with graffiti and red paint was dumped on the statue of Mary.\par \par \uc2 And over the weekend, this hit home, very close to home for me and other 'Angle' staffers as three churches were hit in Bethesda, Maryland. Now, one of them, St. Jane de Chantal, the catholic church I know very well because we attended mass there frequently when my children were really little.\par \par \uc2 Now in this security video, you can see the arsonist flames inside the church. Just hours later, forced to hold mass in an adjacent building due to the condition of the main church. Father Samuel Giese describe the damage that was done.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SAMUEL GIESE, THE PASTOR OF ST. JANE FRANCES DE CHANTAL: Last night, our church was vandalized. People broke in. They overturned statues. They tore down the stitches of the cross, they discredited the tabernacle and tried to set the church on fire. I believe that this is because of the church's stand on the issue of life.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yet the parishioners were encouraged to remain resolute.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GIESE: There are those who believe that we do not have given the right to practice our faith. However, and this is the important thing to remember. However, we are the church. We are the living stones. We are the body of Christ.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And over the past month, churches have been subjected to graffiti and religious statues have been defaced from New York to Louisiana.\par \par \uc2 In this exclusive video from New Orleans parish, masked goons came in the night, toppled this statue of the Virgin Mary and then stole it. They've come back to steal other statues since. The perpetrators have yet to be found or charged.\par \par \uc2 Of course, attacks on religious symbols, houses of worship, they're nothing new in world history. From the Bolsheviks to the Maoist, despotic movements have often felt compelled to extinguish all things religious, because remember to them the state is their religion. There can't be anything above the state, the worship of state power is where it's at.\par \par \uc2 And today, the American left has adopted the same tactics. They feel totally justified in waging a campaign of intimidation and harassment against anyone who believes in the sanctity of life.\par \par \uc2 And these domestic terrorists and, yes, they're domestic terrorists, believe they can do this with impunity. Well, we haven't heard anything from the Department of Justice on any of these attacks.\par \par \uc2 Even with the clear constitutional implications, there should be a federal investigation. This is a coordinated criminal enterprise. And they're conspiring to deprive thousands of Americans of their First Amendment right to free exercise a religion.\par \par \uc2 Now we know that Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , he has plenty of time to focus on his department's real priorities. He even had one of his minions launch an entirely new unit.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MERRICK GARLAND\uc2 , ATTORNEY GENERAL: The top domestic violent extremists threat comes from racially or ethnically motivated violent extremists, specifically those who advocated for the superiority of the white race.\par \par \uc2 MATTHEW OLSEN\uc2 , ASSISTANT ATTORNEY GENERAL FOR NATION SECURITY: We face an elevated threat from domestic violent extremists. I decided to establish a domestic terrorism unit to augment our existing approach.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. Where are they?\par \par \uc2 Imagine what Biden and his DOJ and the media would be doing. Instead of churches being set on fire, it was planned parenthood clinics. Imagine that.\par \par \uc2 Now MSNBC, CNN, they wouldn't be doing live coverage all day long. We'd be covering it at Fox as well rightly so. Now, interviewing terrified workers, they'd be demanding Republicans, denounce the violence, all of it.\par \par \uc2 Think about this just for a moment now. What kind of people would target the volunteers who work tirelessly to help women and their babies. At these crisis pregnancy centers, I've had a chance to go to a lot. These are amazing people. And what sort of monster rips down religious iconography and trashes the holiest places for Christian families.\par \par \uc2 Jane's revenge and shut down DC, they're two groups that have urged the targeting of Supreme Court justices. So where they live, where they worship, and even where they eat, where they go publicly with their families. They're even offering a bounty, you might have heard of this, of $250 for anyone who gives them the location of any of the Supreme Court Justices who voted to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 So look, let's just say what this is. This is not legitimate protest. This has become very dangerous. And the Biden administration is egging this on in two ways. First, by what they failed to do, not immediately launch a federal investigation into these crimes. And second, by what they do say.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PETE BUTTIGIEG, SECRETARY OF TRANSPORTATION: These protesters are upset because the right, an important right that the majority of Americans support was taken away. Not only the right to choose by the way, but this justice was part of the process of stripping away the right to privacy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That's a Rhodes scholar. Yes, that guy is being touted as a possible 2024 contender. God help us.\par \par \uc2 I guess he solved the whole air travel mess. He's already handled that since he has so much time in his hands to comment on issues totally outside the transportation department.\par \par \uc2 Did conservatives do this by the way to sitting Justices who voted for Roe back in 1973? Of course not. Because they had something called class and decorum. We've arrived at that very perilous moment in the United States. And contrary to what the Democrats and \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  are alleging, Trump supporters are not the problem.\par \par \uc2 January 6 was an outlier event and most everyone I know decried the law breaking that did occur. Conservatives are for the preservation of our institutions, of our history, and of democracy itself. Leftists, however, they want to tear it all down.\par \par \uc2 But we warned you this would happen during the summer of 2020 when Democrats refuse to condemn the radicals, who are exploiting the awful, horrible death of George Floyd. They were terrorizing American cities, they were ripping down statues, they were denuding our country of its history in the classic Marxist tradition.\par \par \uc2 The assaults on our religious centers, the depraved levels of violence in our cities, the targeting of Supreme Court Justices. It's all of a piece. I