d I want to stress, everything. Think about the weaponization of government we have seen from this Justice Department, both in a passive sense where they will prosecute people who directly violated statute and protest that Supreme Court Justices' home with the design on influencing its decision, at case, pending in front of the court. And then, of course, the active weaponization of government, like what they did with parents.\par \par \uc2 I mean, you think about this school board situation, understand what happened to moms, what happened to families. They first told kids, you can't go to school. They closed the schools. Then when they opened the schools, they said we're going to teach your kids CRT.\par \par \uc2 And then if as a concerned parent, you showed up at a school board meeting, they treat you as a domestic terrorist and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  investigates you. So much so that we've had multiple whistleblowers come forward and tell us about over two dozen cases where moms and dads have been investigated for that same scenario I just described.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Congressman, we - yes, we have a situation where there are attacks happening across the country against religious centers, against these crisis pregnancy centers. They have to be communicating on some type of, whether it's an encrypted platform, or instant message - some type of messaging platform to coordinate a lot of these attacks. This is being done.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department refuses to do anything about this despite announcing the big domestic terror task force. So what can you do now to urge action?\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Well, they're too busy going after parents, they are too busy setting up the disinformation governance board to actually do things that we would expect them to do and do things that are direct violation of the statute as the case with Supreme Court Justices.\par \par \uc2 So we can continue to highlight it, draw attention to it, ask questions, do the kinds of questions, get the facts out to the American people. But in the end, it's going to be up to the we the people on election day to change the makeup of Congress. And then in two years, change the makeup of the White House and reelect President Trump as our new president. So that's what has to happen.\par \par \uc2 But in the meantime, we're going to do everything we can to highlight just how political, just how wrong, just how much this Department of Justice attacks faith, attacks freedom and attacks the institution of the family. We're seeing it across the board. The left going after those three key institutions in our American culture.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, I'm a little surprised. And I'm not directing this at you. But I'm a little surprised that we haven't had more Republicans in the aftermath of these attacks. We just highlighted a few from the area over the weekend, but pretty bad.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Yes.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I'm surprised that Republicans like - aren't doing what Democrats do. In case, where they'd have press conference where they demand action. I mean, you speak out but where the Republicans?\par \par \uc2 JORDAN: Well, it plus - it add to the fact that this is not new. Remember, a year and a half ago, \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  said if you go to church, if you go to synagogue, we're going to come get you. Now we have an escalation in this evil intent. We see where they're going after crisis pregnancy centers, pro-life voters, and of course churches, as you point out. This is an escalation of something that started a long time ago.\par \par \uc2 But this is how the left operates. It's all about intimidation. It's all about silencing their opposition and their political opposition. It's not going to work. You're going to keep speaking out, and you were the first to speak out when this whole COVID stuff started happening and the lockdown started happening.\par \par \uc2 So we got to continue to do that. And I think more and more Americans are waking up to this. Laura, there is a reason nine out of 10 of our fellow citizens think the country is headed in the wrong direction. They think that because it is. And it's heading in the wrong direction because of the crazy policies where faith is attacked, families attacked, freedom is attacked, your first amendment rights, your Second Amendment rights.\par \par \uc2 And Americans have had it, and they are going to, in my judgment, show up in a big way on November 8, and say, enough is enough. We're putting Republicans back in charge. And then we better have the courage to do what we told him we were going to do and what they elected us to do.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. Congressman, thank you for being here tonight.\par \par \uc2 Now, it's not just that the left wants you to feel unsafe in your house of worship, but also in your cities and in your workplaces as well. And don't even think about defending yourself when you're attacked, because they will still come for you.\par \par \uc2 Now, case in point, Jose Alba, a 61-year-old Bodega worker in New York City was charged with murder after fatally stabbing a man who assaulted him. Now it started when a woman tried to buy food where Alba was working and her electronic benefits card didn't work. The video obtained by the New York Post shows what happened.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The card works. I swipe it everywhere.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: That's not my fault, the card is not working. It's not working now.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now the woman told police that Alba then reached over the counter and grabbed the chips out of her daughter's hand. It was then that she started warning Alba that her boyfriend was coming.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The boyfriend Austin Simon is seen on video towering over Alba, grabbing him by the neck, shoving him. And Alba then grabs a kitchen knife from behind 