e came out and he said he supports hardworking people, men and women. So I've got to give it to Mayor Adams for sticking up for the right person.\par \par \uc2 Alvin Bragg needs to do the same. He needs to understand that what he has done is a terrible mistake. And we're hoping that he's going to come to his senses and say - and to be quite honest with you, in speaking to him, he seems to want to hear what we have to say.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, I'm not holding my breath for you, Fernando. Yes, I'm not. OK. We'll see. But Fernando, Austin Simon's family told The New York Daily News that he didn't go into the Alba's bodega looking for trouble. So what's your reaction especially after seeing those videos? He didn't go in looking for trouble.\par \par \uc2 MATEO: Well, listen, if that's not trouble, I don't know what trouble is. To shove an old man almost to the ground, and to pick him up and move him over and start beating on him, that's (ph) unexcusable. I'm sorry.\par \par \uc2 Listen, the man was killed. But he basically deserved what he got, because of what he did. Stand your ground in Florida is a good thing and we hope that we can convince our legislators in New York to allow small business people to stand their ground and do what Jose Alba did, defend themselves and not get killed.\par \par \uc2 Jose Alba has a family. He's a family man. He goes to work every day to just pay his bills. He didn't deserve what was coming to him.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Fernando, thank you very much for joining us tonight. And we look forward to hearing what happens after your meeting.\par \par \uc2 And, remember, if you cannot watch us live, set a series record on your DVR so you don't miss us every weeknight at 10pm. But up next, the real reason the media are turning on Biden and why they shouldn't be celebrated for waking up so late to reality. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Call it the great American cover up, because we've been tellin