ans minds. As the cost of the Biden agenda costing voters more everywhere from the gas prompt to the grocery aisle. But despite 40-year high inflation, record gas prices, the president is convinced the economy is headed in the right direction. Really?\par \par \uc2 Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Now, look, I know times are tough, prices are too high, families are facing the cost of living crunch. But today's economic news confirms the fact that my economic plan is moving this country in a better direction.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JARRETT: In a better direction. Really?\par \par \uc2 And while energy costs continue to surge here at home, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is compromising U.S. energy security by appeasing adversaries abroad because we're continuing to learn more tonight about the Biden administration actually shipping oil from our U.S. reserves to a Hunter Biden-linked gas giant prompting increased scrutiny and demands for transparency from Republicans on Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 Joining us for reaction, former energy secretary and Texas governor, Rick Perry.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Secretary, great to see you as always.\par \par \uc2 You know, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has the reverse Midas touch. You know, if he touches gold, it turns to stone.\par \par \uc2 You know, his profligate spending, his war on energy, drove up prices of everything at the gas pumps, at the grocery stores. It will only grow worse, will it not, unless he reverses course and he ain't going to reverse course. So it's only going to get more dire for Americans.\par \par \uc2 RICK PERRY, FORMER ENERGY SECRETARY: Yeah, it's -- it's frankly very disheartening to watch an individual who is supposed to be trying to make America a better place to live, that he has such disregard for the average citizen out there. You know, I -- it's probably been decades since he pulled into a gas station and bought a gallon of gasoline. He doesn't understand what the average