tegic petroleum reserve it's there for a natural disaster or a national defense issue. It's not there to play economics with, and the idea that that you can -- it's not that much. I mean, we're talking a relatively small amount in the ground scheme of things from the standpoint of refining.\par \par \uc2 What he should be doing is sending the message to the country -- to the oil and gas industry, listen, we're not going to overregulate you. We're not going to overtax you. Send the message to the refining industry that we're going to do what we can to be able to use American energy.\par \par \uc2 If you care about the future, you've got to be for American fossil fuels.\par \par \uc2 JARRETT: Secretary Perry, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Coming up straight ahead, despite being cleared of all wrongdoing for the fake migrant whipping incident, Biden's CBP still wants to punish the Border Agents involved. \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  joins us to explain.\par \par \uc2 Plus, Andy Biggs, Sara Carter reacts.\par \par \uc2 Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 JARRETT: Now, tonight, another example of the media mob's hate hysteria and outright hoaxes, because remember last year when Border Agents were accused of whipping Haitian migrants down in Del Rio, Texas. Well, yet again, facts in reality got in the way of a far left narrative because \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's own CBP commissioner admitted today no agents were carrying whips and no migrants were attacked. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: OPR investigators determined that the agents involved in the Del Rio activity were not carrying whips. OPR found no evidence Border Control agents involved in this incident struck any person with their reins intentionally or otherwise.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JARRETT: But get this, despite the agents being cleared of wrongdoing that Biden DHS reportedly still wants some form of discipline for, you know, minor i