ant in New York City.\par \par \uc2 And it reportedly all started when these women found out that there would be a charge for extra dipping sauce. The co-owner of the eatery is quoted as saying his employees are now fearful for their lives.\par \par \uc2 So what is it going to take to stop incidents like this?\par \par \uc2 Let's ask former New York City police officer Joe Gamaldi.\par \par \uc2 Joe, it's -- I mean, it's -- I see these videos almost every single day just floating around on social media. You wonder if people do them in part to be in social media, but it's certainly out of hand, isn't it?\par \par \uc2 JOE GAMALDI, FORMER NYPD OFFICER: Yes, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 I mean, this incident is just a stark reminder of the culture of lawlessness that is gripping this country. I mean, take these three young ladies. And I hesitate to call them ladies, based on the behavior that we saw in that video, Charles.\par \par \uc2 But they're jumping all over the counters. They're assaulting employees, all because they had to pay $1.25 extra for sauce. Sorry, ladies, inflation impacts sauce prices too. But to make matters worse, we get the idiots in the background cheering them on and videoing.\par \par \uc2 But this is what happens when people know that they will not be held accountable for their actions, thanks to woke DAs like Alvin Bragg in Manhattan. These criminals know that they're going to get a P.R. bomb when they just pinkie promise to show up to court. Their charges are going to get dismissed, or they're not even going to have to show up to court on their court date.\par \par \uc2 I mean, it's a complete joke. And it just continues to perpetuate this lawlessness we're seeing. And you know what it really says? For the politicians that support this crap, they're telling victims, we don't give a damn about you. And they're telling businesses, we don't care if you can't keep your doors open. We don't care if your business needs to look like a military installation just to operate, because, in the end, it's the woke agenda over people. And it's disgusting.\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: Yes, the large businesses are picking up and leaving, and the small ones are struggling to stay afloat.\par \par \uc2 And, of course, this week in New York City, we're reminded in just how far this kind of stuff can go with the incident in a bodega that resulted in the death of a young man by a bodega worker, who most people feel from watching the video was defending himself.\par \par \uc2 I mean, so, something like that, could that be a clarion call? Could that jar the folks in charge who, for some reason, have bought into this idea that the direction they're going in is fair and right? And it actually puts us all in danger.\par \par \uc2 GAMALDI: Yes, I don't think that's going to wake them up at all.\par \par \uc2 I mean, Alvin Bragg is charging this bodega owner for defending himself from someone who was choking him. And he charged him with murder. The only thing that is going to wake these folks up is holding them accountable at the ballot box. Put their ass on the unemployment line. They did it out in San Francisco to \uc2 Chesa Boudin\uc2 . They're trying to do the same the George Gascon.\par \par \uc2 That is the only thing they respond to. And I'm telling you, Charles, the current path we are on is not sustainable. Violent crime is up 40 percent in New York. Seattle, murders are up 55 percent, Portland, 21 percent, in New Orleans 36 percent.\par \par \uc2 We are seeing crime and disorder everywhere. It's not sustainable if we want a civilized society.\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: But, at the end of the day, society itself is going to have to rise up. And I think they will.\par \par \uc2 Joe, thank you very much. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 GAMALDI: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 PAYNE: All right, folks, \uc2 Twitter\uc2  shares falling even further.\par \par \uc2 Is this is -- that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  deal really falling apart, Kelly?\par \par \uc2 KEL