y after COVID recovery, that there's no natural immunity, so to speak, which is - was false in October 2020 when we wrote the Great Barrington declaration, false today.\par \par \uc2 And they pushed vaccine mandate in a way that was guaranteed to breed distrust in large parts of the community. They've now caused people to start questioning other vaccines which are actually quite important for children, for instance. So I just - like the DPT vaccines or the MMR vaccines.\par \par \uc2 I just am shocked to hear Dr. Jha talking this way. They really should be apologizing to the American people for the panic mongering that they did, for ignoring science and for censoring dissident voices who argued vehemently against the policies that they follow that have created this distrust.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And what they did to our children. Dr. Bhattacharya, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 And up next, we just learned something stunning about who exactly was the recipient of Biden's strategic petroleum release and what it might have to do with his son, Hunter.\par \par \uc2 Plus, Victor Davis Hanson details how the Democrats have become the Marie Antoinette party. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We already know that President Biden sent 5 million barrels from the SPR to foreign countries, including to China. But since then, the news has only gotten more disturbing.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, we can report about exactly who inside China was a direct beneficiary. The Free Beacon is reporting that 950,000 of those barrels went to Unipec, a trading arm of the \uc2 China Petrochemical Corporation\uc2 . Now that company, commonly known as \uc2 Sinopec\uc2 , is wholly owned by the Chinese government. Meanwhile, of course CCP.\par \par \uc2 Now here now is Daniel Turner, founder of Power The Future. Daniel, I keep saying this is beyond disturbing. The words don't even capture this at this point. Tell us why this matters. There's also a Biden connection to \uc2 Sinopec\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DANIEL TURNER, FOUNDER OF POWER THE FUTURE: Yes. This is disturbing on multiple levels. To start with, the President told us he was releasing these reserves to lower the price of gas nationally. And then you find out that, he through Secretary Granholm, the Department of Energy, is selling them around on the world market and selling them to the Communist Chinese.\par \par \uc2 So, A, we're selling our strategic raw materials, our strategic reserves to the communist country who's our adversary. And then you find out one of the companies that was brokering this deal, one of our top investors is, of course, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 . So the son's - the President's reprobate crackhead son has invested in a company that is buying our strategic reserves, while we're paying more than $5 a gallon at the pump.\par \par \uc2 If we had an impeachment hearing about a phone call with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and President Zelenskyy, if this doesn't cause \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2  and it doesn't cause Adam Schiff to ask some questions and for Congress to do its job and wonder how this Biden crime family is profiting while the American people are suffering. I don't understand if there is a more offense that is more worthy of investigating for impeachment. Let's put it that way.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, where's the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  on this? Where's the \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 ' \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  on this?\par \par \uc2 I mean, yes. This is a massive story. And people ask if, the Biden administration or the Biden family is owned by China, because they're about to lift the tariffs too. We know that. I mean, I don't know what you say about this. I mean, if they're not owned by China, they're acting like they're owned by China.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: And the President also uses the Defense Authorization Act to using military powers to commandeer the purchase of wind and solar, that are also made in China. So thank goodness for the Free Beacon, Colin Anderson, who wrote the story, deserves a shout out because they broke a major story.\par \par \uc2 But I'm getting angry at this, Laura, for very personal reasons, because this president just last week questioned our patriotism. The press secretary said that, we were not upholding our American standards. We've been told that we're shills of \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , because we the big bad oil and gas company, aren't lowering prices. We were accused of price gouging, profiteering.\par \par \uc2 And then you find out his administration is selling oil on the world stage and potentially his own family is profiting from it. And that is beyond offensive. I would like to thank Senator Manchin and Senator Barrasso, who had the energy Natural Resources Committee.\par \par \uc2 I'd like to think they would hold Secretary Granholm, who's in charge of this as the Department of Energy Secretary, and ask her some really tough questions. We're paying $5 a gallon because of this administration's energy policies. And now his family is potentially profiting on the world market. It's unpatriotic, and it's shameful, and it's potentially criminal.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Meanwhile, he's beating up the mom and pop gas stations. I mean, this was the great part of this. I mean - by the way, I got to play this from the economic adviser at the White House \uc2 Brian Deese\uc2 . He insisted that the President is focused on lowering gas prices. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BRIAN DEESE\uc2 , DIRECTOR, NATIONAL ECONOMIC COUNCIL: We have to show action on behalf of the American people. And that's exactly what the President is doing. And every day he's focused on practical things that he can do. So the release of oil from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve sounds esoteric to people, but oil market analysts you've had on the show will say, it was single handedly responsible for keeping oil prices going higher.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: