decision came out. And the evolution of Biden and abortion in 1974, the year after Roe was decided he said, "when it comes to issues like abortion, I'm about as liberal as your grandmother. I don't like the Supreme Court decision on abortion. I think it went too far. I don't think a woman has the sole right to say, what should happen to her body."\par \par \uc2 Fast forward to 2006, he didn't even view abortion as a right, saying it was always a tragedy. But in 2008, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  's running mate, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  agree that Roe was a very good decision. So that is why he got the question in Madrid. Are you really the best messenger when it comes to Roe v. Wade, Kurt?\par \par \uc2 SCHLICHTER: Well, look, I think he's pretty terrible messenger for everything, not just abortion. Look, far being for me to say something good about \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  , but you got to assess your opponents objectively. I learned that in the army. \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  was a great politician, and he created the formulation safe, legal and rare. It's a formulation that even reached out to people who didn't believe in abortion, and said, look, it's not a good thing. We just want - we want to keep it safe. And we want to make it rare. And that was very successful.\par \par \uc2 Now you've got these lunatics shouting their abortion. Who does that? That's insane. That's crazy. It's always a tragedy. And they're embracing it. I think they're driving away normal people who really don't want to talk about the subject. They find kind of distasteful and very painful.\par \par \uc2 And, look, I don't want to stop my opponents from making mistakes. But it's \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  , so I guess I really don't have a choice.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: The one thing I'd like to say Kurt, Jason, we're just into this. Jason real quick, we're self-correcting country. Things have to get severely bad to understand how bad they are. When there's subtle, you can debate it. It's getting so bad. The Harris just did a poll seven of 10 people surveyed do not want him to run for president again. Do you believe as a country, not as a different parties, we're starting to see the forest through the trees?\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Yes, I do. I think truth surfaces. America tends to figure these things out. They're smart, they understand, they plow through the information themselves. And I - America always gets it right. We're the greatest nation on the face of the planet. And there's a reason why and we figure these things out.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: All right. Kurt final thought?\par \par \uc2 SCHLICHTER: Look, I'm an optimist about America. I served my country for 27 years in the military. I lived overseas, I saw other countries in comparison. We've got like - they say on those home improvement shows, America's got good bones. And I think we will be back and I think we're going to be back better than ever. We just got to get through two more years of this doddering, senile old weirdo, but we'll do it. We'll be back.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: OK. I'm going to take some something positive out of that. Thanks guys appreciate it. Have a great Fourth.\par \par \uc2 All right, I want to turn now to some breaking news. In New York, Democrats have just passed a massive restrictions on concealed carry in the wake of the Supreme Court's decision to expand gun rights and allow the Second Amendment to exist in places like New York. After passing both chambers in a special session today, Governor Hochul signed into law, moments ago, a measure banning concealed carry pretty much everywhere. Listen to this list.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. \uc2 KATHY HOCHUL\uc2  (D-NY): We are creating a definitive list of sensitive locations where individuals will not be able to carry firearms. Restaurants, bars, public transportation, subway, buses and in Times Square.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: All right, that's just the start. Now that list went 