ns six other cities. You can have a concealed carry permit. In a two page insert Justice Kavanaugh came out and said, listen, name some places to restrict to bring guns by courthouses, like schools, like Times Square, and then just name it. But they've simply gotten over the top. Don't you think this invites a another lawsuit?\par \par \uc2 ZELDIN: Yes, exactly. It's almost as if they saw what the Supreme Court did. And then they wanted to go even further than they went earlier. In a way, they just went even worse than what the Supreme Court just said was unconstitutional. So now they are inviting another lawsuit. And now you're wasting the judicial system's time, because it's going to have to go through that entire process. The Supreme Court is going to have to decide again, and it's showing a lack of respect for the rule of law and the lack of respect for the Constitution.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: $35 million - $35 million will be set aside to make sure New York is a welcome place for abortions. That was also put forward by the governor today. She brought that up, talking about different places to provide abortions for states that might be banning it for the most part. What's your reaction, we need $35 million to have more abortions.\par \par \uc2 ZELDIN: No, the reason why Governor Hochul is pushing this is because she doesn't want to talk about the issues that matter most to New Yorkers. This state is going in the wrong direction. She doesn't want to talk about crime and public safety. She doesn't want to talk about people struggling to afford to survive in New York, whether it's getting your own home, or it's the cost of gas and just the overall cost of living.\par \par \uc2 So she's trying to find some other way to activate her base because they don't really like her. New Yorkers have not had a very good first impression of Governor Hochul. There's a lack of excitement, enthusiasm. They don't think that she's doing a good job. So she's trying to put fear into p