d, he talked about standing on hallowed ground and about fighting for the ideals that these men had fought and died for in this country. But we don't value that anymore as far as the woke are concerned. They don't care what was fought for. They don't care about American ideals. So who cares if you get rid of a Lincoln statue. And one complaint is all it takes to make that happen.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: All right, listen, if we can't agree on Lincoln and the Gettysburg Address, I don't know where we go. But I remember President Trump pointed it out, you start pulling down these statues, you're going to come for Washington and Jefferson next. They answer is yes.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, let's move on. How "Sesame Street" is indoctrinating our kids. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: You're super-duper today, getting your COVID vaccine, Elmo.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Yes. There was a little pinch, but it was OK.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Elmo getting vaccinated if the best way to keep himself, our friends, neighbors, and everyone else healthy and enjoying the things they love.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: All right, it's time for the children's shows to have your parent -- to teach you how to get vaccinated to make sure your parents do it. Does this concern you?\par \par \uc2 EKPUNOBI: Absolutely it concerns me. I used to watch "Sesame Street" and get messages about families, about values, about friendship. Now they're giving you medical advice, which is sheerly pure propaganda. It's ridiculous. And I want everyone to remember that "Sesame Street" is government-funded, so that's probably where they're getting the money and being paid to put out a message that can be truly harmful to kids and their families.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: Amala, it's unbelievable, but I think if we pointed out then people will realize there might be an issue with it. I don't know how many times this needs to be said. We are over the vaccination. We're going to make our own decisions, especially when it comes to our toddlers as well as our teens. Amala, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 EKPUNOBI: Thanks for having me.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: All right, let's move ahead. And why not move ahead to this. Never before been done, has THE INGRAHAM ANGLE managed to mesh with FOX & FRIENDS. Can this crossover actually happen? I say yes. Why? Because Janice Dean is still up. She is here with details on her brand-new gig. I hope the outfit doesn't give it away. Stay here. That goes for you, too, Janice.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The Team that eats the most hot dogs in 10 minutes will be declared the winner. On your mark, get set, eat.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Is there any mustard?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: No mustard. No mustard. Just eat it. Eat it, Phyllis. Dip it in the water so it will slide down your gullet more easily.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: We have exciting news here for someone in our FOX family. Chief meteorologist -- yes, that's right -- Janice Dean is an official judge for the Nathan's famous hot dog eating contest happening this July 4th as it does every July 4th in Coney Island, New York. Here is the judge ow. Janice, how did you get this gig? I am so jealous.\par \par \uc2 JANICE DEAN, NATHAN'S HOT DOG EATING JUDGE: I still don't know. And what an honor. When I got that email, Brain, I said to my husband that they want me to be an official judge in Brooklyn on the Fourth of July to judge this historic hot dog eating contest. Joey Chestnut, of course, will be back. And his title is 76 hot dogs in 10 minutes. So I will be one of the esteemed judges that gets to count not only Joey Chestnut, but we also have a competition between the women as well. Miki Sudo is also the reining championship of 48 hot dogs two years ago. She was pregnant last year so couldn't compete. But what an honor. And not for the faint of heart, by the way, because one of the judges last year passed out, apparently.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: Listen, stay upright, promise me. Also, it's good to see a birthing person took a year off. So let me ask you this, Janice, what do you see your role being as a counter? Are you somebody who is going to be counting? Are you going to disqualify people? Are you going to give them red cards? Because you're wearing a referee outfit.\par \par \uc2 DEAN: There are red cards. You get a red card if you reject the hot dog. That's a polite way of saying it you don't throw up the hot dog. So you will be disqualified. I will disqualify you if you can't keep the dogs down. As well for messy eating, that is a yellow card. So if you're really message and you're spewing the hot dogs on the judges like me, you get a yellow card.\par \par \uc2 But I am just excited about it. My whole family is coming, my kids, my husband, my sister-in-law, my niece, my nephews. It is going to be crazy. This is an honor, Brian Kilmeade. Do we know anyone on FOX & FRIENDS that have ever had this kind of honor? I think you'll have to call me the judge after this.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: Wait a second, we went to our official. No, nobody has ever had this honor. I think that people have talked to Carly (ph) about it, but she has not been able to close it.\par \par \uc2 Last question for you, you only have 45 seconds to answer it. Is the hot dog a sandwich?\par \par \uc2 DEAN: Oh, my goodness, I don't know how to go there. That is going to require more than 45 seconds. The hot dog is not a sandwich, I have to say. What do I win?\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: Not a sandwich. I don't know if you're right. What do you mean if you win? I asked you a question. You can't say, you can't answer the question and declare you got it right and then demand a prize.\par \par \uc2 DEAN: I'm the judge. I judge myself.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: What time does it all start at Coney Island? What time does the event begin?\par \par \uc2 DEAN: I am going to be on FOX & FRIENDS starting at 5:00 a.m. onward, and then the actual competition starts at 10:00 a.m. and it ends at 1:00 p.m., 10 minutes for the boys, 10 minutes for the girls, and there will be a champion. And I will be an official judge.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: Janice, I've known you for a long time. I have never seen you this excited. And I am so happy for you and your family.\par \par \uc2 DEAN: It's amazing.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: They finally are happy about what you do for a living. I appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: Janice, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Final thoughts on what makes America great when we return.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: While you are celebrating your Independence Day and Independence Day weekend, I want you to do this. Log on to FOXnation.com or just download the app, check out my brand-new season, it is the ninth, of what made America great. I explore all the triumphant firsts that changed our country for the better. How we became a military superpower, like, for example, the aircraft carrier, how the history of Hollywood is pretty amazing, the creation of the automobile. Those are just some of the topics. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: This is the 1949 Ford , which was the first completely new design by \uc2 Ford Motor Company\uc2  following World War II production. And as you can see, the size of the vehicle itself has grown. They started to take in more consideration for storage. Where are you going to put your family when you're riding in these vehicles? And some say this was really the car that really saved \uc2 Ford Motor Company\uc2  , because at the time we are coming out of postwar production, we really needed something that was going to inspire people to drive a Ford .\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: And of course, you can go on vacation if you can put some luggage in the back.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes, exactly.\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: And the other thing I think is very patriotic and noteworthy is Ford shut down to help the war effort.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes, we completely stopped civilian vehicle production during the 40s so that we could invest all of our time and our labor efforts into producing things that would help aid in the war effort.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KILMEADE: Kind of cool. So download that app and watch. And also watch me Saturday night 8:00 and 11:00, "One Nation with Brian Kilmeade." Thanks.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020220702ei7100001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden Plays Blame Game As Failures Mount\b0\par\par\uc2 Tammy Bruce, Joe Concha, Rachel Campos-Duffy, Gregg Jarrett, Tom  Homan, Sara Carter \par \uc2 8,073 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 July 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 TAMMY BRUCE, FOX NEWS HOST: Hello, everyone, and welcome to this special edition of HANNITY. Happy Fourth of July weekend. It's an honor to be here with you. I'm Tammy Bruce, in tonight for, Sean.\par \par \uc2 And we begin with the conflict in Ukraine. The Biden administration is now using the war as a scapegoat for all of our economic problems here at home, while also pumping money into the region. As Americans struggle with record high gas prices and spiking inflation, the president is generously sending our tax dollars abroad to Ukraine, including a fresh new infusion of $820 million just this week, bringing the total commitment -- are you guys ready -- to $54 billion, which is about a third of Ukraine's entire GDP.\par \par \uc2 But according to one Biden advisor, we all must sacrifice so that the liberal world order is upheld. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The military analyst, the director of national intelligence, they say that this could be a long a war measured in years and I think everybody understands why this is happening. But is it sustainable? What do you say to those families who say, listen, we can't afford to pay $4.85 gallon for months if not years, this is just not sustainable?\par \par \uc2 BRIAN DEESE, DIRECTOR OF NATIONAL ECONOMIC COUNCIL: What you heard from the president today was a clear articulation of the stakes. This is about the future of the liberal world order, and we have to stand firm.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: So, just how long will you be expected to suffer in silence for the liberal world order? Well, according to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , as long as it takes. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: And how long is it expect -- fair to expect American drivers to continue to hit a premium because of this war?\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Let me get to the second part of the question, was would it bring down the price?\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: Will it bring down prices? And the war has pushed prices up, they could go as high as $200 a barrel, some analysts think. How long is it fair to expect American drivers and drivers around the world to pay that premium for this war?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: As long as it takes, so Russia cannot in fact defeat Ukraine and move beyond Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Extraordinary. For the record, gas prices and inflation were spiking long before \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  invaded Ukraine. And there is no mystery as to why.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  shut down the Keystone XL pipeline. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  restricted American oil and gas production. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  obstructed fracking. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ended exploration in Alaska and now breaking tonight with gas prices already at record highs, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is blocking new offshore drilling in the Atlantic Ocean and the Pacific Ocean.\par \par \uc2 Why would the president limit drilling at a time like this? Sadly, we won't soon get an answer to that question because Joe is headed for another long weekend off, away from the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here now with reaction is the author of the upcoming book "Come On, Man!", FOX News contributor Joe Concha, along with former Massachusetts Senator Scott Brown and "FOX and Friends Weekend" co-host, Rachel Campos-Duffy.\par \par \uc2 Scott, let me start with you because when I hear about the importance of keeping a gas high and oil high because we're fighting Putin through Ukraine, isn't it true that as long as the oil prices are high, Putin is getting even more money and this is funding his adventurism, that the way to stop him would be in fact to bring oil prices down, not to keep them high?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT BROWN (R), FORMER U.S. SENATOR FROM MASSACHUSETTS: Well, we know when oil was below $50, $40 a barrel and even less, that Russia was hurting. Yes, you're absolutely right. But you know, this liberal new world order, another clueless Biden representative -- newsflash, the world is not all liberal. There are certain parts of the world that are, but in the United States of America which is where, we are we need to focus on our needs and not other people's needs right now.\par \par \uc2 We're paying now a little less because it's Independence Day weekend, so that, you know, doing the manipulation. But I just paid $5.15 last week, came back a dollar $1.72 when I got back from being the ambassador in New Zealand.\par \par \uc2 And, Tammy, it's no secret here -- President Biden said that he was going to end fossil fuels in America. Well, I guess that's okay that he's doing a good job, but I guess he doesn't really care about the other parts of the world because he's going to Venezuela, obviously dealing with Iran, dealing with the Saudis, making their oil industries a booming industry. So he's creating jobs everywhere else but here.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 BROWN: A 38 percent approval rating, 85 percent of the people say we're going in the wrong direction, and he's got to get his act together. This administration is doomed and it's not doing anything right. Tell me one thing, please?\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Yeah, dooming all the rest of us with it.\par \par \uc2 Joe, the title of your book is perfect because it really -- it should be our explanation. It's like come on, man. You saw his performance there, embarrassing at \uc2 NATO\uc2 , noting, you know, the nature of as long as this takes, making a fool of himself but also harming our national security in the meantime. What's your take on what Biden's up to at this point?\par \par \uc2 JOE CONCHA, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Besides that, Tammy, everything went great, right?\par \par \uc2 Scott put up that stat before about 85 percent of voters don't like the direction of the country. I'd love to do some keg stands over the weekend with those 15 percent who thinks things are going in the right direction. Who are these people?\par \par \uc2 But seriously, you see now the press is turning on Mr. Biden, I keep reading. You know, that should have happened the minute he actually tried to sell the country on this notion that if you spend trillions upon trillions of additional dollars on top of the trillions we already have, and you flood the system, somehow he made this argument that that will lower inflation in the deficit.\par \par \uc2 And Brian Deese who somehow is the chief economic advisor to the president of the United States, he said the quiet part out loud right that this is all intentional. The attempted transitioning of this economy and energy policy to the new liberal world order, it sounds like something out of the -- you know, Star Wars Senate, I guess that's the plan.\par \par \uc2 Fortunately, Tammy, we have elections in this country and come November, as many Democratic strategists will tell you, voters are overwhelmingly going to reject this liberal world order and restore order to the political universe. So we have that going for us which is nice.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Well, we certainly hope so because you know the system seems to be effectively fine with what's going on.\par \par \uc2 Rachel, this is what I get concerned about is that there are people running the administration it's clearly not \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . And they think all of this is fine. They keep putting him in front. They keep arranging, you know, they whether it's like this kind of a press conference where he refused to really take many questions at all.\par \par \uc2 So, there's people within the establishment that are moving this along. Is that something we need to be concerned about post-November and the midterms?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL CAMPOS-DUFFY, "FOX AND FRIENDS WEEKEND" CO-HOST: Of course, there's three years left of this administration. So, yeah, we can put the brakes on it in the midterm, but believe me, there is a lot more damage that can be done. I do like that this guy slipped up and told the truth because remember, Tammy, we were called conspiracy theorists when we talked about you know the liberal world order or we said the great reset. We know it's true now.\par \par \uc2 They are totally willing to impoverish us and it's not just because they have, you know, an obsession with environmentalism and they want to transition us to fossil fuels -- out of fossil fuels and into, you know, energies that will make us more dependent on China, yes that's part of it. But it is bigger. It is a great reset.\par \par \uc2 They are trying to give us, you know, what \uc2 Charles Schwab\uc2  wants at Davos with the world Economic Forum, which is a Chinese system, a social credit score, a Chinese type of capitalism where the top has capitalism and wealth, the elites, the state and the rest of us live under socialism. This is a big, big deal, but we're starting to see the curtain open up and we're starting to see behind and we know what's going on.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Yeah, Scott, doesn't it matter as a result who gets elected in November, the statement, the volume of the statement that is made in the midterm elections. Is that -- in your time in Washington and as an ambassador, have you found that that's the thing that makes a difference when it comes to what politicians are willing to do like maybe finally listen to the American people?\par \par \uc2 BROWN: Yeah, listen, it's going to be a very serious warning shot especially leading into the presidency. Everyone's saying there's going to be this huge red wave, well, that's true if we don't screw it up like we tend to do and not unite behind the candidate who may not be your candidate, but it's a Republican who may be according to \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 , your 60, 70, 80 percent friend not your 100 percent friend, or a 100 percent enemy is as he would say.\par \par \uc2 But listen -- you find -- just getting back to something we said earlier about the press, you know, listen my wife is a former journalist and, you know, I have a lot of respect for the press. But you got to do your job, according to Bill Belichick. Just do your job, hold them accountable between the cue cards and the ushering in and out and the amazing handling of the president.\par \par \uc2 It is embarrassing. It's dangerous. It's affecting our national security and it's got to stop.\par \par \uc2 But when we look at the farm team behind it, we're going to go to Harris or Pelosi? No, we have some very serious issues and we need somebody strong to deal with them and we're not.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Yeah, look, Joe, and this is your bailiwick in a sense with the media, isn't him have -- Biden having a list of people that he goes to, doesn't that tell us that the media is colluding effectively with the Biden administration in, you know, making sure they know if certain someone is picked on and chosen for a question that it's either going to be easy or there's not going to be a hard follow-up or that person can be trusted? Isn't that part of the problem here with the especially with the White House press corps?\par \par \uc2 They complain about access but my goodness, haven't they been facilitating this debacle?\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: Yeah. It's funny when you mention access, Tammy, that the guy who was president before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was probably the most successful president that that we've ever had, right? He took more questions than probably his three predecessors combined sometimes, sometimes press conference is going on for two and a half hours and yet the press complained that you know he was trying to destroy the free press.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Right.\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: Well, I'm pretty sure, compared to what we're seeing now with this president who from day one has had that list, and then is smart enough to share -- oh, by the way, they gave me a list of reporters that I have to call on, again saying the quiet part out loud.\par \par \uc2 But it's not just \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Scott touched on it just a second ago as far as the farm team. Try get a -- try getting a flight somewhere this weekend without it being canceled or greatly postponed or costing you a fortune because we have a transportation secretary in \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  who's supposed to be maybe the plan B who has no business being in this position as transportation secretary, who doesn't have a clue how to fix the problem despite his, you know, vast experience as the mayor of a small town in Indiana, Tammy.\par \par \uc2 So, yeah, that's the whole team in general. It's not just Biden. It's all the adults that are supposed to be back in the room, and it's amateur hour.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Let me tell you, the two people that represent the Democrat party, the Democrat base really are Kirsten Sinema and Joe Manchin. So this is -- that is the answer for them. But my goodness, the condition they're in now is quite a disaster.\par \par \uc2 Joe, Rachel, Scott, thank you so much for joining me tonight.\par \par \uc2 Now, the Fourth of July is just three days away, but according to a brand new FOX News poll, pride in America is now plummeting under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Gee, I wonder why.\par \par \uc2 Just 39 percent of voters are proud of the country, including just 46 percent of Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now with reaction is the first Green Beret to be elected to Congress, Representative Michael Waltz.\par \par \uc2 Michael, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 You know, people can look at a poll like that and think like that we do -- we don't like the country. It's not that, we -- because we love the country. We don't like what's happening to it and how we're being represented. Is that your take on this?\par \par \uc2 REP. MICHAEL WALTZ (R-FL): Yeah, Tammy, I think that's part of it but I think there's something more fundamental here because if you look at the polling data, you see a steady decline over the last decade plus, and I point to our education system and COVID exposed to us the garbage that's being taught in our schools.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Great point.\par \par \uc2 WALTZ: And we have things being taught in our schools that this is a fundamentally bad country, that at its core it is misogynist, it's racist, it's colonialist, it wasn't founded to establish individual freedom for we, the people, away from monarchies and emperors, that it actually was established to protect slavery, when that's being taught in our schools and then on top of that, you have things even in like math class which we discovered in Florida, word problems in math class that talk about counting the numbers of oppressors and oppressed and now in our military. They're sending -- you know, they're saying on the one hand you need to be willing to go die for our Constitution and our flag, but it is fundamentally on its core bad and flawed.\par \par \uc2 I think you take all of that together, and when you talk about a military as this president has and the secretary of defense has that's overrun with white supremacy, it doesn't surprise me you're seeing this kind of decline -- in pride in our institutions and pride in our flag.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Yeah, and you know, I think that there is a combination of things going on. I think it's that. That's an excellent point, that we have young people especially being indoctrinated with loathing the country and they don't know because history's not taught anymore, right? They don't have much of a background.\par \par \uc2 WALTZ: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: But I do think that we know that a good majority of Americans know that what you described is a result of policy. It's -- this is not -- this is not a natural organic thing that's going on, that this is a group of people running the country that have done this to us.\par \par \uc2 Is there -- on this Fourth of July, you know, there's even you know this sense that the Fourth of July might become a partisan holiday -- do you envision that happening?\par \par \uc2 WALTZ: You know, I pray not and I'm going to do everything I can to fight and remind people that this flag that stands for individual liberty, the right to assemble, the right to free speech, the right to criticize your own government, and that there are literally more people out right now, more military members out right now willing to die for that flag --\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: That's right.\par \par \uc2 WALTZ: -- than the entire Canadian and Australian armies combined.\par \par \uc2 But, you know, Tammy, you know who does appreciate this country and is literally dying to get here -- those are immigrants like the Afghans that were so desperate to come to this great nation, they were willing to cling to the side of a jet.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 WALTZ: Or the people dying coming across our southern border.\par \par \uc2 But to your point, it's all self-inflicted wounds, and if you look at where we were the month before the pandemic hit, with record unemployment across every ethnic sector, black, white and brown, women and men, with a roaring economy, with justice reform, tax reform, Middle East peace -- if you look at where we were under the previous administration and people looked at the results in their lives, they were pretty excited.\par \par \uc2 And now, they look at everyday problems and they're only compounding it -- right.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Yeah, I mean, this is it And we have to remember. I think that the debacle of Afghanistan is what kind of shook the nation to its core, really.\par \par \uc2 WALTZ: And when we understood that this something very wrong had happened and we are seeing that kind of failure move through every single other issue that we face in this country, that that was not an accident. That was not a bug. It was a feature of what we are to expect.\par \par \uc2 Congressman, great job. Thank you so much. I appreciate it. Have a very good Independence weekend.\par \par \uc2 Now, let's turn to the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 , where a series of important rulings have Democrats very upset. Let's just say \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was at a loss for words. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Can you see us? Can you hear us?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Hey, everyone. Thanks for doing this. Thanks.\par \par \uc2 Leave it to you -- I open it up. Okay.\par \par \uc2 I know you're all busy as I am. Thank you for making the time because I need not tell any of you we're in a really -- an important area here and we have to act.\par \par \uc2 And politicians invading the most personal decisions that -- not only women but you find if they expand on this decision, men as well.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Yeah, I'm not totally sure what Biden is trying to say. But his fellow Democrats and the media mob have been hysterical all week long. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. JAMIE RASKIN (D-MD): The court is utterly fraudulent and the only thing that can explain their decisions is what is right-wing Republican dogma.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: The one thing that has been destabilizing is the outrageous behavior of the \uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2  on overruling not only Roe v. Wade but essentially challenging the right to privacy.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIANE AMANPOUR, CNN CHIEF INTERNATIONAL ANCHOR: Never in the history of women's rights in America have we seen such a reversal in a developed country. It just hasn't happened. And the rest of the world is watching this very, very closely.\par \par \uc2 SEN. ELIZABETH WARREN (D-MA): This court has lost legitimacy. They have burned whatever legitimacy they may still have had after their gun decision, after their voting decision, after their union decision. They just took the last of it and set a torch to it with the Roe versus Wade opinion.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Oh dear. So much for respecting America's institutions.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now is the author of "The Price of Principle: Why Integrity is Worth the Consequences", Harvard Law professor \uc2 Alan Dershowitz\uc2 , along with FOX News legal analyst Greg Jarrett.\par \par \uc2 Gregg, let me start with you here. When we hear about, you know, my background has been uh with women's rights and even abortion rights for a period of time. The fact that the Supreme Court effectively returned democracy to the American people so that they could vote on these things, removing it out of that category of a court of lawyers making decisions about these things, how is it that they're arguing that this is a strike against democracy when the court was pretty much removing it from their jurisdiction to the jurisdiction of the voters themselves?\par \par \uc2 GREGG JARRETT, FOX NEWS LEGAL ANALYST: Well, the Supreme Court represents the sanity and common sense world order, if you will. And you know, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  whenever he weighs in on the Constitution or the Supreme Court or the rule of law, he mangles the subject matter which only underscores that this is a guy who got kicked out of law school. I mean, the sum total what Biden knows about the law could be written on a yellow Post-It, and I'm talking about the little one.\par \par \uc2 You know, his latest thing is let's federalize abortion rights. That's a fool's errand for two reasons from a legal standpoint. Remember what the Supreme Court said, they said, we are returning the decision-making to the states. So if Congress were trying to codify it, it would immediately be met with a lawsuit, to strike it down, usurping the power of the states.\par \par \uc2 But from a practical standpoint, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wants to create this chronic state of whiplash. Every time a new party takes over Congress and the White House, they would reverse the previous decision on abortion.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Right.\par \par \uc2 JARRETT: So you'd have this right persistent ping-pong effect. Look, abortion is important. It shouldn't be treated like a rubber band, expanded and contracted.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Yeah, yeah. You know, thank you, Gregg.\par \par \uc2 And I -- Professor Dershowitz, regardless of what we think of the decision, the fact that the president of the United States on foreign soil is complaining about the Supreme Court, do you find that troubling?\par \par \uc2 ALAN DERSHOWITZ\uc2 , HARVARD LAW PROFESSOR: I do, and I find the whole attack on the Supreme Court's integrity and the Supreme Court's justification to be very troubling. You know, I've been studying the Constitution and the Supreme Court now for 60 years. I've seen it go through cycles. The pendulum swings widely.\par \par \uc2 I remember when the Birch Society had signs up, impeach Earl Warren, impeach Bill Douglas, when the right was very upset at the left swing of the Supreme Court. Now, the left is concerned about the right swing of the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 We have to respect the institution. We have to remember that these justices stand for the rule of law. We may criticize particular decisions, that's fine. But when my former colleague Liz Warren who I sat next to for years and taught the same section of, trashes the Supreme Court as an institution, that's going to do tremendous damage to this country and it's going to come back to hurt her and her liberals because today, the attack comes from the left, tomorrow, it might come from the right.\par \par \uc2 We -- those of us who love the rule of law, a rule that we celebrate on July 4th, have to stand by our institutions as institutions. Yes, criticize a particular decision, try to do better next time. Yes, think about whether you can do legislation. But don't trash the court as an institution. Don't do it.\par \par \uc2 My other former colleague Laurence Tribe now says, pack the court, let the Democrats add four, then the Republicans will add four.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DERSHOWITZ: Soon, the Supreme Court will sit in Yankee Stadium with 30,000 justices deciding these cases.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 DERSHOWITZ: No, nine is the right number. Let's keep the Supreme Court as it is. Don't tinker with justice.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Gregg, isn't the answer to have I don't know who's why the left suddenly wanted these unelected lawyers to be making all of our decisions, that -- isn't the answer to have Congress be involved, to have the state houses be involved? Isn't this the normal order? It's almost as though they're making a reversal out of this effort to protect politicians from having to make decisions on these issues.\par \par \uc2 JARRETT: And that was the point of yesterday's Supreme Court decision on the \uc2 EPA\uc2 . The Supreme Court was saying essentially, read the darn law. I mean, nowhere in the Clean Air Act section 111 does it give the \uc2 EPA\uc2  this unbridled power to remake an entire industry with punitive draconian measures against coal-fired plants and natural gas plants.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JARRETT: You know, the Supreme Court is saying, read the Constitution, read the statutory law, don't read things into them.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Right.\par \par \uc2 JARRETT: But limit yourself to what the law says.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: And that they're not going to do -- they're not going to make legislation. They're -- that's the job of legislators.\par \par \uc2 DERSHOWITZ: Return to the public. Win elections, win elections.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 DERSHOWITZ: I'm a liberal Democrat. I want to see us win more elections. I want to see you guys lose in the state legislatures, but --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: I have to go. Thank you, gentlemen. I appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 DERSHOWITZ: I want to vote Democrat.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: All right, all right. Coming up, Biden's border crisis is about to get much worse. Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  explains, plus, the open borders left is calling for even less border security. 