ature of the -- the soul-crushing horror that these people are put through, as we see in every Democrat city and clearly now here also at the border, what do you think has been key when it comes to what the Democrats have done as this is an unforced error reversing everything President Trump did which saved lives across the board?\par \par \uc2 REP. ANDY BIGGS (R-AZ): Well, they've been obsessed with through unpacking what President Trump did and President Trump's policies were so successful. And so, that's why you get Democrats right now who are saying, hey, wait a second, I'm going to be held accountable for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's bad policies and I don't want to be held accountable.\par \par \uc2 And so, I would urge those people like Representative Cuellar, just come to the floor of the House. I actually have a bill that would keep title -- MPP in place, remain in Mexico in place. Chip Roy's got one that would be Title 42. We're trying to take it out of the speaker's drawer, she's got it hidden there.\par \par \uc2 If he would come over with four, five, six other Democrats who don't like these policies, we could actually revert back to the policies that were working so well under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . That's -- so don't just talk the talk. Walk the walk with us, Rep. Cuellar.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: You know, I mean, because there are things it seems like there's nothing they can do. But in fact, it is a pretty close split. You can just bring a few people over who care. If they really care about the lives of migrants, shouldn't they do exactly what you've suggested? That is exactly what needs to happen here.\par \par \uc2 Gentlemen, thank you very much for being here with me tonight. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Now straight ahead, the left's COVID lunacy continues, but Senator \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2  is pushing back. She joins us next to outline her latest legislation protecting unvaccinated National Guard members. Stay right there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Now, today, President Biden announced he's awarding the Presidential Medal of Freedom, our nation's highest honor, a civilian honor, to the New York City nurse who was the first person in the nation to receive the COVID-19 vaccine back in December of 2020. But meanwhile, fully vaccinated and twice boosted tiny tyrant, Dr. \uc2 Tony Fauci\uc2 , is revealing a so-called COVID rebound, saying he was infected and then recovered and but then tested positive again and is apparently feeling worse than ever.\par \par \uc2 And now, that the shot has been approved for kids age zero to five, even they aren't immune from the left pressure tactics to get the jab. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHARACTER: Now, daddy has super duper bandages just like Elmo.\par \par \uc2 CHARACTER: You were super duper today, getting your COVID vaccine, Elmo.\par \par \uc2 CHARACTER: There was a little pinch, but it was okay.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Oh, boy, and while the Supreme Court back in January blocked Biden's vaccine mandate for private employers, there's still a mandate in place for federal employees, including for the military and the national guard. Now, a guard spokesman tells us that guard troops who have not gotten the shot yet face -- who've not gotten the shot yet face penalties including separation.\par \par \uc2 So while the fate of those troops hangs in the balance, Republicans in Congress are moving to protect them. Thank goodness.\par \par \uc2 The leader of that effort is Tennessee Republican Senator \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2 , who joins me right now.\par \par \uc2 Well, thank goodness for you on so many different fronts. Americans perhaps -- we know we feel that, you know, we're moving on with our lives. We've got some lifting of certain mandates like mass mandates, et cetera, and yet there's this hanging on and at its time, Senator, when the world is effectively kind of slouching into war, we are now still looking at separating or punishing some of our troops or not getting the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 What will your legislation do to stop that?\par \par \uc2 SEN. MARSHA BLACKBURN (R-TN): Tammy, my legislation would prohibit any taxpayer funds from being used to enforce this mandate. This mandate is about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  trying to take control over your lives. He wants a forever pandemic and it is absurd that he would fire members of the National Guard. And thank goodness our governor in Tennessee, Governor Bill Lee, has granted the exemptions for religious and medical reasons to 800 of our members of the guard that have been affected by those exemptions.\par \par \uc2 But they have to wait on the National Guard bureau to make their decision and, of course, they -- here's the deal. The Guard Bureau, the Department of Defense, DOD, they've got a choice in front of them -- they can fulfill their mission, which is to protect and defend.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Right.\par \par \uc2 BLACKBURN: They can choose freedom or they can go totally woke like they have been doing. They have spent 5,889,000 military man hours on initiatives like climate, diversity, equity, inclusion -- this woke agenda. So they can stand for freedom and fulfill their mission or they can do \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's bidding.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: You know, this is shocking because we're now dealing with a crisis of legitimacy of the government as Americans are looking funny at institutions as they remain under attack, that they don't seem to be doing their job. We see the military as you've noted go woke.\par \par \uc2 And then we've got, you know, the attitudes, the chaos that has been brought to our country. We have these -- this new poll of Americans not being proud of the country anymore and we we're sending more troops to Europe. We're dealing with Ukraine, et cetera. North Korea's not settled down, China is you know looking to eat us for lunch.\par \par \uc2 And, you know, it's hard enough to get people to join our volunteer military but to cut tens of thousands of those who've chosen to serve almost seems like a deliberate effort to undermine us. Am I going too far with that?\par \par \uc2 BLACKBURN: No, you are not going too far for that, and I had a Tennessean ask me about this very thing the other day when I was in one of our counties and, Tammy, they say, you know, if I didn't know better, I would think that this is intentional.\par \par \uc2 When you look at the border policy, when you look at what is happening with fentanyl that is ravaging families and taking precious young lives in our country, when you look how it appears that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is doing his best to lose the next war, you look at Afghanistan, you look at Ukraine, you look at what we're facing with the Chinese communist party, you look at what he has done to the U.S. energy sector, when you have our G7 partners, when you have our \uc2 NATO\uc2  allies asking us to help them with energy and he wants to go meet with the Saudis, and not meet with the U.S. oil companies, and he could find a solution to this.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: It is -- it is remarkable, even -- you know, as they say, even a broken clock is right twice a day. So you have to really work hard to not be right at any point.\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much for joining me today. I appreciate it. Thanks for your work.\par \par \uc2 BLACKBURN: You bet.\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: Coming up is a possible food shortage on the way? Signs indicate it may be coming. Our own Sara Carter joins us with a full report when we return.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: All righty. Welcome back to the special edition of HANNITY.\par \par \uc2 Now, amid Biden's surging inflation, new reports indicate that this year's 4th of July cookouts could cost nearly 20 percent more than last year. Is a nationwide food shortage looming? Some say it's inevitable.\par \par \uc2 Our own Sara Carter spoke with the National Black Farmers Association president \uc2 John Boyd Jr\uc2 . Here is what he had to say.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SARA CARTER, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: The American farmer, you, you are suffering right now under the current economy. Can you talk a little bit about it?\par \par \uc2 JOHN BOYD JR\uc2 ., PRESIDENT OF THE NATIONAL BLACK FARMER'S ASSOCIATION: Oh, yes, I can. You know, inflation rate now has really hurt myself and other farmers around this country. And it's not being talked about enough from the high cost of diesel fuel, the high cost of fertilizer.\par \par \uc2 CARTER: And that just trickles down to the consumer, right?\par \par \uc2 BOYD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CARTER: The farmer is the consumer.\par \par \uc2 BOYD: The American people will pay the price for what is going on right now. Being ignored in the farm crisis, because this is a crisis.\par \par \uc2 So, the three things that the American farmer can still do better than anybody in the world is produce corn, wheat and soybeans. When you don't support them, you are taking away the base and freedom to farm in this country.\par \par \uc2 CARTER: That's at risk. Who is not supporting them?\par \par \uc2 BOYD: Well, right now, it's the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 CARTER: If you had a moment to speak to President Biden directly, what would you say to them?\par \par \uc2 BOYD: I would say, you've got, you've got to take care of the American farmer in this country. That's rural America. You cannot turn your back on rural America.\par \par \uc2 If you want the country to survive take care of the American farmer. You see the stuff we are sitting on? This is called land.\par \par \uc2 Land knows no color. Land knows no party. Land produces food. And when you take away that ability for the American farmer to produce food, it's about as low as you can go.\par \par \uc2 Take care of the American farmer and the country will take care of itself.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BRUCE: