, their private island out there in the Bahamas, they are sold out. So for people who want that quintessential, not just cruise experience, but \uc2 Disney\uc2  experience, certainly, this bodes quite well.\par \par \uc2 And when you look at the other cruise lines, the fact of the matter is, they're anticipating for the most part ending Q2 with load factors between about 60 and 80 percent. And maybe by the end of this year, we will be at 100 percent load factors in some of these bigger ships setting sail.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Wow.\par \par \uc2 SAGLIE: So, we're starting to see some positive signs in the cruise industry as we head toward the end of this year and into 2023.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, look forward to it,my friend. Great job, \uc2 Gabe Saglie\uc2 , right now, the Travelzoo senior editor on that ship.\par \par \uc2 Can you imagine the first reaction if you're a character, let's say, there And better than $5,000 -- $5,000!\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Just a bad Mickey Mouse thing. I digress.\par \par \uc2 Let's get the read on what's happening for people who maybe can't afford a $5,000 drink, but they do got a bunch of pennies, and try to make sure that, at least if they're going to enjoy the big -- the big Independence Day cookout, they don't go too far.\par \par \uc2 Heather Wheeler is here. They call her The Krazy Coupon Lady. She's the co- CEO. So she called herself that, so I'm not disparaging her.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Heather, you have been very helpful to viewers and a lot of your followers over these years trying to help them navigate these high prices, but almost everything's here. So what do you do?\par \par \uc2 HEATHER WHEELER, THE KRAZY COUPON LADY: Yes, the deals are a little sparse this year on the barbecue items that we typically see on sale for the Fourth of July.\par \par \uc2 So the biggest things that will save you a lot of money is to find cheaper cuts of meat than you might normally do. Skip the filet mignon. Instead, go for ground beef. And instead of buying the prepackaged patties, buy a big chunk of ground beef and make the patties yourself. That's going to save you significant money.\par \par \uc2 And consider instead of -- if you're hosting, instead of providing everything for your guests, consider a potluck, so that everyone can kind of pitch in. And then I say, go down to basics. Skip the decor, and do lots of side dishes, so that people can get full on the side dishes with vegetables and fruits that might be a little bit less expensive than those cuts of meat that are going to tend to run you a little bit higher.\par \par \uc2 And then you have got to stock up on the things that are really cheap this time of year. So, soda, this is one of the best times of year to buy 12 packs of soda.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Really? Huh.\par \par \uc2 WHEELER: We're seeing them under $2 at several stores.\par \par \uc2 Chips and popsicles are also some of the cheapest prices that you're going to see all year. So, even stock up a little bit and get you by for the next couple of weeks.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Now, the one thing that infuriates me, Heather, and I'm sure it does you, is that Italian sausage prices have doubled in the last year.\par \par \uc2 WHEELER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: And you cannot tell me to look for a cheaper alternative or to make the sausage really tiny. But what's going on there?\par \par \uc2 WHEELER: Yes, I mean, meat prices across the board.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WHEELER: So what you need to do is, instead of running to the store the day before you need your sausage, look for prices across different stores than maybe you're used to going to.\par \par \uc2 Look at a few different circulars and see if something's on sale. And then download the store app and download the \uc2 Ibotta\uc2  app. And always look at those right before you head into the store just to make sure there's not a coupon that you're not missing out on.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Now, there's a lot of shrinkflation going on for folks.\par \par \uc2 But I was thinking when you were mentioning about get your own ground beef and make the patties yourself, you can shrink that for your guests, right, instead, make a really tiny little hamburger, and they will be none the wiser, right?\par \par \uc2 WHEELER: Yes, you could go smaller. And that's if you have lots of side dishes and then maybe the burgers are a little bit smaller.\par \par \uc2 That's a -- that really does add up. That's a significant savings right there.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: What is just verboten these days, it's just too crazy?\par \par \uc2 Steak, I imagine. You mentioned that. That's not an option. I...\par \par \uc2 WHEELER: That's the biggest one. And those...\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: I perish the thought that people are going vegetarian. What's happening on that front?\par \par \uc2 WHEELER: No, no, no, I don't think people are going vegetarian.\par \par \uc2 But you really do need to look at those cuts of meat and make decisions.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Got it.\par \par \uc2 WHEELER: And so those, like -- and even, like, chicken breasts, that's really expensive right now, so maybe go for chicken legs or chicken thighs instead.\par \par \uc2 Anything that's bone in is going to be a little bit cheaper than if there's no bone. So that's another thing to look at as well.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Heather, you know your stuff. You know your stuff.\par \par \uc2 WHEELER: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Heather Wheeler, The Krazy Coupon Lady, the co-CEO.\par \par \uc2 She's been ahead of this trend. In fact, the shrinkflation, when I was going -- she was doing that years ago. Now everyone's saying, what is going on with shrinkflation?\par \par \uc2 So you have got the basics on how you're going to plan for the big day. We have got you covered tomorrow beginning at 10:00 a.m. Eastern time other ways you can save.\par \par \uc2 Now, a lot of you have been frantic, as I have, about this whole problem going on with Italian sausage. We're going to try to resolve that tomorrow by seeing if we can steal it from some people. But, barring that, we will keep you abreast of the latest developments here.\par \par \uc2 See, chicken breast and all?\par \par \uc2 Anyway, tomorrow, we will see you then.\par \par \uc2 Here's "The Five."\par \par \uc2 THIS IS A RUSH TRANSCRIPT. THIS COPY MAY NOT BE IN ITS FINAL FORM AND MAY BE UPDATED.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document CAVU000020220701ei710005l\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Interview With Sen. \uc2 Charles Grassley\uc2  (R-IA)\b0\par\par\uc2 Neil Cavuto \par \uc2 1,828 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 July 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Your World w/ Neil Cavuto\par \uc2 CAVU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 NEIL CAVUTO, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: In the meantime, I do want to bring in Senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2 , the Republican senator from the beautiful state of Iowa, get his thoughts on all of this.\par \par \uc2 Senator, as you know, almost two weeks ago, the president had a plan. Maybe take a federal gas tax holiday for about three months. That`s about 18.4 cents a gallon. He has urged states, California certainly among them, that have some of the highest state gas taxes, if it were to nix that, I mean, that would be more than $1 a gallon that folks would save.\par \par \uc2 Do you support either, both measures?\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHARLES GRASSLEY\uc2  (R-IA): No, I do not.\par \par \uc2 And I`m glad that Speaker Pelosi said she hasn`t supported it. And, consequently, since tax bills have to start in the House of Representatives, I doubt if it will ever come before a vote in the \uc2 United States Congress\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But, also, I have had some county meetings the last three days in Iowa. And I find opposition even from Iowans about it, at the very same time that they complain about the high cost of gasoline. So I don`t believe it has support at the grassroots any more than it does in the \uc2 United States Congress\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: So what would you advocate to bring these prices down?\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: Well, in a very general way, why do we have high prices? Because we don`t build pipelines. We`re not drilling. We`re not loaning money to energy companies. Were putting additional regulations on fracking.\par \par \uc2 I will bet, except for 20 cents of the $2 increase in gasoline tax over the last year is because of this president`s bad energy policies. And just reverse them. I will give you one example that I came to on a couple of weekends ago, a person that`s got a contract to deliver fresh fruits and vegetables.\par \par \uc2 He says his price has gone up 7.5 cents. He says, of those 7.5 percent -- percentage points, 6 of it is directly related to the increase in diesel. The trucking, in other words, has gone up because of the high energy prices. So food prices have gone up not because of Putin, like the president said on -- from Europe at a news conference. It`s going up because the high energy prices.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Well, the fact of matter is, you`re right on the -- certainly the gas and oil prices. They had run up already 50 percent before the first Russian boots were heading toward Ukraine. Then it went up from there.\par \par \uc2 But, having said that, Senator, I`m just curious as to the administration`s posture with the oil companies, doing a lot of finger-pointing, refused to meet with the oil chiefs when they were in town.\par \par \uc2 So they met with the energy secretary, the Energy Department, which I`m told is about an eight-minute bike ride for the president, if he were to go to the Energy Department, but given his experience on bikes, maybe -- maybe not an ideal time.\par \par \uc2 But I`m wondering what you made of that, because the industry and the administration have been at loggerheads. Do you see anything that they can work out?\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: Isn`t it totally inconsistent to have the bad policy that just heard me describe to you, and then, a year later, go to the energy companies and say, you ought to pump more, when you have done everything to hurt their ability to look ahead the years that they must if they`re going to invest?\par \par \uc2 And then you go to Saudi Arabians and say -- tell them to send us more oil, when we got it right here under our own two feet. It just -- it`s laughable that they would have such an inconsistent policy.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Let me switch gears, if you don`t mind, sir, on the president, because what he was also talking when he was abroad, particularly in Madrid at the \uc2 NATO\uc2  summit, where he volunteered his frustration with the Supreme Court on some key decisions, including Roe v. Wade and reining in the EPA`s powers.\par \par \uc2 But he said that he would seriously call for removal of the filibuster rule to protect U.S. abortion rights. What do you think of that?\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: Well, first of all, separate from the pro-life abortion issue, all that, the filibuster, the 60-vote requirement in the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  is what forces cooperation and bipartisanship.\par \par \uc2 And if there`s anything I hear at my town meetings around Iowa, they say why you folks can`t get along. So I`m able to explain to him that, when you have a 50/50 Senate and a 60-vote requirement, the institution drives cooperation and bipartisanship.\par \par \uc2 And that`s what the people want. So, whether it`s connected with the abortion issue...\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes, but we don`t have it, right, Senator? We don`t have it.\par \par \uc2 We approve the Supreme Court justices. The filibuster is gone. It`s a simple majority. That dates back certainly to Harry Reid doing the same when a lot of Obama administration judgeships were not being approved.\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: Well...\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: But it seems like it`s out the window anyway. What do you say to that?\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: Well, I think that you brought up Senator -- Senator Reid.\par \par \uc2 When he did that in 2013, we warned him that he`s going to regret it. And if Democrats are in the minority after the next election, they`re going to regret that they changed the filibuster. So, if it ain`t broke, don`t fix it.\par \par \uc2 But the other thing is that, if you start doing it just for abortion, that`s a slippery slope. And pretty soon, you`re not going to have any 60- vote requirement at all. And everything`s going to be partisan, whether it`s a Republican majority or a Democrat majority. And people want cooperation in their government.\par \par \uc2 The lack of political cooperation is what`s hurting the credibility of the \uc2 Congress of the United States\uc2  and the federal government generally.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Senator, while I have you, I don`t know how closely you have focused on these January 6 Committee hearings going on. Too soon to tell how they will conclude.\par \par \uc2 We might be getting some evidence that it`s putting a dent in some support for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , if he should entertain a run for office again. Do you think that is -- that is hurting him?\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: I think it`s a little bit too early to tell that yet.\par \par \uc2 But I think some of the evidence that you`re speaking to is weak from this standpoint. In other words, the evidence could be entirely accurate, but the fact that there isn`t cross-examination and all nine members of the committee think the same way, and there`s not an opportunity to, let`s say, for instance, with Ms. Hutchinson`s testimony about what the Secret Service was doing, and they want to testify.\par \par \uc2 I don`t know how you get an answer until you bring the Secret Service in, and hear their sides of the story.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: And they might -- and to your point, they might do that.\par \par \uc2 But isn`t a lot of that, sir, Kevin McCarthy`s fault? He didn`t look for that, and maybe because of frustration with it was going to be a stacked deck. Say what you will.\par \par \uc2 But even President Trump has come back to criticize Kevin McCarthy for doing that. Do you think that`s fair? Do you think that, whatever one-sided nature you see of this -- there are two Republicans on this committee -- but that it`s not the way he wanted it?\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: Well, if I understand your question, right, and it`s a little bit crackly, but, anyway, when Pelosi didn`t allow the Republicans on the committee that the minority leader wanted to put on...\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Right.\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: ... and she didn`t want them, that hurts the credibility of the committee.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: OK. So there were other possibilities that could have been mentioned, but Kevin McCarthy stopped it there. But you`re right. It`s way past that.\par \par \uc2 Let me ask you a little bit. There are some polls also, Senator, that show \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  in Florida leading President Trump in states like Florida and New Hampshire. Now, nationally, the former president enjoys about an eight- or nine-point lead over DeSantis, but he used to enjoy more than a 20-point lead.\par \par \uc2 What do you make of all this?\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: Well, I think whoever wants to be president on the Republican nomination in 2024, whether it`s President Trump or any of the other nine people that have been to Iowa so far, because we`re the first-in-the-nation caucus -- and Senator Cotton is here next week as just another example -- Trump and everybody else is going to have to fight for the nomination.\par \par \uc2 So I think it`s too early to draw any conclusions about what`s going to happen in `23 and the first half of `24 to get that nomination.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Right.\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: But nobody can count on it just because they`re a governor of a famous state like Florida or an ex-president of the United States. You got to fight for it.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Do you have any favorites yourself, Senator?\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: Well, we in Iowa don`t have favorites, because we don`t want to discourage anybody from coming to the first-in-the-nation caucus, Iowa, at least on the Republican ticket.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: Now, we don`t know whether the Democrats are going to be first- in-the-nation or not, because they`re having internal fights.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes. They`re debating that.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: At least, the Iowa...\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: It will still be first for Republicans, right? OK.\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: At least, the Iowa Democrats -- the Iowa Democrats want to be first in the nation, but we don`t know if the national Democrats will let them do that.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: But the Iowa Republicans want the Iowa Democrats to keep fighting to be first in the nation.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, in Iowa, you agree on that.\par \par \uc2 All right, Senator, great seeing you. Have a safe July 4 weekend.\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2  on all of that.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, Inc.  Copyright CQ-2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All materials herein are  protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced,  distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the  prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You may not alter  or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the  content. \par \par \uc2 Document CAVU000020220701ei710002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden Rambles About Gas Prices, Putin; Biden Attacks SCOTUS For Overturning Roe, While Lying About Inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Joe Concha \par \uc2 8,312 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 June 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: And welcome to HANNITY.\par \par \uc2 Now, tonight, Democrats, the media mob, they are focused on one thing and one thing only and that is the one riot that took place on January 6th, 2021, not the 574 riots in the summer of 2020. It's literally all they have. They're clinging to it and abortion like manna from heaven, the only political issues they think they have.\par \par \uc2 They have taken every word of this week's double hearsay witness as complete gospel truth they have raced to the finish line and many on the media mob in particular many in Congress, they have announced that former President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  is guilty of everything she accused him of.\par \par \uc2 Never mind the many reports that two Secret Service agents deny her allegation that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tried to commandeer the vehicle that he was being driven in. Never mind that one of President Trump's attorneys says even though she testified under oath it was her handwriting, it's my handwriting. And again, she did that under oath. Never mind that the president, President Trump's denials that he ever wanted to waive armed people into the rally, he's denied it.\par \par \uc2 How about we do a few simple things for once and not rush to judgment and maybe give people the benefit of the doubt and let's do these three things. Let's have one, the Secret Service agents, let them sign sworn affidavits. They don't even have to go before cameras and give up their careers.\par \par \uc2 Two, how about we do this, why don't we hire the best professional handwriting experts because I would probably bet a lot of money that they'll be able to determine whether or not it was Trump's lawyer or the hearsay witness who actually wrote the notes that they referred to in the hearings this week?\par \par \uc2 And how about number three -- how about we see if any of the people that were manning the metal detectors were ever asked to stop doing their jobs and we can put them before the cameras? Then the committee can investigate whether the president authorized the National Guard as for people with the president on January fourth have said to us right here on this program they witnessed him doing it. This is an amazing distraction though for the Democrats and their press secretaries in the media mob because their policies are failing on a spectacular and unprecedented level so they don't have to talk about that because they'll just stick to January 6th.\par \par \uc2 Now, their president, his radical party is a disaster for the entire country. Now, as a result, America's economy is historically bad. The Dow just had its worst six months uh to start a year since 1962. The S&P is off to their worth of start since and the Nasdaq, they've had their worst start ever.\par \par \uc2 Now, meanwhile, breaking today the \uc2 Atlanta Fed\uc2  is projecting that our economy will officially be in a recession by July. Remember, it's defined by two quarters of negative growth.\par \par \uc2 Remember a few days ago, the administration was -- they were telling us not to worry about a recession that it was not inevitable. Of course, these are the same geniuses that promised that inflation was transitory, the same geniuses who seem to believe that some kind of magical transition to wind and solar is unfolding before our eyes and will bring us to the renewable energy independence promised land because Joe and his radical new Green Deal socialists they promised us they would eliminate American fossil fuels.\par \par \uc2 Now, when they said they would eliminate fossil fuels, they didn't say only domestic fossil fuels because they have no problem importing let's see Russian oil, \uc2 OPEC\uc2  nations oil, Saudi Arabian oil. They're open to importing oil from Venezuela, and I hear they even took a million barrels of oil from Iran last year.\par \par \uc2 Now, clearly, they have no idea what they're doing and the pain and the suffering of these radical policies and all that pain that's causing every American now. And earlier today, when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was asked how long Americans would need to fit the bill for these rising gas prices, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  just shrugged it off and said well as long as it takes. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATESD: We are going to support Ukraine as long as it takes. Look at the impact that the war on Ukraine has had on Russia. They've had to renege on their national debt for the first time since the beginning almost well over years. They've lost years of the gains they made in terms of their economy.\par \par \uc2 They're in a situation where they're having trouble because of my imposition of dealing with what can be exported to Russia in terms of technology. They can't even you know they're having they're going to have trouble maintaining oil production because they don't have the technology to do it. They need American technology.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Where's the sense of urgency, the sense of capturing the moment and helping the American people? Apparently, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  doesn't feel your pain, maybe just thinks everyone flies around the world, collecting millions of dollars from oligarchs and bad actors in Russia or the Bank of China or oil and gas companies in Ukraine like his son, zero experience Hunter. Or maybe \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  simply doesn't care or doesn't even know.\par \par \uc2 Now, as we all know, there is one person and one person only who decreased America's domestic supply of oil and gas. It wasn't \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . It was \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  doesn't care about the truth. Just listen to the president's pretty deranged speech in Europe when he somehow managed to attack the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  all while lying once again about inflation. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: We have the strongest economy in the world. Our inflation rates are lower than other nations in the world. The one thing that has been destabilizing is the outrageous behavior of the \uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2  on overruling not only Roe v. Wade but essentially challenging the right to privacy. We've been a leader in the world in terms of personal rights and privacy rights, and it is a mistake in my view for the Supreme Court to do what it did.\par \par \uc2 I can understand why the American people are frustrated because of what the Supreme Court did. I can understand why the American people are frustrated because of inflation.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, in truth, we've got to remind you, Joe wasn't a leader in civil rights because Joe partnered with a former Klansman named Robert Byrd and tried to stop the integration of public schools. He didn't want the schools in his words to become racial jungles. So let's help educate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  because he's deeply confused as everybody knows. Every single other country in the G7 has a lower inflation rate than our country the USA. In fact, almost every single country in the developed world has a lower rate including Canada, Germany, France, Italy, Japan, Saudi Arabia and I can keep going.\par \par \uc2 And, by the way, for Joe to attack one of America's greatest institutions the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  while on foreign soil, that's pretty low even for Joe. But don't take my word for it, listen to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  himself because he said it in 2017. Take a listen.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOI CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: What worries me most and I never thought I'd have to make this speech or want to make this speech, the almost drumbeat of denigration of the institutional structures that govern us is dangerous. When you delegitimize the courts, you delegitimize the legislative body.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It does raise a lot of questions, does \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hold any real principles or values other than enriching himself his family and going to Delaware every other weekend -- well, pretty much every weekend. The country's falling apart. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is just doddering along, doing whatever his far left advisers tell them to do, and it's now so bad, even top Democrats -- they're voicing their concerns.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, according to a poll conducted by the "AP", a vast majority of Democrats, 78 percent, think this country,, our country is headed in the wrong direction under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . That's Democrats.\par \par \uc2 His "Real Clear Politics" average has Joe's approval under 38 percent, the lowest point in his presidency. By the way, that includes outlier polls that give them very high approval ratings that are not real.\par \par \uc2 Former Obama adviser David Axelrod is now venting about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , even on fake news CNN. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DAVID AXELROD, FORMER OBAMA ADVISER: When the president got into those questions, gas prices and inflation and abortion rights, there was a lot less of that certainty, a lot less of that emphatic nature of his initial presentation on \uc2 NATO\uc2  because he doesn't have great answers.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Well, it's embarrassing for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the Democratic Party. But so much worse for the American people that are struggling to fill up their gas tanks and put food on the table because we have a human vegetable that probably doesn't know what day of the week it is today as president.\par \par \uc2 And, of course, he's surrounded by a bunch of radical woke staffers who don't know anything about the economy or energy or anything else. So, if we're serious, if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is not mentally or physically up to the job, he should retire now, a full 59 percent, a new poll of Americans see exactly what I've been telling you since the campaign.\par \par \uc2 I was kind of the lone voice out there saying this guy's weak and frail and a cognitive mess. It wasn't hard to spot. Now, 59 percent of Americans see it.\par \par \uc2 Think about this, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  almost never takes questions from the press. The only sit-down TV interview in the past six months was Jimmy Kimmel. It wasn't exactly a barn burner either. According to "Politico", the White House avoids using the Oval Office for press events because they don't have a teleprompter.\par \par \uc2 And look at your screen during meetings,