ight. There was a stabbing on 64th and I think 3rd or Lex just a couple of weeks back in broad daylight, and that was on tape.\par \par \uc2 It's getting worse every day.\par \par \uc2 CURTIS SLIWA (R), FORMER CANDIDAY FOR NYC MAYOR: Sean, it's fear city again. It's a hot mess, no matter what neighborhood you're in.\par \par \uc2 That particular location that that 20-year-old woman with a baby carriage and a three-month-old child where she was shot in the head, it's just one block from where I used to take my oldest son Anthony and taught him basketball. That was 12 years ago. That was a safe location. It's not safe anymore.\par \par \uc2 And I told you, the swagger man Eric Adams, he has no plan to combat crime as it escalates. And it's amazing -- yeah, I mean, you're having \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2  up next who took on Governor Newsom, I took on Eric Adams, both of them want to go to the White House when in fact they haven't even done the job in their state of the city.\par \par \uc2 Crime is the number one problem. The criminals are ahead and the culture that snitches get stitches and end up in ditches prevail, so that you're not solving most of these crimes.\par \par \uc2 You're losing cops. They're going on early retirement. They're being recruited away and the war on police continues unabated and now you see people mass exodus in California where Larry is, mass exodus in New York where I am, to states that are a lot safer, south of the Mason-Dixon line.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, billions of dollars in just the last two years leaving New York City alone.\par \par \uc2 Larry, same problem out in California when you're -- where you are. Curtis is right.\par \par \uc2 LARRY ELDER\uc2 , RADIO TALK SHOW HOST: Oh, absolutely. And, Sean, thank you for having me nice to see you again, Curtis.\par \par \uc2 And as you pointed out, Sean, it's happening everywhere including high-end areas. I'm out here in California, in Hancock Park, a very high-end area where \uc2 Maxine Waters\uc2  has her five million dollar mansion, a UCLA graduate student stabbed to death by a career criminal should not have been out in the streets.\par \par \uc2 Beverly Hills, a music mogul's wife was murdered. She's in her 80s and they had arm security at the home. Guy comes in with a firearm, shoots the woman, again a long criminal record.\par \par \uc2 And just two weeks ago, two Almonte police officers right outside of L.A. were murdered by a guy who was also career criminal, two years earlier was facing three years in jail because as a career criminal, you're not supposed to have a firearm. He had a firearm and the assistant D.A. handling the case said because of the soft on crime policies of the D.A., George Gascon, who's facing a recall election in November, he got 20 days and two years probation. And the day before, he killed the cops.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Unbelievable.\par \par \uc2 ELDER: The day before, Sean, his probation officer wanted to revoke his probation because he had assaulted his girlfriend and wanted him arrested. He wasn't arrested. They gave him a hearing. He shouldn't have been on the streets in the first place.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You know, Curtis, I saw you with Mayor Giuliani out campaigning for Andrew the other day, and the thing is we know how to stop crime especially murder with good policing, because \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  got the process started. We were getting near 3,000 murders in New York City a year, and between Rudy's policies then continued by Mayor Bloomberg, we got down to about 300. I mean -- and those policies worked.\par \par \uc2 You ran on refunding the police and bringing back Rudy's policies. We wouldn't be having this type of crime wave, would we?\par \par \uc2 SLIWA: No, and you have to have stop and frisk, particularly in the high crime areas where young men decide that they want to raise their nine millimeters shoot it in the air like they just don't care.\par \par \uc2 The other problem though, Sean, if you notice with the \uc2 United States Supreme Court\uc2  ruling that law abiding men and women should have the right to have a concealed permit to carry a handgun, all these mayors and all these governors both in California where Larry is and where I am in New York, they act as if this is the worst possible thing, that law-abiding legal Americans carrying a concealed weapon is a danger.\par \par \uc2 Look at all the places where that takes place already. You go to Arizona, you go to Florida, you go to Texas, you go to all these states where law- abiding citizens are able to defend themselves and their fellow citizens, and it's a much safer place to be than in the places that Larry and I live in, in which they make it almost impossible for you to have a concealed carry permit, yet the criminals -- they have a license to shoot and loot and steal and do it again and again.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And now, the right to keep arms or the right of the people to keep and bear arms shall not be infringed is back. Let's see how the states try and work their way around it.\par \par \uc2 Larry Elder\uc2 , thank you. Curtis, great to see you.\par \par \uc2 When we come back, more HANNITY straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Unfortunately, that is all the time we have left this evening. Thank you so much for being with us. Thank you for making this show possible. We hope you'll set your DVR so you never miss an episode of HANNITY.\par \par \uc2 By the way, news anytime, FOXNews.com, Hannity.com. Have a great Fourth of July weekend. Enjoy this beautiful country, all the blessings and liberty and freedom from God. Their rights come from God, not government.\par \par \uc2 Let not your heart be troubled.\par \par \uc2 Happy Fourth, Laura Ingraham.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020220701ei6u00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden's Transatlantic American Smear; Euro-Elites Agree With Biden On Abortion; Not Content In Disliking America, Left Wants To Tear It Down; Biden Hoping For \uc2 Quiet Revolution\uc2  To Protect Roe; Legacy Of Left: Juneteenth Over July 4th; U.S. Inflation Rate Surges, Biden Shrugs; \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  Gives Speech To Win Over More Leftists; Possible Negative Effects Of Continuing Inflation And Raising Interest Rates On U.S. Economy Examined; New Yorkers Answers Questions On U.S. History And Whether They're Proud Of America; Rep. \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  (R-CO) Interviewed On New York Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 's Comments Criticizing Of Concealed Carry Permit Holders\b0\par\par\uc2 Laura Ingraham \par \uc2 7,658 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 June 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: DVR, so you never miss an episode of "HANNITY". By the way, news anytime, Foxnews.com, Hannity.com. Have a great Fourth of July weekend. Enjoy this beautiful country. All the blessings and liberty and freedom from God. Damn right, it's come from God, not government.\par \par \uc2 Let not your heart be troubled. Happy Fourth, Laura Ingraham.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Happy Independence Day. You know, you made me sad on the crime story, because I can't stop thinking about that poor woman and what's happened to the city of New York.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It's terrible.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We're back in the 1970s, the no man's land, early 1980s. It's - people got to vote for change.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Think of our friend Gianno Caldwell, losing his 18-year-old brother same weekend a five-month old baby girl shot and killed. I mean, it happens every weekend. You never hear the names. They never talk about it. They never solve the problem.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, this democratic leadership's got to change. Sean, have a wonderful Fourth. And we'll see you next week.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You too. Have a great Fourth. Have a great weekend.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. I'm Laura Ingraham - and I will, and this is THE INGRAHAM ANGLE from Washington tonight.\par \par \uc2 The most unpatriotic president ever. That is the focus of tonight's 'Angle'.\par \par \uc2 Now, going into the Fourth of July weekend, the most patriotic time of the year. But of course, it's really a miserable time for the left because they're embarrassed by our people and our history. Let's face it, they hate most of our past presidents, including Washington and Lincoln. Everyone on Mount Rushmore, they want them all ripped down.\par \par \uc2 And the last thing they want to do is celebrate America's independence, because after all, they don't want America to be independent. So you think I'm exaggerating, or it's just TV stuff? Well, I'm not think. Think about who these people have become. Think about what they truly believe, how they feel about American history.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Racism is real in America. And it has always been. Xenophobia is real in America, and always has been. Sexism too.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: You should not be relying on a history filled with racism and sexism and homophobia to determine our fundamental rights today.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Original sin of slavery weaved white supremacy into our founding documents and principles.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What a horrible person. And how do these people feel about the actual people who live here?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MERRICK GARLAND\uc2 , ATTORNEY GENERAL: The top domestic violent extremists threat comes from racially or ethnically motivated violent extremists.\par \par \uc2 GENERAL MARK MILLEY, CHAIRMAN OF THE JOINT CHIEFS OF STAFF: I want to understand white rage, and I'm white.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT, UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: White supremacy is a poison. It's a poison running through our - it really is. Running through our body politic, that's been allowed to fester and grow right in front of our eyes.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He's talking about half the country right there. Now, how do they feel about our being an independent country?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Foundation of a rules-based international order, built out of the wreckage of two wars, world wars.\par \par \uc2 NED PRICE, SPOKESMAN FOR THE DEPARTMENT OF STATE: Violations of our core tenets of the rules-based international order.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: One of our defining missions is to strengthen the international rules-based order.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, my god. OK. Let me define rules-based international order for you. They're vague rules that exist only to restrain and weaken the United States, and then empower countries that enjoy free riding off of us, or China. That - other rules never, never apply to China, which would never dream of doing anything against its own self interest. Forget about it.\par \par \uc2 Now, remember, the Biden administration doesn't go overseas to defend American interests. Oh, no. They engage in multilateral talks to advance global interests. American interests don't even come second or third and Biden world.\par \par \uc2 Why should we be trusted to make our own policies, or even frankly, even choose our own leaders? We should have to live under international norms drafted by bureaucrats in Europe. The EU, they should run our domestic policy, our climate agenda, our foreign policy. And of course, they should decide all hot button cultural issues. And we know what they think.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BORIS JOHNSON\uc2 , PRIME MINISTER, UNITED KINGDOM: It clearly has massive impacts on people's thinking around the world. It's a very important decision. I've got to tell you, I think it's a big step backwards. I think it's a big step backwards.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Of course, Biden rather than stand up for our Constitution and defend our system, even when he disagrees with some court rulings, he piled on.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: America's better position to lead the world than we ever have been. The one thing that has been destabilizing is the outrageous behavior of the \uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2  on overruling not only Roe v Wade, but essentially challenging the right to privacy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Wait, wait. I'm confused. I thought that the one thing destabilizing the world was President Putin and Ukraine. Now, of course, Biden never talks about President Xi's forced enslavement of millions of Chinese, or the extermination of God knows how many dissidents in China.\par \par \uc2 Biden never speaks about how destabilizing it is when China threatens Taiwan. Nah, potatoes, small potatoes. Instead, we saw \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  standing in Madrid, telling the world that what is truly destabilizing is that some women in states like Mississippi can't get more abortions.\par \par \uc2 Talk about outrageous behavior. It's beyond unpatriotic. It's disgusting. But for him, placating the far-left by trashing America abroad is far more important than standing up for the American people in front of the sneering Euro-elites, who are being guarded, by the way, by soldiers from the same country that they despise.\par \par \uc2 We know this by the fact that they're scrambling to do everything they can to reverse our independence. They think our health policy should be made by the WHO. They think our trade policy should be made by the \uc2 WTO\uc2 . That our foreign policy, as I said, should be shaped by the Europeans, and Xi over there in Hong Kong doing a victory lap and these European fools are complaining about the fact that Americans in all 50 states get to vote on abortion.\par \par \uc2 OK. Well, send me a memo the next time that Boris and Emmanuel lecture President Xi about the lack of fundamental rights over there. Don't hold your breath.\par \par \uc2 In fact, this was \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  today. I was up early and I decided to watch him live and his press conference after the G7. He was asked if the UK needs to reexamine its relationship with China. Now, notice the equivocation.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: It's very important that we remember that we have to - we had a huge economic relationship with China. So does every country around that table. It is very, very important that we understand that China is a great country. It's going to be a gigantic fact of the world's economy for a long time to come. So you need to - there has to be a balanced approach.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: A balanced approach, but no step backwards in China, I guess, only in the United States. That's real courage, Bo Jo. Of course, what Biden should have been doing in Europe is standing up for America, not