c2 INGRAHAM: I love him.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: He's the best. But you know what is disturbing, how many people dislike the country.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Really.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: These are citizens that actually hate their own country. Even the celebrations are kind of get togethers there. And when you look at this new FOX News poll, judging whether you're proud of your country or not, the poll revealed Republicans, 36 percent are proud of their country, 60 percent are not. That's a lower number than Democrats. I'm sorry --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Who are these Republicans who aren't proud of the country?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Laura, I don't care what your political fortunes are.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That makes me mad. That makes me mad.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: The political fortunes of the moment should not judge or in any way prejudice your love or pride of country. That's your future and your heritage, and you should defend it. It's no wonder some people are down on the country. They've been taught this by Republicans and Democrats.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: My family never celebrated July 4th. And it was met with like so much shock. And it was because my father was a student of history.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: They knew what they were doing. These Republican members of Congress knew what they were doing, and they need to be shamed for it in the very least.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: They have coopted this term "patriot" to mean something that is really just bastardized the term. "Patriot," that's not when a patriot is. Patriots don't do this.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Laura, division is not a virtue. And trying to separate people rather than unite them, that's what people should be doing in the media. And every day it's running down not only a portion of the citizenry, but the country itself. This is really dangerous. And people don't stop to think about it enough.\par \par \uc2 But when I was out interviewing people, we constructed a little historical quiz. I'll see if you can get these.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Who established the celebration of July 4th and said we should celebrate with fireworks and celebrations coast to coast? Do you remember?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I don't, actually, because I think it's been changed around. Everyone has a different opinion of it.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Probably the woman, it's probably Martha.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Martha Washington.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: I'm going to guess Martha.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I stopped history when I left school. So yes, school is out for the year. I'm not doing any more questions.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Can I phone a friend?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yes, you can phone a friend.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: OK, dope, dope, dope. Can I phone you?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I'm going to go with a wildcard Martha Washington.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I'm not giving anything away. Who was it?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: John Adams.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: She got it right. Leave to it the Bostonian to know. You're the only one all day.\par \par \uc2 This celebrity is a district descendant of someone who signed the Declaration of Independence, is it Denzel Washington, Amy Adams, or Reese Witherspoon?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Amy Adams.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: I'll do Amy Adams.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: When you have power, people will always try to take it from you, always.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Let's just go with Reese Witherspoon.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Reese Witherspoon.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Hello, patriots.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Oh, my God. It's Capital Barbie.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Damn, I'm going to have to go with him on this one, because I wouldn't know either, bro.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: You got it. Reese Witherspoon.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: John Witherspoon is her ante -- she's a descendent of John Witherspoon, who was the only clergyman to sign the Declaration of Independence, Laura.\par \par \uc2 How are you celebrating?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I'm going to be with my children.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: OK.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And we're going to be somewhere.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Oh, my goodness, look, you are a Star Spangled girl right now.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, my gosh.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: You are our Fourth of July. I'm glad we can celebrate. I wish we could put a historical panorama right there in the dress. Now you have a historical panorama.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK, that is disturbing.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK, that is disturbing. I don't know.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Go to break.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Raymond is telling me I've got to wrap. OK, wrap, Sam says. All right, thank you, Raymond. I'm exploding here.\par \par \uc2 Despite a win for gun owners at the court last week, leftist leaders are doing their best to unilaterally strip them of their constitutional rights. Congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  is here next. She'll respond to one of the most revealing comments on the issue from New York's \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 . Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The 29 Republicans in Congress, the ones who helped the Democrats pass their gun safety bill, have repeatedly assured gun owners that no one is coming for their guns or stripping them of their rights. Two recent instances have us seriously doubting them. Earlier this week, the personal information of every Californian who applied for a concealed carry since 2011 was accidentally leaked by a liberal attorney, Attorney General \uc2 Rob Bonta\uc2 . And then just yesterday, New York Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  engaged in this stunning exchange.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Do you have the number to show that it's the concealed carry permit holders that are committing crimes?\par \par \uc2 GOV. \uc2 KATHY HOCHUL\uc2 , (D) NEW YORK: I don't need to have numbers. I don't have to have a data point to point to to say that this is going to -- all I know is I have a responsibility to the people of this state to have sensible gun safety laws.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: A responsibility to the people of the state not to have numbers, hear me?\par \par \uc2 Here now is Congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2 , co-chair of the Second Amendment Caucus. Congresswoman, you can't even make up the stupidity of \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , who is up for reelection. If New York votes for that, I don't even have words.\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 LAUREN BOEBERT\uc2 , (R-CO): Right. I think my constituents have a very healthy distrust of big government, and this is exactly why. We have California liberals losing personal information, leaking personal information of gun owners. And then you have this New York governor who is saying we don't need data. It's the pesky permit holders that are New York's problems. This is why we do not trust big government, and this is why we need to put a stop to it happening.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: FOX News Digital compiled \uc2 FBI\uc2  data from 2019 detailing murders and gun murders. They found that many states with higher percentages of gun ownership had lower or similar rates to states with strict gun control. So why is the left so fixated on this narrative?\par \par \uc2 BOEBERT: They certainly hate firearms, and they hate gun owners, and they hate our rights. So they want to paint this other picture that this is dangerous and this is what we need to go after. But we know that the gun- free zones are actually the deadly zones. It's a soft target for all of our community members, for our children.\par \par \uc2 And the leaking of this data is an absolute target --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's dangerous.\par \par \uc2 BOEBERT: Very dangerous on firearm owners. And this is why I'm on legislation with my good friend Michael Cloud to make sure that the ATF does not have a registry. They have over a billion names in a database, and we are making sure that that ends.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, Republicans have to absolutely be on that.\par \par \uc2 Your old pal -- does he cry a lot, I guess, I don't know, \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , he took some shots at you on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  over your comments about the separation of church and state. And he said "There's no difference between your comments and the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 . We must oppose the Christian \uc2 Taliban\uc2 . I say this as a Christian." Are you now or have you ever been a member of the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 BOEBERT: Oh, goodness. No, no, no, I have not. But little Adam, he is retiring. America does not like him. He cannot win reelection. He would not win reelection for dog catcher. So Adam is not going to be our problem anymore. I have bigger things to worry about, protecting the rights of my constituents. I certainly honor the Lord and praise God with all that I have. But I'm not going to --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You don't have a Christianity litmus test --\par \par \uc2 BOEBERT: Correct, right, right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You don't have a Christianity litmus test, however, for legislation, which I think is kind of what he's referencing.\par \par \uc2 BOEBERT: Right, exactly. But Adam is absolutely irrelevant. He's already proving that he's a Democrat with his January 6th unselect committee. And then on his way out the door, he wants to say that he supports gun control. And just to put that nail in the coffin that says I am not for this.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Great to see you.\par \par \uc2 The Ronald Reagan Library might have lost its way, but the president they honor never did. The Last Bite is next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And now a few words from President Reagan, my old boss, on July 4th, 1986, about our founding fathers.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RONALD REAGAN\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT: Fifty-six men came forward to sign the parchment. It was noted at the time that they pledged their lives, their fortunes, and their sacred honors. That was more than rhetoric. Each of those men knew the penalty for high treason to the crown. They must all hang together, Benjamin Franklin said, or surely we will all hang separately.\par \par \uc2 Their courage created a nation built on a universal claim to human dignity, on the proposition that every man, woman, and child had a right to a future of freedom.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, can you imagine hearing anything like that so reverent about our founding fathers from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  or \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , or frankly, from any Democrat, for that matter? Our founding fathers knew the risks they were taking. They put their lives on the line to make a better future for themselves, but really for their children and their grandchildren, and for you, and for me, for our children.\par \par \uc2 So remember that this weekend when you're barbecuing, watching parades, spending time with your family, have a lot of fun, but remember that our country was founded in strength and bravery. We need to stand proud of our country, not trash it on the world stage or gratuitously at home or try to dismantle what makes us great.\par \par \uc2 So fly your flag, have an ice-cold beverage in your Freedom Matters koozie, get them free on the website, and remember, it is America now and forever.\par \par \uc2 And Greg Gutfeld takes it all from here.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020220701ei6u00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Brazil's President Bolsonaro Talks To \uc2 Tucker Carlson\b0\par\par\uc2 Tucker Carlson, Kevin Corke \par \uc2 6,751 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 June 2022\par \uc2 Fox News Channel: Tucker Carlson Tonight\par \uc2 TCARL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: I didn't try to lose it. It just happened that way. And every time I go back down to Philly, I start saying things like "Watters." I can't help it.\par \par \uc2 But it's also true like when I go down south, I start speaking with a southern twang. I'm just very impressionable.\par \par \uc2 Tucker is next. I'm Watters. This is my world.\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST, TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT: Good evening and welcome to TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT.\par \par \uc2 Here in the United States, we've been so deeply engrossed in our own debates over whether men should be allowed to compete on girls' swim teams or whether it's immoral to carry our groceries in plastic bags that we've missed the fact that the government of China has been busy with its own agenda -- taking over the world.\par \par \uc2 In the space of just 15 years, for example, the Chinese have succeeded in re-colonizing the entire continent of Africa. Didn't think that could happen? Well, it is happening.\par \par \uc2 In Africa, China now calls the shots and takes the natural resources for itself. Period.\par \par \uc2 As of tonight, there is only one remaining African country that dares to recognize Taiwan, and it happens to be among the smallest countries in Africa -- Swaziland. Everyone else on the continent obeys Beijing.\par \par \uc2 But wait a second. How can this be happening? Isn't colonialism racist and bad? Yes, it is and no one is worse and more racist than the Chinese. Go on Chinese social media sometime and see how they describe the Africans they've subjugated. It's horrifying.\par \par \uc2 So, why isn't "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " writing stories about any of this? You know why -- because "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " is on China's side. That's why they all but ignore the brutal Chinese colonization of Latin America, which is also in full swing right now.\par \par \uc2 Colonialism violates everything "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " once claimed to believe in, but that's okay, because they never really believed any of it anyway. It was always about power.\par \par \uc2 We came to Brazil this week to see for ourselves what the Chinese are doing to Latin America. We're making a documentary about it for our "Tucker Carlson Originals" series.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has the last pro-American government in Latin America. It's our single most important ally in the Western Hemisphere.\par \par \uc2 Allowing Brazil to become a colony of China would be a significant blow to us and potentially a very serious military threat. The Biden administration appears to be in favor of it.\par \par \uc2 One person who is emphatically not in favor of it is the President of Brazil, \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 . So, of course, the American media hate him. Here's some of their slander.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CHRIS HAYES, MSNBC HOST: The United States isn't the only country lurching dangerously towards authoritarianism. It is happening all over, indeed.\par \par \uc2 Just yesterday, for example, Brazilians elected \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 JASON JOHNSON, MSNBC POLITICAL COMMENTATOR: Usually you don't get rid of an aspiring dictator through the electoral process. Brazil is going to have trouble with Bolsonaro.\par \par \uc2 LINETTE LOPEZ, BUSINESS INSIDER: It's that same authoritarian, like women- hating, racist energy. He's the Trump of Brazil.\par \par \uc2 MSNBC REPORTER: President Bolsonaro doesn't believe in social distancing, doesn't want lockdowns -- much, much more extreme than President Trump.\par \par \uc2 FAREED ZAKARIA, CNN HOST: Brazil's far-right nationalist President \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 , spoke at an event in Dallas. These two men and fellow travelers like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  represent the growing global threat to the ideals of liberalism.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: These are people whose research consists of three minutes on Wikipedia on the way to the studio. "He's a racist." Of course, he is. He "doesn't want lockdowns." There's your proof.\par \par \uc2 But it is the last clip from plagiarist, Fareed Zakaria that explains why they're so mad at Bolsonaro. Bolsonaro, Fareed Zakaria tells us, represents a "growing global threat to the ideas of liberalism" -- liberalism? Meaning neoliberalism, meaning globalism.\par \par \uc2 And in fact, that is true. Bolsonaro is no \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2 . He's not a low- IQ fascist who would be working as an \uc2 Instagram\uc2  influencer if he didn't have his own army.\par \par \uc2 He's not the President of Ukraine who shuts down television stations that dare to criticize him and outlaws opposition parties and arms Nazis.\par \par \uc2 In conventional terms, Bolsonaro is, in fact, liberal. He has done nothing to stop civil liberties in Brazil. But at the same time, he is a nationalist. He cares about his country. He resists China. Therefore, he must be stopped.\par \par \uc2 George Soros\uc2  hates him and so does \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . He's not with the program.\par \par \uc2 So naturally, we wanted to meet him. Yesterday we did. We sat with Bolsonaro for more than an hour and the first thing we learn is that the left in Brazil hates him very much. They tried to kill him when he first ran for President four years ago.\par \par \uc2 With very little money and the backing of no party, he came out of nowhere to get 57 million votes. But he almost didn't survive to be elected.\par \par \uc2 He was stabbed by a leftist almost to death at a rally, at which point the left funded lawyers took him come in and rescue his attempted murderer -- an amazing story that hasn't gotten a ton of coverage in the United States. "He's an authoritarian," says MSNBC. All right.\par \par \uc2 So, we asked Bolsonaro about the stabbing in our conversation. We also asked him about his Christian faith, which is on display, something else that triggers them. We asked him about our Supreme Court stance on abortion, his views on gun rights, and we asked him fundamentally, why do you think you're so hated?\par \par \uc2 Here's the first part of the conversation.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: The parallels between politics in Brazil and politics in the United States are striking to an American. You are opposed by a coalition of billionaires, college professors, and CNN. Tell us what the opposition wants. What will Brazil look like if your opponent wins, do you think?\par \par \uc2 JAIR BOLSONARO\uc2 , BRAZIL PRESIDENT (through translator): My election itself was almost a miracle. I had nothing going for me to be elected. I was just say, an isolated Member of Congress known as the lower segment of National Congress in Brazil.\par \par \uc2 I conducted my campaign anchored on a biblical passage, John 3:32, "Thou shall know the truth, and the truth shall set you free."\par \par \uc2 The media never gave me any visibility or space. Much to the contrary, they attacked me all the time throughout the campaign.\par \par \uc2 On September 6th, 2018, the eve of the election, I suffered an attempted assassination.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 NBC REPORTER: The far right candidate, \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 , who was being carried through a crowd, you can see him there on the shoulders of some supporters when suddenly, a man with a knife stabs him in the abdomen.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BOLSONARO (through translator): Doctors say my survival was a miracle, and the same is true for my election.\par \par \uc2 And a very important factor, which you may perhaps not be aware of, was the fact that Brazil had a country that upon taking office as President, the incumbent President surrenders strategic positions in the Cabinet political parties, including the Cabinet Ministries, state banks, state companies, I did not do that. So I got a lot of pushback, strong pushback from Brazilian Parliament, and we were able to withstand.\par \par \uc2 In 2019 and 2020, of course, the pandemic hit, and everything changed and this country was doomed to a fiasco because many Governors actually gathered forces through the economy to defeat me.\par \par \uc2 We were able to successfully come to the end of 2020-2021 and came to a positive balance of about three million new job posts created in Brazil during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 And we're now in the last year of my current term in office, and the left wing is really going desperate, because despite everything, you know, we're doing pretty well.\par \par \uc2 Now, the problems in Brazil are the problems that are there for the whole world such as, for example, inflation as a result of mistake and policies adopted during the pandemic, such as stay-at-home and the economy will take care of itself later.\par \par \uc2 The lockdown policies, as well as the war between Ukraine and Russia, which has partly, of course affected the price of fuels, which in turn, of course, reflects in higher inflation levels.\par \par \uc2 The left wing uses that to -- tries to use that to defeat me.\par \par \uc2 If they do come back to power, in my view, they will never go back or go out of power again. Even former President Lula, I mean, everything he says despite all the foolish things he says, and despite attacking so many people, such as Christians, for example, when it comes to the issues such as abortion policy, and the apparent partnership he has with many crooks and thieves, he wants many crimes to no longer be crimes.\par \par \uc2 And he wants to be able to lend money to dictatorships all around the world. He wants to disarm the good-willing population. They also want to revitalize the MST, the landless people movement and arm them.\par \par \uc2 I mean, they should have no less or no more than 10 percent of votes, but they do. The opinion polls conducted by data following one of the last polls indicated that Lula is perceived as being more honest than I am. I mean, this kind of opinion poll, of course, is totally mistaken, it doesn't work, but they do conduct these polls to attach some element of credibility to potential future manipulation of votes.\par \par \uc2 That's a suspicion we clearly have. That's actually more than a suspicion. We have some circumstantial evidence, and if the left wing does come back to power, in my view, they will never leave power anymore, and this country will follow the same pathways as Venezuela, Argentina, Chile, Colombia -- Brazil will be one more wagon in that train.\par \par \uc2 And the losers will be the Brazilian population and also the left wing itself. I mean, the left wing voter will lose as a result, and all of South America will be colored red, if you understand me, and in my view, the United States will become virtually an isolated country in the world.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: There are so many questions, but back to the stabbing during your campaign, you were stabbed by a leftist at campaign event. He was never sent to prison. He went to a mental hospital.\par \par \uc2 Did you think you were going to die?\par \par \uc2 BOLSONARO (through translator): The doctors in the city where I underwent the surgery and also the following day in Sao Paulo, the capital, they said out of 100 people who were stabbed like I was, only one person survives, and thank God I survived.\par \par \uc2 And also due to my physical preparation, also because healthy lifestyle I had throughout my life, so that helped me resist.\par \par \uc2 And as a coincidence on the eve, the day before, I had taken a shot of benzidine, a drug that helps to fight a more serious or what would otherwise be a more serious infection because the knife was infected. The person who stabbed me was affiliated with the left-wing party, PSOL.\par \par \uc2 The following day, after the stabbing, three renowned lawyers came to the town, Juiz de For a to try to defend the person, and the person who stabbed me, Adelio on the same day, September the 6th, someone tried to go into the House of Representatives using false documentation, which could serve as an alibi if he had fled the crime scene Juiz de Fora.\par \par \uc2 So someone tried to use his documents to go into the House of Representatives as an alibi. No one can possibly explain to me why the investigation has not involved with so many elements available.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: The media in Brazil is highly concentrated, 90 percent of all ad dollars go to a company called "Globo" which dominates television here. They're opposed to you.\par \par \uc2 How did you win? How could you win again with the entire Brazilian media against you?\par \par \uc2 BOLSONARO (through translator): Yes, there is the weight of the media against me. True. But social media has been doing a great job in Brazil.\par \par \uc2 My social media channels are among the most interactive in the world, and I believe that today, we have about 40 percent of the population who has not yet expressed their voting intentions, and most of the voters we believe will vote for me during the elections.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Why is there no FOX News in Brazil? CNN is here. You got over 50 million votes in the last election. CNN is a political player here. So is Globo, but there is no TV channel for your voters?\par \par \uc2 BOLSONARO (through translator): Well, if I could, you know, launch an appeal to you, I can only say that you will be the most welcome in Brazil. You will be an excellent counterpart to the other vehicles or outlets.\par \par \uc2 There are very few media outlets that are really unbiased in Brazil. That's something we need and we do have one program in the Javanpa Network (ph) called "The Dots in the I's." "The Dots in the I's" or "The Dots on the I's", and they're excellent. They really showcase the good things going on in this country.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So you find yourself in a place where the permanent bureaucracy here in Brasilia, the state-owned companies, the media, leaders in countries around Brazil are all opposed to you. You stand effectively alone. Are you bothered by that? Or how do you deal with that?\par \par \uc2 BOLSONARO (through translator): Brazil is an economic powerhouse in South America. The 10 countries with which we have political, geopolitical, physical borders are not that economically strong as compared to Brazil. We are what you might describe as a cherry on the cake.\par \par \uc2 If Brazil goes down or collapses, the whole of South America will go down and be colored red, if you understand me, and it will certainly of course be a country aligned with other ideologies outside of Brazil and it will establish a wonderful bloc, "wonderful" between quotation marks, and they will be able to impose their will on the world.\par \par \uc2 Brazil remains a democracy, but we do run a serious risk of collapsing.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: It was the COVID pandemic that revealed to Bolsonaro really is. Bolsonaro did what our leaders refused to do during COVID, he thought for himself. He didn't let \uc2 Tony Fauci\uc2  or Klaus Schwab make decisions for Brazil. He did what he believed was in the best interest of his own country.\par \par \uc2 He declared there will be no national lockdown in Brazil during COVID. He refused to take the COVID shot himself having already recovered from the virus, and he raised concerns about vaccinating children. A fascinating story.\par \par \uc2 Bolsonaro explains why he did all this after the break.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Bolsonaro is one of the very few world leaders, certainly the only leader of a big country in the West who refused to destroy his own nation's economy in response to COVID. He also raised questions about the mandatory vaccination of children. Why are we doing this? He asked, "Shut up," they said,\par \par \uc2 Bolsonaro himself did not take the COVID shot. He had already recovered from COVID and believed in natural immunity. It turned out to be a smart decision.\par \par \uc2 We asked him about all these decisions during our conversation.\par \par \uc2 Here it is.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Why didn't you take the vaccine?\par \par \uc2 BOLSONARO (through translator): When the virus actually hit strongly in March 2020, people began to seek out the vaccine, of course, against the virus. And I too, of course, sought a medication because we began to see cases surfacing. We started seeing the number of cases begin to go up.\par \par \uc2 Now, someone who contracts the virus like I did, I mean, the vaccine doesn't really help. I mean, you don't take a vaccine if you have already been contaminated.\par \par \uc2 The vaccine would be innocuous. You should rather take the medication. And in Brazil, of course, I studied the issue. I called other countries, including in Sub Saharan Africa and Brazilian doctors and physicians, because there were people out there who either did not catch the virus or when they did catch the virus, the virus was not strong enough to send them to the hospital or to kill them.\par \par \uc2 And in Brazil, we saw the emergence of two medications that began to be used more widely. I myself took them when contaminated, but the global pressure all over the world, from the media outlets, from the pharmaceutical companies. I mean, they were all against the early treatment, they actually focused on the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 I read \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 's contract and one of the clauses said, "We shall take no responsibility whatsoever for any side effect arising from the vaccine." I became concerned about that.\par \par \uc2 Congress in Brazil decided to vote and pass a piece of legislation saying that \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  or any other pharmaceutical company would not take responsibility for any side effects arising from the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 We also had information, including from the \uc2 US FDA\uc2 , that several side effects are likely to emerge this year or next year in the foreseeable future.\par \par \uc2 So the concern, as mentioned by many doctors was that people who were infected by the virus were already immune, and did not have to take the vaccine. That was my case. That's why I did not take the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 But I did purchase vaccines for all Brazilians. I did not demand that people be vaccinated. I respected individual freedom. Each one was free to vaccinate or not and I believe that about 20 percent of the Brazilian population decided not to take the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 As I said before, maybe I was the only Head of State in the world who did not accept restrictive measures or was against restrictive measures, and perhaps one of the few heads of state in the world who did not take the vaccine because I had already contracted the virus.\par \par \uc2 The left was so worried about taking me out of office that they wanted me to take the vaccine. And I said, "Well, let me die. Just let me die then and choose my policy."\par \par \uc2 In South America, we are the one country that best addressed the issue involving the need for vaccines and we very properly and adequately equipped our hospitals with equipment and medications, and I believe we have pretty much turned the page there.\par \par \uc2 And based on the studies that we have available outside of Brazil, many deaths could have been avoided had there not been so much pressure on the part of the mainstream media against early treatment.\par \par \uc2 Early last year, I sent a team to Israel, a team of Brazilian experts to Israel to look into the nasal spray solution that they had developed on an experimental basis. I was highly criticized, and we weren't able to make progress in that negotiation.\par \par \uc2 Last month, a large Brazilian company published a news article indicating that nasal sprays are currently a very successful solution against COVID today.\par \par \uc2 So, you are technically allowed, of course, to take an experimental vaccine, which was the case in the past, but not the nasal spray?\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: I think you're the only world leader to admit not taking the vaccine, that's for sure. Why would \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  or any pharma company have liability protection against the side effects of their own drugs? Why would your Congress allow them to have that?\par \par \uc2 BOLSONARO (through translator): The population was appalled. They were desperate and afraid of the virus, especially the elderly population that also had some kind of disease or comorbidity, as a result of which Congress decided to pass a law to that effect.\par \par \uc2 We regretted really, because today in hindsight, you know, we see in studies, you know, conducted outside of Brazil that perhaps two-thirds of deaths could have been avoided in Brazil and in the world.\par \par \uc2 I mean, take Sub Saharan Africa. In Sub Saharan Africa, they take ivermectin to fight river blindness, as well as hydroxychloroquine to fight malaria. Because the number of deaths was very low and the HDI was pretty low, one of the lowest in the world, the natural conclusion was that those medications could somehow also help fight the virus and the effects there.\par \par \uc2 We regret the pressure that took place and perhaps due to the economic power of pharmaceutical companies, I mean, they went on and invested in vaccines.\par \par \uc2 And today you see, you know, people who have taken the third, the fourth dose of the vaccine, and they still contract the virus and die.\par \par \uc2 We have a lot of, say stranded vaccines in Brazil. In Brazil, a considerable portion of the population did not want to take the booster. I understand that to be their right. I support individual freedom.\par \par \uc2 As I said before, we are sorry, we regret all the deaths, but I believe many deaths could have been avoided through early treatment. Much is said about lack of scientific evidence about those two medications for COVID. It is true, but they were useful for other things.\par \par \uc2 I mean, very often drugs or medications are discovered by chance. During World War Two, for example, due to a lack of medication, soldiers were given coconut water in their vein, and they survived.\par \par \uc2 As I said before, very often medications are discovered out of accident or you know, sheer chance, including medications against to treat sexual impotence, for example.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Viagra. So --\par \par \uc2 BOLSONARO: Cialis.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Where do you think the COVID virus came from?\par \par \uc2 BOLSONARO (through translator): Well, allegedly from a laboratory on the other side of the world, but no deep investigation or no in-depth investigation has been conducted.\par \par \uc2 It would seem that COVID has proved to be of interest for many people in the world. Many heads of state ended up imposing their will and they felt the taste of dictatorship.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, State governance felt the taste of acting as dictators by mandating that people should stay at home and shutting down shops, and not allowing people to go to school if they had not been vaccinated. So they felt that power in their hands. They could do everything during COVID.\par \par \uc2 And more importantly, when it came to the public will itself, I mean, many things could be purchased by governors and mayors, although many of them are the vast majority are honest, they were nevertheless able to buy just about anything without much of a sense of responsibility.\par \par \uc2 So that taste of not being accountable for your actions during COVID is something that flourished among many top officials in Brazil.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: The left in Brazil, just like the left in the United States is intent on disarming the civilian population, it makes them more obedient. But it doesn't make the country safer and Bolsonaro proved that by loosening his country's gun laws and thereby lowering Brazil's murder rate by quite a bit.\par \par \uc2 That's straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 KEVIN CORKE, FOX NEWS CHANNEL WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: Welcome to "FOX News Live." I'm Kevin Corke in Washington.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court issuing a major blow to the Clean Air Act. In a six-three ruling, the High Court says the law does not give the \uc2 EPA\uc2  broad authority to regulate power plant emissions. Critics calling that decision a major step in the wrong direction.\par \par \uc2 Delta Air Lines\uc2  pilots picketing outside airports across the country, their calls for higher wages and more time off comes as thousands of flights are either delayed or cancelled ahead of the very busy Fourth of July weekend.\par \par \uc2 Texas love triangle murder suspect, Kaitlin Armstrong has been arrested in Costa Rica ending a 43-day international manhunt for Armstrong, who is facing charges in the May 11th killing of Anna Moriah Wilson. Wilson, you may remember was romantically linked to Armstrong's boyfriend.\par \par \uc2 I'm Kevin Corke in Washington.\par \par \uc2 Now back to more TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: For decades, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  freely admitted that the Roe v. Wade decision was bad law and inherently extreme, "I don't like the Supreme Court decision on abortion. I think it went too far. I don't think that a woman has the sole right to say what should happen to her body." Which makes sense because you can't create a baby without a man. So, why is it not a man's issue, too? "Shut up," they screamed.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has changed his view. Now, he will say precisely what they tell him to say. Today, he attacked the overturning of Roe v. Wade. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (D), PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: We have the strongest economy in the world. Our inflation rates are lower than other nations in the world.\par \par \uc2 The one thing that has been destabilizing is the outrageous behavior of the \uc2 Supreme Court of the United States\uc2  on overruling not only Roe v. Wade, but essentially challenging the right to privacy.\par \par \uc2 We've been a leader in the world in terms of personal rights and privacy rights and it is a mistake, in my view, for the Supreme Court to do what it did.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: "We are a leader in the world in terms of personal rights." Unless you criticize \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on the internet, in which case the \uc2 FBI\uc2  may wind up at your house, but free speech is no longer a personal right nor a self-defense.\par \par \uc2 So here in Brazil, it is still in mostly pro-life country. It is still mostly a Christian country, but the left here would very much like to change that. "Babies are