ubpoena to provide documents as part of an investigation into his business organization.\par \par \uc2 A former Texas state trooper and military veteran will be able to continue with his wrongful termination case after the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  ruled in his favor over claims he was forced out of his job when he returned from Army service in Iraq.\par \par \uc2 The justices ruled in a five to four vote that Army veteran Le Roy Torres' rights to employment were under a federal law that was enacted in 1994 in the wake of the Persian Gulf War for returning service members.\par \par \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  joins the Supreme Court tomorrow officially, she'll be sworn in as Justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  retires. Jackson will be the first black female justice.\par \par \uc2 There are conflicting signs coming from the Biden administration tonight in the aftermath of the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturning the Roe versus Wade abortion decision.\par \par \uc2 Chief Washington correspondent Mike Emanuel takes a look.\par \par \uc2 MIKE EMANUEL, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CHIEF WASHINGTON CORRESPONDENT (voice-over): Some prominent progressives are pushing the White House to take action by setting up abortion clinics in states where it is now illegal on land owned by the federal government that could include national parks.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. ALEXANDRIA OCASIO-CORTEZ (D-NY): I'll start with the babiest of the babiest of the baby steps. Open abortion clinics on federal lands in Red States right now.\par \par \uc2 SEN. ELIZABETH WARREN (D-MA): It also means asking the president of United States to make abortion as available as possible, including using federal lands.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: The health and human services secretary sounded open to the idea of trying to reassure pro-choice Americans. The Biden administration is looking for a federal response.\par \par \uc2 XAVIER BECERRA\uc2 , UNITED STATES SECRETARY OF HEALTH AND HUMAN SER