ect, for the steering wheel.\par \par \uc2 And wait, there is more, because according to CNN's Shimon Prokupecz, "A secret service official said that Tony Ornato denies telling Cassidy Hutchinson that Trump grabbed the steering wheel, or an agent in the first place".\par \par \uc2 I can't wait to see that surprise hearing Liz. And as their surprise witness testimony blows up in their faces, there's another problem for the Democrats. It turns out the voters just don't care about this January 6 charade.\par \par \uc2 A new \uc2 CBS\uc2  poll finds that the lowest number of voters polled consider investigating January 6, a high priority, while most consider it a low priority.\par \par \uc2 Wow. All the while the bad news keeps streaming in for the Democrats. More than a million voters in 43 states have now officially switched their party registration to the GOP in just one year. But don't worry, because the Democrats and their media supporters are hoping abortion is going to galvanize all the suburbanites and save the Democrats from an midterm route. Well, unlikely.\par \par \uc2 According to the AP, "Nowhere is the shift more pronounced and more dangerous for the Democrats than in the suburbs, where well educated swing voters who turned against Trump's Republican Party in recent years appear to be swinging back."\par \par \uc2 And just when you thought, things couldn't get any more dire for the Democrats, she's back.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING, CBS HOST: Do you miss the day to day of politics? Is there any scenario in your brain, you would think I want to get back in?\par \par \uc2 HILLARY CLINTON, 67TH UNITED STATES SECRETARY OF STATE: No. But I miss it. I miss it.\par \par \uc2 KING: No scenario in 2024 even remotely consider?\par \par \uc2 CLINTON: I can't imagine it. I really can't. But--\par \par \uc2 KING: Just got to know.\par \par \uc2 CLINTON: Well, but what I can imagine is staying as active and outspoken as I can.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That's right. While Hillary plays coy, she's out doing the media rounds, auditioning clearly to run in place of old Joe. She's vibrant. She's strong, right? Why can't she do it?\par \par \uc2 Now, doesn't it sound like a Democratic presidential candidate to you?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CLINTON: I've been saying for quite some time, I think the filibuster is - should be eliminated at the very least for constitutional questions, like voting rights, like a woman's constitutional rights to make decisions about her own body. This is going to, I hope, wake up a lot of Americans. Women are going to die, Gayle. Women will die.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Is that going to go on the button? Vote Hillary, women are going to die.\par \par \uc2 All right. The leftist media are already assembling their Hillary amen corner. Chris Cillizza at CNN is gushing the whispers of Hillary Clinton 2024 has started. And John Ellis is raving, now is her moment.\par \par \uc2 And being the political sage that Hillary is with no concern at all for the voters, she's betting it all on Jan 6th.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CLINTON: I think these hearings have been incredibly powerful. I hope the justice department is paying attention. I hope in these midterm elections, candidates and the Democratic Party pay attention. If there were ever a time to vote and to vote literally for your rights and our future, it's this midterm.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Literally.\par \par \uc2 Now, the woman is now and always has been a complete and total fraud. No one cares about this side show. They care about the fact that they're getting poorer every day that Biden is in office.\par \par \uc2 So Americans out there, you hear it right? You feel it? In their own way, they're begging for relief. They want their old country back. They want clean, safe streets. They want a situation where parents aren't worried that their kids are going to die from fentanyl, where families can actually, heaven forbid, afford a summer vacation. And where optimism about the future living here in this incredible country of ours is shared across a broader array of demographic groups. That's the America we love and we all deserve.\par \par \uc2 The January 6 hearings, the abortion scare mongering, the Hillary revival, none of it will add up to a better America. And Democrats don't even care, they never have. And Americans, they are onto them. The shiny objects have lost their luster. And the bad acting, it's just not funny anymore. It's just bad. And soon, this show will be shut down for good. And that's the 'Angle'.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Mollie Hemingway, editor-in-chief at The Federalist, Fox News contributor; and \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , former senior adviser to President Trump, founder of America First Legal.\par \par \uc2 Mollie, let's start in reverse order of the shiny objects that we discussed. Let's start first with Hillary Clinton emerging on the scene this week. Kind of playing coy with 2024. But I think it sounded like, without a doubt to me, Hillary is back in the game.\par \par \uc2 MOLLIE HEMINGWAY, EDITOR-IN-CHIEF, THE FEDERALIST: Yes. She's not known for subtlety. So it didn't come off coy. And it's really a sign of desperation on both the part of the Democrat party, but also \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , that they're trying to get the gang back together to have another round of things.\par \par \uc2 She was a terrifically bad candidate in 2016. Forgetting to visit the state of Wisconsin, being so unlikable that Americans really could not envision - so many Americans couldn't envision voting for her. But it really is a testament to how dire the Democrat party's situation is right now. That they are - they don't have a good bench and they are looking for someone who at least seemed more competent than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  does.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And the DNC chair, Stephen, tried to spin the Democrats' dire situation this way. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JAMIE HARRISON, DNC CHAIRMAN: We are seeing right now, an energy and an activism, particularly amongst women that we have not seen since the election of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And the march - women's march, we have to make sure that we push back against these Republican efforts to take away American rights.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Stephen, The Cook Political Report today came out with an analysis of eight new races, six of them are now pointing toward the Republicans. That's an addition to the other 30 or 35, or so. I think, they think maybe 25 seats so far for the Republicans as a pickup. But I don't know what fantasyland he's living in. But this doesn't seem like it's going in their direction.\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN MILLER\uc2 , "AMERICA FIRST LEGAL" FOUNDER: Well, they are right. That they are energizing woman to run as fast and as far as they can from the Democratic Party and into the arms of Republican candidates.\par \par \uc2 I mean, you saw history being made when Congresswoman Flores won in the 84 percent Democrat Latino district and won convincingly in a special election. The first Mexican born Congresswoman in the United States of America. All the Democrats have to offer is this circus show of conspiracy theories and witch hunts on January 6.\par \par \uc2 And now this new immediately debunked James Bond fantasy and opening - write about this crazy story about trying to commandeer a vehicle that was debunked within 30 minutes of it being told. And then of course, they have this single issue of late-term abortion on demand through the ninth month. So we're saying we want to create more jobs, we want to create more opportunity, we want to create safety, we want to secure the border, we want to lower inflation. And all they're saying is, we've got January 6 and abortion clinics. That's it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And, Mollie, to Stephen's last point there. I want to move on to this disaster on the Hill today. This Cassidy Hutchison wasn't the only one caught lying.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. ADAM SCHIFF (D-CA): If you had any question about whether the President knew these people were armed, or that they were dangerous. I think it's pretty clear from that testimony today. He knew what a threat they posed, and yet he was insistent on marching to the Capitol at the point of potentially getting an altercation with his own secret service about it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Mollie, reaction to that from your old pal.\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: If Adam Schiff is saying something, it's a pretty good indication that it's not true. This committee has engaged in widespread manipulation of evidence. They are refusing to provide the testimony of people who dispute the narrative that they're trying to construct.\par \par \uc2 They are really running roughshod over our American ideals of what should happen when you accuse people of crimes, and whether there should be ability to make a defense, or have a cross examination. I mean, those rights are enshrined in the constitution and our congressional committees are supposed to honor that in the way that they conduct their hearings. That has not been the case since day one.\par \par \uc2 And today, this was just absurd. And I have to say, if you believed this absolutely ludicrous story from this person, even before it was disputed by everyone on the record, you should not be involved in politics, in journalism. And you should really think deeply about whether you're able to really analyze information at a level that you should.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. These are so-called journalists. Stephen, I've written in the Beast a few times, and I can't - I couldn't remember, if you could even reach across. Can you even reach that way to get - I couldn't remember, but it seemed the whole - no, the whole story seemed ridiculous. But you knew Cassidy Hutchinson, and what kind of a - I've met her a few times, but I didn't really have much contact. What kind of a person is she?\par \par \uc2 MILLER: She's an extremely junior low level aide. I don't think I ever had a conversation with her that I can at least recall of any substance or death.\par \par \uc2 But to Mollie's point, this is a workshop test for your sanity. If you heard this story, and you thought, Man, I believe every word of this. I'm going to go online and say something about it energetically, then something is wrong with you. Something is wrong with you, if you're that gullible, especially after five years of the hoaxes, and the witch hunts, and the fabrications.\par \par \uc2 People keep falling for it again and again and again and again. At what point do people just lose their credibility?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And, Mollie, did you notice she kept saying something, something to (inaudible) not admissible in any kind of real court? But she kept saying something to that effect, whether it was about Trump's reaction depends and the hanging chant - but I found it all, it was like she was auditioning for a seat at the view or the real staffers of Pennsylvania Avenue or so. It just seemed like an audition tape. That wasn't going well for her. God bless her. I mean, I don't know her well. But it just seemed bad.\par \par \uc2 HEMINGWAY: Well, I mean, when you have people coming out and saying that they did not, in fact, tell this information that she claimed that she had been told by them, it is probably wise of her to distance herself from her own testimony. But again, this is really the fault of the committee. There is not a single Republican appointed member of this committee. They are not engaged in any rights of minorities. They're not engaged in any back and forth on evidence.\par \par \uc2 They are lying and they've done it with really high level witnesses and it has massive implications, because the Department of Justice appears to just be following their lead in what they're choosing to prosecute and who they're choosing to target. This is a really serious attack on the country and on our norms.\par \par \uc2 And it's - I know a lot of people on the right are checking out because it is so absurd, but what they're doing is very damaging and very dangerous.\par \par \uc2 MILLER: Amen.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, I'm glad you said that. Stephen, they're trying to make her out to be like Alexander Vindman, right? Like she's the new Vindman for the - this latest chapter and the attacks on him.\par \par \uc2 MILLER: Well, if she tries to start a war in Europe, maybe she will be Alexander Vindman. But look, the bottom line here is that these secret service agents that we're seeing, according to news reports that are vociferously rebutting this, these are decades long, distinguished career nonpartisan law enforcement officers. It doesn't get more credible than that when it comes to rebutting, a fantastical fairytale.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Aside from the fact that it looks like she wanted to go down to Mar-a-Lago and work down there. And I guess she was next. I mean, she was on the manifest at one point. One of the staffers told me.\par \par \uc2 Mollie, Stephen, great to see you both.\par \par \uc2 And tonight is also primary night across the country. And our own Bret Baier is manning the touchscreen tonight to take us through some of the big primary contests. Bret, where are you taking us first, pray tell?\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: We'll take a little tour here. Hey, good evening, Laura. Let's start in the governor's races.\par \par \uc2 We've got five states with primaries tonight. We have to run offs, one special election. But let's go here to New York. The current incumbent winning, overwhelmingly not a surprise there. But the race is still ongoing on the Republican side.\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2  holding 41 percent. There's roughly 40 percent in. And Andrew Giuliani with 24.6. If you look at this, this is the area for Giuliani support, Brooklyn, Queens, the Bronx, Staten Island. He's leading in all of those places.\par \par \uc2 However, as you look at the state, Zeldin is well positioned. He had the endorsement of the state committee and Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , former vice president campaigning for him. Well, watch this with 40 percent in.\par \par \uc2 And let's head back out to Illinois. Here you have state senator Bailey, who is now declared but this has just happened. Senator - state senator \uc2 Darren Bailey\uc2 , he will face the current incumbent governor JB Pritzker.\par \par \uc2 And this is interesting. This is a Trump endorsement in over the past few days, the race flipped in the past few weeks. But as you can see, overwhelming his colors throughout here.\par \par \uc2 All right. Let's go back here and take you on a little tour of House races. We're talking Illinois. This Republican race pitted two Republican current incumbents against each other. It was a redistricting deal. This is the congressional district 15.\par \par \uc2 Not over yet, but it looks like the Trump-backed representative Mary Miller is going to beat Representative Davis here. It's not called yet, but it looks like it's heading that way. This is in the south and east of Illinois, this particular district.\par \par \uc2 OK. Let's head back here and head out to the Senate and go out to Colorado. And this has just been called. Joe O'Dea construction firm owner is now going to go up against the Democratic incumbent Michael Bennett. That'll be an interesting race of businessman. And Hanks was the more to the right candidate, who actually had the most votes in the GOP effort in Colorado. But O'Dea pulling this out pretty significantly. And that has now been called.\par \par \uc2 There's a number of races we're watching in House races that have yet to be called. But that's the overview across the country for you tonight, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Colorado is always a fascinating state, Bret. Still pretty purple. And that didn't surprise me, that race, but fascinating. We'll keep watching it. Thank you, Bret.\par \par \uc2 All right. We're going to keep an eye on all those races and make any big calls if we need to. But up next, the less casual racism as it relates to my old boss Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . Horace Cooper has a reaction. Plus, every single branch of the U.S. military is now under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  struggling to make its 2022 recruiting goal. Nice going, Joey.\par \par \uc2 Lieutenant Colonel Stu Scheller was just charged for calling for accountability over Afghanistan. He responds to this disturbing development in moments.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: If you read \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 ' concurrence, he said, Thank you f*** \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CLINTON: He is signaling as he often did. People --I went to law school with him. He's been a person of grievance for as long as I've known him, resentment, grievance, anger.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That's the woman who coined the vast right wing conspiracy comment. Yes, she's the one - pot kettle black, Hillary. And you wouldn't know Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  authored the Dobbs decision overturning Roe by the reaction from some of the most unhinged politicians in our midst.\par \par \uc2 So it's worth asking, what is driving their intense anger directed at my old boss? The lone black man on the court, \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Horace Cooper, co chair of Project 21. Horace, remember, back to 1991, and Justice Thomas' confirmation hearing when he made it clear that he believed they didn't like anyone like him because he refused to remain on their plantation. He didn't agree with them and their worldview, so he didn't count as a human being. And boy, all these years later, what he said, completely is still obviously true.\par \par \uc2 HORACE COOPER, PROJECT 21 CO-CHAIRMAN: You know, that's the very reason why Project 21 was created. We wanted to make sure that Americans understood that black Americans have conservative views, moderate views, liberal views. There's not a one-size-fits-all. That we come from all walks of life.\par \par \uc2 And that someone amazing as and as talented as \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  is, in fact, authentically black. The challenge from my perspective, as I see it, has been the American people embrace this idea. I don't have a lot of pushback with America.\par \par \uc2 I have a lot of pushback with the progressives. They act just like Democrats did during Jim Crow. Hey, black guy, stay in your lane, stay in your space. There's only certain things that you're supposed to be able to do. Ironically, 20th century Democrats (inaudible)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Stay in your side, stay in limitation. He called it a high tech lynching all those years ago, and they're still trying to do it to him.\par \par \uc2 And if you thought those attacks, by the way, Horace were pretty gross. Then there was Don Lemon and Jeffrey Toobin last night.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DON LEMON, CNN HOST: Why doesn't he feel the same about interracial marriage?\par \par \uc2 TOOBIN: Well, you know, look, let's not be coy about that. Everybody knows he's involved - he's married to a white woman.\par \par \uc2 LEMON: Still didn't mention it.\par \par \uc2 TOOBIN: I'm trying to be fair here, Don.\par \par \uc2 LEMON: And loving this as a couple years before Roe. I mean--\par \par \uc2 TOOBIN: No, I mean, look, it was a conspicuous absence.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Horace, it's a new low even for CNN, who can't get much low in the ratings.\par \par \uc2 COOPER: Well, you just probably tripled their audience by showing this clip. That --I was going to say the good news is, no one is actually watching CNN.\par \par \uc2 First point I want to make, though, is \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  is the leader of this court. This is \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  court. He's the intellectual leader, and what he has promised, and what he demonstrates is a fidelity to the Constitution. The left hates our Constitution.\par \par \uc2 Oh, you say no, that's not true. That's stretching it. They want to eliminate every state getting to senators. They want to eliminate the Electoral College. They want to get rid of our Supreme Court. They want to throw out the most wonderful, amazing document that has allowed liberty and free people to operate.\par \par \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  is its champion. Shame on those people for using racist names that would have been welcomed and normalized in the 1920s, 30s and 40s. And then to see them today on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , shame on them. And also, why hasn't our president said a word? Why haven't any of the Democrats said, let's come up with an argument. If you don't agree with \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , why the bigotry? Because it reveals who they really are.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes. And I'd say after all these years, his philosophy, his judicial philosophy is preeminent. They have no judicial philosophy, and they're losing. And they're angry and bitter. And he's one of the nicest, most hilarious, most awesome people.\par \par \uc2 COOPER: Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That everybody who clerked for him, but everyone on the court, I mean, all the justices, they love him. He is a great person and brilliant.\par \par \uc2 COOPER: It's a privilege to have him in your life, it's a privilege.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: You bet. To all of us. And Horace, thank you.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT, UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: We're committed to advancing transgender equality, in the classroom, on the playing field, at work and on military everywhere. Simply everywhere.\par \par \uc2 LLOYD AUSTIN\uc2 , SECRETARY OF DEFENSE: One of the things I want to do is make sure that I create as an inclusive environment as possible. Diversity is really important to us.\par \par \uc2 GENERAL \uc2 MARK MILLEY\uc2 , CHAIRMAN OF THE JOINT CHIEFS OF STAFF: I want to understand white rage, and I'm white. And I want to understand it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: After hearing all that, the next bit of news might come as little surprise.\par \par \uc2 According to NBC, "Every single branch of the U.S. military is now struggling to meet recruiting goals" With both a record low percentage of young Americans eligible to serve and an even tinier fraction willing to consider it.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Stu Scheller, a Marine Corps Lieutenant Colonel discharged after criticizing the military's Afghanistan withdrawal. He is also the author of "Crisis of Command." Stuart, this really is the chickens coming home to roost moment. I think you predicted it. I predicted it. They want to military to be like, I don't know, Harvard Law School, like a Thursday night seminar. It's no really different from any college campus.\par \par \uc2 LT. COL. STUART SCHELLER, (RET) AUTHOR, CRISIS OF COMMAND: Yes, Laura. Thanks for having me on. Bottom line, you alluded to it. This is not a recruitment problem. This is a problem with our senior leaders. Our senior leaders' inability to have courage, their hypocrisy, it's affecting all other things. You would think a young American would want to raise their right hand, support defend the Constitution, similar to your last guest talking about wanting to support and defend the Constitution and have trust in our senior military leaders. But our senior military leaders have demonstrated through action that we can't trust them. And you would be naive to think that a young American isn't getting online, going on the Internet, and seeing all the missteps that we can clearly see of our senior military leaders.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I was lucky enough to be at the Michael Murphy Navy SEAL Museum opening at Long Island today, and had a chance to meet so many incredible men and women in uniform and former SEALs and so forth, and looking at the wall of all of these special operators who gave their lives for this country, and I actually got angry. I got angry about what is happening to this military and all their sacrifice, and the families who are still sacrificing to this day. We owe them a lot, and a lot better than this.\par \par \uc2 SCHELLER: Yes, I actually just spent some time down in Texas with \uc2 Morgan\uc2  and Marcus Luttrell. I saw some pictures of Marcus Luttrell at the museum.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He was there today.\par \par \uc2 SCHELLER: And I was talking to Marcus, and he was talking about our generation born in the 70s and 80s that has been forged in fire through combat where our senior leaders have made consistent mistakes. But I think it's our time to step up and get us back on track to a constitutional mindset. We need leadership. We need courage. I think that is what the 22 election cycle is going to be about. That's what I'm dedicated to. And I think our senior leaders need to make up to the real problems right now.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We're going to need a new commander-in-chief for that, I think. Here is something else affecting recruitment and retention. Since the military's COVID-19 vax mended, over 5,000 military members were discharged for refusing to comply. Stuart, most of these people are in good health, a lot of them have already had COVID. How do we expect the military to meet their quotas when we are kicking out perfectly healthy men and women?\par \par \uc2 SCHELLER: Yes, Laura, I will tell you firsthand that those numbers are much larger, especially if you start going to the National Guard or the Reserves. You start getting into the 40,000 to 100,000. There's still a bunch of medical waivers that are making it hard for them to discharge. But the problem is much bigger than the 5,000 that you described. And it even is exacerbated by people coming in. Right now, we have a senator candidate in New Hampshire Don Bolduc, a former one star general. His kids went through ROTC and were told right at the end that they couldn't join because they weren't going to get vaccinated, and then they were told that they had to pay back the ROTC scholarship.\par \par \uc2 All of these servicemembers that have served for two decades in war, they made an individual medical choice not to get vaccinated. I don't care what your opinion is, but for you to say that they don't deserve an honorable discharge on the way out the door is criminal, and it's indicative of our lack of courage and hypocrisy in our senior military leadership.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Again, the message comes from the top, and Republicans are the ones who help fund all of this. So the Republicans have to, at some point, Lieutenant Colonel Scheller, they have to say no more, not a dime is going to go to this diversity, equity, inclusion nonsense, and then follow through on it. And they just have to. We appreciate you. We appreciate you and your book.\par \par \uc2 SCHELLER: Thank you, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We got our hands on a leaked video from a Department of Labor training session titled "The Power of Trans Inclusion in the Workforce." The exclusive video and Congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  is here in moments. Stay there.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: THE INGRAHAM ANGLE has exclusively obtained leaked footage from a Department of Labor panel about transgenderism. FOX's Matt Finn is in our west coast newsroom with all of the alarming details. Matt.\par \par \uc2 MATT FINN, FOX NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Hi, Laura. The video was obtained by a Congressional source and shows transactivists speaking at a Department of Labor webinar about how to provide safe and nurturing spaces for trans employees. One of the activists with the pronoun "she," "her," and "goddess," told attendees that some white men don't acknowledge trans identities and want to criminalize trans people.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: What we are dealing is really reclaiming all those identities that have always existed, right, but because of colonization and those cis white men not understanding and being confused about what they saw, like, well, you're either male or female, that's it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 FINN: Another trans activist said that if insurance companies will not lower copayments for gender reassignment surgeries, then she might go back to sex work to pay for it.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: If I go get elective surgery, top or bottom surgery, and my copayment is $4,000 and $5,000, $8,000, I might as well go pay for the surgery myself and back out into sex working if that's the case.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 FINN: Republican Congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  sent a letter to the Labor Secretary Martin Walsh on Monday requesting more information about the webinar and asking Walsh to investigate, writing, in part, "The conversation is entirely inappropriate, and the claims made are without any merit. It is shocking that \uc2 DOL\uc2  employees are using their time at work that have an open-ended partisan foreign consisting of abrasive social commentary." We have reached out to the Labor Department for response but so far have not heard back just yet. Laura?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Matt, thank you.\par \par \uc2 And joining me now is the aforementioned Florida Congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  who got his hands on this video. Congressman, now, what does any of this have to do with furthering the mission of the department? What am I missing here?\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 MATT GAETZ\uc2 , (R-FL): What's bizarre is that in the name of inclusion, our government is embracing the policies of exclusion. And it is really state-sponsored racism for your money to be used by the Department of Labor to try to say that all of society's flaws are the fault of white men. So I believe we have to expose these things when they happen. I believe when we retake the House, we have to actually use the power of the purse to stop this. And then when we retake the White House, we have to reorient these agencies where they actually work for people's freedoms. If the Department of Labor is going to be focused on pronouns instead of the freedom of people to actually work in our country, why even have a Department of Labor?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think that is a great question. That's what we should do is get rid of the whole department.\par \par \uc2 Now, I want to play another clip from this panel.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: For a long time, I had this trans identity, right, that did not allow me to center my femininity. And I often walked that line of looking androgynous. I have allowed myself to go completely into what I like to call my goddess mode. I am both male and female. I am just energy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Congressman, again, the purpose of the Labor Department, I shouldn't laugh. This is actually serious. Someone is paying for this somewhere along the line, I imagine. Maybe they do this for free around the country, but I doubt it, because a lot of these people get paid big money to be consultants in this arena, speaking of the goddesses and centering femininity and all these important Labor Department topics for birthing people.\par \par \uc2 GAETZ: I'm going to find out exactly how much this cost, because we may see a circumstance under divided government where we have to shut down the government in order to get what we need to secure the border or to de- wokify these agencies.\par \par \uc2 And if it comes to that, I at least want the American people to see the government that we are shutting down, literally people focusing more on pronouns than people and whether or not one has gone into goddess mode effectively probably doesn't inform on whether or not they are an effective worker in our society, in our economy. I remember the Trump economy where we had rising wages and success and actual labor that was prosperous. Now under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  we just have a weird Labor Department. That seems like a bad trade.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Matt, at some point I think the Republicans, more than just you and a few others saying this, actually have to start saying we are not spending any more money on this. We're not -- right now we could do that with the U.S. military, but there are too many establishment GOP-ers who would never touch a dime of military spending. But this is happening across every agency. It's one of the reasons why we are not recruiting up to the goals that we need for each branch of the military, as we just discussed. So this has got to be defunded across the board.\par \par \uc2 GAETZ: I do think we're going to have to bifurcate our analysis. There will be some agencies like the \uc2 Department of Defense\uc2  that we have to keep around, and they will have to be de-wokified. But there may be other agencies where the rot is so deep, like at the Department of Education, or the Department of Labor, or at the \uc2 EPA\uc2 , where we really can't salvage a meaningful government mission for our people. And the question is whether or not that Republicans will endeavor to fight on that and to expose it and to actually use the power of the purse.\par \par \uc2 Our friend \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  has a saying, when the Democrats are in power, the Republicans are the conservative party. And when the Republicans are in power, there is no conservative party. That is why these primaries you are reporting on tonight are so important, because we need the backup to have a spine to stop this, to shut it down and to actually make our government work for our people.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The establishment keeps failing. We don't want to reelect them. Congressman, thank you.\par \par \uc2 And some news out there in New York where our guest from last night, frequent guest on the show, Congressman \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2  just won the Republican primary for governor, and now he gets the chance to take on \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  this November. If Republicans really want to make a difference in this country, they need to fight everywhere. The empire state, it deserves a lot better than it has been getting, to say the least. And this is the beginning of a new start for New York.\par \par \uc2 But up next, two drug traffickers were arrested Friday for having enough fentanyl to kill millions of Americans, but because it happened in California, they are back out on the street just days later. Isn't that lovely. The sheriff whose deputies made the original arrest is furious. He's livid. He's here next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Take a look at this photo. What you are seeing is 150,000 fentanyl pills seized Friday by police in California. That is enough to kill millions of Americans. Two suspected drug traffickers were arrested and booked on numerous charges. But it's California, so you can guess what happen next. They were released just days later. They had enough drugs to kill millions and they are back out on the streets. By the way, on their own recognizance after a risk assessment was done by this judge, Tulare County Court Commissioner Mikki Verissimo. Joining me now is Sheriff Mike Boudreaux of Tulare County. Sheriff, you said that you weren't even consulted on this decision and this risk assessment?\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF MIKE BOUDREAUX, TULARE COUNTY, CALIFORNIA: Yes, that's right. We have about 600,000 people that live in our county. Right through the center of it are two major highways that have heavy drug trafficking. And as you know, fentanyl is incredibly dangerous, and we come across 150,000 pills of fentanyl. This case went before a judge through the probation department on a risk assessment, never notifying us at the Sheriff's office, and then ordered a court ordered release of these two people.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Sheriff, CDC data now is showing that this synthetic opioid death count, primarily through fentanyl, they have gone up 91 percent since 2019. So it just takes your breath away. Obviously, the lockdowns and all of that exacerbated it. Everyone is locked up, things were going crazy. But this drug has essentially become a WMD, and we are still not allowing those selling in to just goat free on their own recognizance after this bogus risk assessment? This is maddening.\par \par \uc2 BOUDREAUX: Let me tell you this, law enforcement leaders in the state of California are frustrated. This soft on crime approach that we see from the governor's office in Sacramento and our legislators, we are completely frustrated. I sit on the California State Sheriffs Association executive board, and I speak with law enforcement leaders all up and down the state. And we have to stop this soft on crime approach, because there's no deterrent to the criminals, no deterrent to the drug trafficking organizations, and no deterrent to the cartels. As a matter of fact, what we sent the message was, is the risk is very low and that your reward is very big. We've got to quit doing that in California. We want our criminals to be held to the justice, and in our court system, we have failed to do so in our California system.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The people of California, they are going with Newsom. They're staying with Newsom. Speaking of him --\par \par \uc2 BOUDREAUX: Let me tell you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Go ahead.\par \par \uc2 BOUDREAUX: Yes, I think that that is changing in California. I think that the message for California is not what we're portrayed as. I can you that Central Valley is largely supportive of more of a conservative justice approach, and that the citizens of California are getting fed up. When we see these criminals running into stores, when we see the borders open freely to allow this type of drug and guns, sex trafficking, human trafficking to freely come across our border, the citizens of California are beginning to get fed up.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Wow. Long since overdue in the Central Valley. Good people there, and they've been hit by this criminal wave of drug trafficking. Sheriff, we appreciate you, and it must be incredibly frustrating for all of you and your men and women out there, but we appreciate you.\par \par \uc2 Congressman Adam Schiff today should listen to Adam Schiff of, let's say, 2005 or so. The Last Bite will explain it.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now when you hear this clip from the now fork-tongued Adam Schiff, ask yourself, did he fall on his head at some point in the last 17 years or so?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. ADAM SCHIFF, (D-CA) JANUARY 6TH SELECT COMMITTEE: This protracted war against the judicial branch will only denigrate both Congress and the courts. Why does it matter if the Congress and the courts are at war? Because if the separations of powers has eroded and an independent judiciary is impaired, decisions become increasingly politicized, public confidence in the rule of law erodes, and people begin taking law into their own hands.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What changed, Adam? What?\par \par \uc2 Remember your USA made Freedom Matters gear, all on LauraIngraham.com, great stuff there for the Fourth of July and all the summer. Honor Flight Network gets all the donations in June.\par \par \uc2 "GUTFELD!" is next.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by Uni