abortion on those who don't want it. What a disgrace.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, I'm standing in the middle of what by American standards is a poor country, Brazil, and poor people have huge families and no one is forcing them to and it seems like that's true around the world.\par \par \uc2 People who don't have much know the one thing they have is the thing that matters most, which is children. So how can our leaders pretend to speak for them when they want the opposite of what our leaders are pushing?\par \par \uc2 CAMOSY: My previous book was entitled "Resisting Throwaway Culture." You may remember that book.\par \par \uc2 There is a throwaway culture here that the privileged classes, the classes that you just talked about benefit from, but who gets thrown away, who gets discarded, who does not get hurt. It's precisely the folks that you and your show really care about.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes. And we do. Charles Camosy, I appreciate your coming on. As always, I know we'll see you again. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CAMOSY: Thank you, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So if you go to any college campus, you'll learn the one thing they hate on college campuses is colonialism, and yet, you are seeing colonialism at a scale that dwarfed anything that happened in the 19th Century and China is the colonial power.\par \par \uc2 It is happening here in Latin America, it is happening here in Brazil, turning Latin American nations into colonies of China. What does that mean for us? And why is no one noticing this?\par \par \uc2 We'll be right back from Rio de Janeiro.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: We are back from Rio de Janeiro, Brazil.\par \par \uc2 You often hear that drugs are a problem in South America, and they certainly are an enormous problem. But they're also an enormous problem in the United States in a different way.\par \par \uc2 Over a hundred thousand Americans died of drug ODs just last year. But our ruling class ignores this completely. The people who are supposed to be helping are letting it happen. In fact, they are letting drug traffickers go free.\par \par \uc2 No one has covered this more assiduously than our Bill Melugin who has been following one extraordinary case in the State of California, which he has for us tonight. Hey, Bill.\par \par \uc2 BILL MELUGIN, FOX NEWS CHANNEL NATIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Hey, Tucker, that's right.\par \par \uc2 In a stunning turn of events here in California, two men who were arrested with enough fentanyl to kill millions of people were both released from custody just hours after their arrest.\par \par \uc2 The Tulare County Sheriff's Office recovered 150,000 fentanyl pills off two men during a traffic stop on Friday night. It's a potentially life-saving bust worth about $750,000.00 on the streets.\par \par \uc2 Two men were charged in the bust, 25-year-old Jose Zendejas and 19-year-old Benito Madrigal, but they were both released from Tulare County Jail on their own recognizance as a result of a Court Order from a Judge following a risk assessment.\par \par \uc2 Now, the Tulare County Sheriff is irate about the release of these alleged fentanyl traffickers. He says the so-called risk assessment was done behind the scenes. He was never contacted or notified and he says California's justice system is a failure.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MIKE BOUDREAUX, TULARE COUNTY SHERIFF: I could not believe that we had 150,000 fentanyl pills, one of the most dangerous epidemics that is facing our nation today with people in custody, that we may potentially be able to impact the future of this type of drug trafficking organization and/or cartels in California, in my county, and we let them go.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MELUGIN: And Tucker, most of that fentanyl is pouring in through the open Southern border where there was just a mass casualty human smuggling event.\par \par \uc2 Take a look at this video. San Antonio yesterday afternoon, at least 50 illegal immigrants were found dead in the back of a tractor trailer subjected to the blistering Texas summer heat in a human smuggling attempt gone wrong, one of the deadliest immigration related incidents in recent history.\par \par \uc2 And Tucker, the White House was asked about those deaths today. Press Secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  responded by claiming that the border is closed.\par \par \uc2 We send it back to you.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Grotesque. No one has covered this better than you have. Bill Melugin, thank you.\par \par \uc2 MELUGIN: Thanks.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So one of the many reasons we came to Brazil this week is to take a closer look at China's effort to control Brazil and its economy. Roughly 70 percent of China's global infrastructure investments in Brazil have centered on its energy sector. Once you control a country's energy, you control that country.\par \par \uc2 Increasingly, China has been doing the same thing in our country, the United States and the Biden administration has been encouraging. It has been encouraging China to funnel money towards so-called renewable energy sources.\par \par \uc2 Now, they call this the Green New Deal, but in effect, what the Biden administration is pushing is dependence on China. Total dependence on Chinese made solar panels and batteries. Chinese control of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Salena Zito is a journalist who has looked carefully into this story and joins us tonight to explain. Salena, thanks so much for coming on.\par \par \uc2 So just starting with the premise: If you control a country's energy supply, you control that country. Where is the United States moving?\par \par \uc2 SALENA ZITO, JOURNALIST: Well, our problem here is that everything within the Biden administration's approach to how we fuel our country, right, their whole climate change agenda. It makes us reliant on China for all those sources of energy.\par \par \uc2 So take for instance solar panels. They aren't manufactured, at least in to a degree that is necessary in the United States. They are mainly manufactured in Southeast Asia and in China.\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, the Biden administration recently put a tariff on them. So all these solar panels that are across the country just have the rod sticking out, there are no panels because we couldn't get them from China. He recently lifted that, however, it's going to take a year or two for those panels to get here.\par \par \uc2 And the problem with the panels are not only are they made in China, but even if we made them here in the United States, we need the raw minerals from China to make the panels, so they wouldn't -- again, we are totally relying on China to make our energy sustainable under this climate change mandate.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Yes. So it's a Chinese takeover of the United States. I mean, I don't know why we don't call it that, and I think going forward, we will.\par \par \uc2 Salena Zito, thank you for reporting on that.\par \par \uc2 ZITO: Thanks for having me.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So, there is no greater proof of the rule that it plays depends upon the quality of its leadership than the City of Chicago, one of the great cities in this country, a city that built this country completely falling apart, because its mayor is deranged, literally deranged. It's not an overstatement.\par \par \uc2 Racist, incompetent, stupid, and worse. Just went on a completely bizarre rant, screaming the F-word at \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Why exactly? We've got some ideas, straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 KEVIN CORKE, FOX NEWS CHANNEL WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: Welcome to "FOX News Live." I'm Kevin Corke in Washington.\par \par \uc2 Ghislaine Maxwell has been sentenced to 20 years in prison for helping financier, Jeffrey Epstein sexually abuse underage girls. Prosecutors say Epstein who allegedly killed himself back in 2019 while awaiting trial couldn't have