pportunity to even be in critical care.\par \par \uc2 I'm floored by the culture of death that exists in the City of Chicago.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: It is a culture of death. That didn't happen in Uvalde. CNN didn't cover it live. It happens every week in Chicago. It's a disaster. Things are falling apart and the people who live there don't deserve it.\par \par \uc2 But instead of doing anything to fix it, the Mayor of Chicago, \uc2 Lori Lightfoot\uc2  puts on one irrelevant performance after another. Here is her most recent.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MAYOR LORI LIGHTFOOT (D), CHICAGO, ILLINOIS: Now, we know what happened with the Supreme Court yesterday, but if you read \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 ' concurrence, he said -- thank you. [Bleep] \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . [Bleep].\par \par \uc2 He thinks that we are going to stand idly by when they take our rights, our right to marry, our right to have children.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: "Eff Clarence Thomas," she screams to a crowd of the most privileged pampered people in the City of Chicago, ignoring the people who are dying.\par \par \uc2 And then in a follow up tweet, to let you know how tough and liberated she is. \uc2 Lori Lightfoot\uc2  wrote this, "I said what I meant." Okay, but what about Chicago exactly?\par \par \uc2 Raymond Lopez lives in Chicago. He's an alderman there. He is running to replace \uc2 Lori Lightfoot\uc2 . It's our fervent prayer he does. He joins us in the meantime.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Lopez, thanks so much for coming on.\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND LOPEZ (D), CHICAGO ALDERMAN: Thanks, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: I mean, look, she can have any view she wants about the Supreme Court. I mean, who cares? But what about the city she is supposed to be running? Why is she wasting a second on performances like this?\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ: \uc2 Lori Lightfoot\uc2  is the embodiment, Tucker, of toxic politics and she practices it