ment right now. Thanks, you, Susan, very much. Here comes THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 DANA PERINO: Hello everyone. I'm Dana Perino along with Judge Jeanine Pirro, Geraldo Rivera, Jesse Watters, and Kat Timpf. It's 5:00 in New York City. This is THE FIVE.\par \par \uc2 President Biden's border policies being blamed for a horrific loss of life in Texas. At least 51 migrants found dealt from the sweltering heat stacked on top of one another in an abandoned tractor trailer that had no working air conditioning or even water, in what appears to be one of the most deadly incidents of smuggling across the southern border.\par \par \uc2 Three suspects are in custody following the terrible discovery. Every month there's been record breaking numbers at the border. And Border Agents constantly say they're overwhelmed by the surge and they do not feel supported.\par \par \uc2 Texas Governor Greg Abbott tweeting this, "These deaths are on Biden. They are a result of his deadly open border policies." And Senator Ted Cruz tweeting, "How many more people have to die before Dems give a damn?" The White House firing back at critics.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: The fact of the matter is the border is closed, which is in part why you see people trying to make this dangerous journey using smuggling networks. We are going to stay focused on the facts and making sure that we hold these smugglers accountable.\par \par \uc2 (END AUDIO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Alright, Jesse, is it fair to blame President Biden's policies?\par \par \uc2 JESSE WATTERS, FOS NEWS HOST: I believe it is fair. He's a snob from Delaware. He doesn't even consider Texas a part of the country. He thinks it's our gas station. That's where they killed Kennedy. It's where they killed the ozone layer and they're a bunch of Neanderthals. That's how he really feels about Texas.\par \par \uc2 He's been to China in the last 40 years more times than he's be