heriffs can try. The governor of California, Governor Newsom could maybe try if he cared. But nobody is doing it. They could actually have an effect here, but for some reason, they are not doing it.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: The reason they won't is because it would require them to police the borders which is where it's coming and they don't want to police the border.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Or at least work with Mexico. I have a dream, you know, of a Mexican secret service, special forces and ours working together to go after the cartels because they have cross border impact obviously. It's killing our kids.\par \par \uc2 TIMPF: I think it is important to point out that fentanyl is a legitimate drug that has legitimate specific medical uses. That's not what's killing people. It's surprise fentanyl that's killing people.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes. Exactly.\par \par \uc2 TIMPF: And as we have crack down on opiate prescriptions, there's a direct correlation with overdoes deaths because there are people who need opiates, who want to seek out prescription opiates who have had that crackdown on. So, then those people go to the black market.\par \par \uc2 It's not just opiates. It's also with methamphetamine. When we started, you know, maybe certainly good intentions, we started to crack down on sudafed because of the meth problems. So, now more of the meth is coming from Mexico. People don't know what's in it. More people are dying.\par \par \uc2 And a lot of the efforts that we have made to sort of crack down on smugglers have ironically pushed smugglers more towards fentanyl because it's obviously, I don't have any smuggling experience but just basic logic, easier to smuggle something that's more potent because it's a smaller amount than something that's larger.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: What about a massive P.R. campaign? \uc2 MTV\uc2 , social media, everything --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: What, "Just Say No?"\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: That prince died. Prince had more money than God. He could buy any drug he wants, but he died of fentanyl.\par \par \uc2 TIMPF: I think years of statistics prove that that's not working. I think that with the direct correlation between not letting people get, you know, having legal options for opiates and this. It's -- we have years of data on this.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: I could see-- I could -- I'd rather than surrender. I can see, you know, the president working with, I don't know, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , pick your Republican. You know, or maybe a younger generation making the pitch that this is death. This fentanyl kills you.\par \par \uc2 You know, I understand the legality or the use of it as prescriptions, but my goodness, look at what has happened. I mean, 75,000 people dying from it, this is obviously --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Half the time they don't even know fentanyl is in it.\par \par \uc2 TIMPF: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: They stamp it as Xanax.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: That's the point. That's the point.\par \par \uc2 TIMPF: That's exactly right.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Every pill can kill. I like that. I like that. Up next, she's back. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  lashing out at the Supreme Court for its decision on abortion.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCILA BREAK)\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Democrats and the media going scorched earth over the end of Roe and unleashing their fury on Supreme Court Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . It comes as the left ramps up their hate-fueled attacks on pro-lice centers and protests at the homes of the justices. Actor Samuel L. Jackson going low by calling Justice Thomas, quotes, "Uncle Clarence." \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  and others also lobbing these bombs. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HILLARY CLINTON\uc2 , FOREMER PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: I went to law school with him. He's been a person of grievance for as long as I've known him. Resentment, grievance, anger.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: If you read \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  (inaudible) he said, thank you (BL