uc2 PIRRO: OK, wait a minute, wait a minute. He said that we're talking about substantive due process. Substantive due process is where there is an explicit right, the right to bear arms --\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Right, right.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: -- not implicit. Not --\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: So --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Let me finish.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: The constitution doesn't say anything about contraception.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Not implied. But he said -- he said that's not what this is about.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: He did not say that.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: He did say that.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: He did not say that.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: And in the end, if you want to talk about racism, the truth is, why was he called Uncle Clarence?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Racism is -- racism, that is a diverting --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No, you just said it wasn't racism.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: -- that is a diversion from the issue. The issue is --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You just said it wasn't racism.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: -- this man has threatened your birth control. This man has threatened your relationship --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No he hasn't.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: -- with someone who has the same sex as you.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: He's married to a white woman.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Same-sex marriage. And Alito said in the majority opinion --\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: That's why it is so bitterly ironic.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: In the majority opinion, Alito said we are not dealing with those issues, Obergefell, Loving versus Virginia, or Griswold versus Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: He mentioned Griswold --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Hold on. Hold on. Dana?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: It's not the first time that he has been called these names by the left. And it doesn't matter what opinion it is. If it goes against what the progressives think is right, then they will call him Uncle Tom. And it's happened for years. And it doesn't make -- that is also racist. It's 