t's obvious. And the Democrats themselves are saying that. You had an anonymous Democrat quoted in a CNN piece this week saying they vacillate between not having a plan or trying to blame somebody else. But they're -- the Democrats are waiting, like, what -- which way are we going here, boss?\par \par \uc2 I think Geraldo is right, that the Democrats are hoping to hide their economic failures by focusing on something like Roe v. Wade. And Republicans are saying, well, there's Roe v. Wade, but they need to figure out a way to deal with that communication as well. But they're planning to run just all across the board on inflation. Today -- do you mind if I call for this soundbite? I just think that this was significant.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Sure.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: OK, so \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2  is a Democrat from Virginia in a swing district. She is a Democrat. She's been saying that the Squad is wrong for a long time. I asked her if she would be willing to campaign with Biden. This is what she said.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. ABIGAIL SPANBERGER (D-VA): I intend to do the campaigning myself. I am the candidate. It's my name on the ballot. Certainly, when I first ran, I ran in an R-plus seven district and I won in that seat by getting out speaking to voters, making sure that they know who I am and what it is that I intended to do for them.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: You'll see a lot more of that. Remember when Stacey Abrams had a scheduling conflict and she couldn't be with Biden and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Right, right.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: So, there's going to be a lot of that.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: All right, Jesse. So, if 75 percent of Americans say that the economy is bad, you even have X number of people worried about Roe vs. Wade, I wonder if Roe vs. Wade will be as heavy on their minds as the economy -- as it continues to get worse getting closer to November.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I think the economy trumps Roe?\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: What if you have a daughter?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: The far left will be fired up about Roe but I just think it's overwhelming that people in this country are suffering economically and that's not going to -- that's a taste that's not going to leave their mouths. I am just relieved, Judge, that Harris is going to tackle costs as well as prices. Not just the costs, we're going to go after the price is too.\par \par \uc2 Is she so bad, you can smell the politician through the screen? She's only good at memorization, right?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Is she?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And I used to be -- well, you can see kind of how she's reciting things as she -- I used to do this. I was hired at 22 years old to work in an asset management company after college. I didn't know anything about economics, but I could memorize things and I could speak. And so, we'd get up at these pitch meetings where I would pretend to be the salesman to clients.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: And what has changed?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: And I'd get up there and I'd just recite beautifully what our sales pitch was, and the guy running it would go, all right, Watters, what is a mortgage-backed security? And I'd say it's a security backed by mortgage? And he go, all right, Watters, sit down. I had no idea what I was talking about. It's the same thing with her.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: All right, "THE FASTEST" is up next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 TIMPF: Welcome back. Time for "THE FASTEST." First up, majority of Americans think they can do this. Nearly six in 10 say they got what it takes to become an action movie star. You obviously probably think you can do that, right?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Before the back surgery, I would have said yes. But now, I need a stunt double.\par \par \uc2 TIMPF: Really?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Probably David Schwimmer comes to mind. You'd have to stand --\par \par \uc2 TIMPF: It comes to my mind too.\par \