ok at the governor's races up here in New York. We have several Republicans vying for the nomination including Representative \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 , well positioned, endorsed by the state's Republican committee officially and campaigned with the Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , \uc2 Andrew Giuliani\uc2 , the son of \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , former mayor of New York City. They will go up against likely the incumbent Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  in November.\par \par \uc2 And as we look out here to Illinois, we may get some indication tonight whether the Supreme Court abortion decision has moved the needle for voters. FOX Business correspondent Grady Trimble in Aurora, Illinois, to tell us how the Roe ruling could affect one of the big primary elections in is that state. Good evening, Grady.\par \par \uc2 GRADY TRIMBLE, FOX BUSINESS CORRESPONDENT: Good evening, Bret. The mayor of this city, \uc2 Richard Irvin\uc2 , was considered the frontrunner on the Republican side when he launched his campaign for governor. But the race has taken a turn. Now polls indicate Trump-backed state Senator \uc2 Darren Bailey\uc2  has a commanding lead in the GOP primary. Democratic governor J.D. Pritzker and the \uc2 Democratic Governors Association\uc2  have also gotten involved, spending tens of millions of dollars in an attempt to damage Irvin, a more moderate candidate, and boost Bailey. The \uc2 DGA\uc2  says it's educating the public on these Republican candidates. \uc2 Richard Irvin\uc2  doesn't see it that way.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MAYOR RICHARD IRVIN, (R-AURORA) ILLINOIS GUBERNATORIAL CANDIDATE: J.D. Pritzker, a Democrat, meddling in a Republican primary, that's unheard of. But he knows who is going to beat him in November. And he knows what he has got to do to try to stop me. But we're not going to allow that.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: They would make the case, though, that they think you are an easier opponent in November.\par \par \uc2 DA