ore importantly, and I think this is extremely important. The authority to seizer all of my information and modern smartphones, that's access to all my private financial records.\par \par \uc2 I'm an attorney, it's access to all my privilege communications, with nearly a hundred different clients that I have currently. This stuff -- this stuff is what we used to call a general warrant that the British King issued to just go rummage through somebody's belongings to see if they could find evidence of some crime.\par \par \uc2 The very reason we have the Fourth Amendment is to prevent that kind of abuse. And yet, that's what they're doing here.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: And it's just another reminder to anyone who didn't vote for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to erase your texts and e-mails every single day and that is a sincere piece of advice I hope everyone follows.\par \par \uc2 But they haven't charged you with a crime. They've given you no evidence that they're going to charge you with a crime, but they treat you like a drug kingpin or a rapist and seize your phone. Is this legal?\par \par \uc2 EASTMAN: I don't think so. And they forced me in the position.\par \par \uc2 Look, I, as an attorney, I have ethical obligations to do everything I can to protect the privilege communications with my clients. So we will be filing a motion, it's called a Rule 41 Motion to retrieve my phone, to retrieve any information they've taken off of that phone that they have illegally seized from me and we'll be doing that in short order.\par \par \uc2 But you know, what they're doing -- the other thing they're doing is they're forcing those of us that, you know, don't bow the knee to the Biden administration to rack up hundreds of thousands of dollars in legal fees, trying to protect our constitutional rights and those of our clients.\par \par \uc2 So let me ask people, GiveSendGo.com/eastman, help us. Help us fight this abuse. We've got to stand together to fight against this.\par \par \uc2 CARL