eenagers. I thought of it as an aunt of preschool children--\par \par \uc2 DANA BASH, CNN HOST: And a woman yourself.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: And a woman myself, and the daughter of a woman, and a granddaughter of a woman.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: A lot of repeating. At least she can identify a woman now. And if that word salad didn't do it for you, she also shared a big concern of hers that men won't be able to knock up girls and then force them into abortions.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: First of all, if you are a parent of sons, do think about what this means for the life of your son. And what that will mean in terms of the choices he will have.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What? But the most important news to come out of this interview came near the end.\par \par \uc2 Now tonight, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  is out with a story headlined "Biden irked by Democrats who won't take yes for an answer on 2024"\par \par \uc2 The peace noting that "The White House is trying to tamp down speculation about plans for him to seek reelection, while aides say President Biden is bristling at the persistent questions".\par \par \uc2 And for better or worse, they tried it out Kamala to tamp down those rumors too.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BASH: Have you talked to President Biden about reelection?\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is running for reelection, and I will be his ticket mate.\par \par \uc2 BASH: Full stop.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: Full stop. That's it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Full stop. As if Republicans needed any more good news these days, you just got it.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Charlie Hurt, Washington Times opinion editor; as well as Ben Domenech, spectator editor-at-large, as well as the host of 'Overturning Roe' outright now on Fox nation. Both of you are Fox contributors.\par \par \uc2 Charlie, let's start with you. Now, with Biden abroad, we are getting a sneak peek, right, at what the messaging from Kamala - Kamala-led administration looks like. It ain't pretty.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE HURT, WASHINGTON TIMES OPINION EDITOR: No, it really is not. And you're exactly right. Just when you think it can't get any worse. Here's somebody who had spent years on the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2 , and of course, has underperformed at every single step of the way.\par \par \uc2 But this is what you get when you have a president who picks somebody based on the color of their skin and their gender, and no other qualifications whatsoever. You wind up with this.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Ben, what about the comment about boys - the how this is going to affect boys? Maybe I'm not getting what she meant, but it certainly sounded like boys are going to have to be responsible - more responsible now. I mean, it was odd.\par \par \uc2 BEN DOMENECH, THE SPECTATOR EDITOR AT LARGE: The horror they are going to have to actually take responsibility for their actions, as opposed to be able to pay a girl to go away and have an abortion. I mean, this is horrendous and it's so disturbing, but it's also so typical.\par \par \uc2 The thing I love about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is that she's too dumb to really hide any of the things that the left wants you to hide about the positions they actually have. She just throws it out there and then she kind of cackles afterward.\par \par \uc2 And in this case, this is another example of that. It's like, oh, my gosh, you're going to have to tell your sons that they're going to have to be responsible if they go out and sleep with someone and have a baby. And they're not just going to be able to kill it and walk away. Isn't that horrible?\par \par \uc2 And that's the sort of thing that she would bring to any kind of ticket in 2024 that she was the head of, the fact that she's emphatic that she's going to be on this ticket in 2024. I'm sure it totally encourages all of 