inue living in fear, how their - how rape victims are going to be compelled by the state to carry babies to term.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: A woman can be prosecuted right now for taking anything, or using any device that is not intended to increase the likelihood of survival of a fetus. That means anything that prevents implantation of this (inaudible)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK. The unhinged reaction to Roe continued this morning. Now, that was until yet another victory for conservatives was handed down. The court sided with the former Washington state high school football coach over his right to pray on the 50-yard line immediately after games.\par \par \uc2 Now, that simple act is apparently quite triggering for the commentariat.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  decision coming down today on a religious liberty case that further erodes the line between church and state.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: This is really another decision from this court that has the effect here of eroding the barrier between church and state.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: A third time this term that has slightly reduced the wall of separation between church and state.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The echo chamber, it's a beautiful thing to behold.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2 , Missouri Attorney General, candidate for \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 ; and Texas Lieutenant Governor, \uc2 Dan Patrick\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Attorney General Schmitt, you filed an amicus brief, I know, in support of Coach Kennedy. We've had him on the 'Angle' a number of times. Now, what do you say to these people saying that this decision is a separation of church and state issue?\par \par \uc2 ERIC SCHMITT, (R) MISSOURI ATTORNEY GENERAL: These people have lost their minds and their real objection is with the Constitution. This country was founded on the idea that people could express their religious beliefs and the government will protect that right, the God given right not infringe upon it.\par \par \uc2 And so, here you have a coach engage in voluntary prayer, and the left has lost their minds that it's now protected. And we're led to believe by the way by these same people that it's perfectly ok to force your kids to sit through drag queen story hour in this woke indoctrination in our schools. They're ok with that, they want to push that. But the idea that you actually have a constitutionally protected right to engage in prayer is very affirming that the court issued this opinion today because this is exactly the right way.\par \par \uc2 The Constitution is supposed to protect these individual rights in the right to express yourself through prayers certainly protected is a big win for religious liberty here today.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right, Dan. On the issue of Roe, Kamala was asked tonight about federal financial resources for women who want abortions. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BASH: What about the idea of financial resources? Some form of voucher for travel for women seeking abortions in states where it's not legal.\par \par \uc2 HARRIS: You're asking a very important point, making a very important point, which is what are the details that are going to go into ensuring that women have the ability to actually travel without an impairment. So this is something that we are looking at.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Dan, she's talking about, I guess, helping women travel out of states like yours, which is currently being sued, right, by the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 . Your reaction.\par \par \uc2 DAN PATRICK, LIEUTENANT GOVERNOR OF TEXAS: This is a culture of death in this administration, Laura. And now they want to give a voucher to go take the life of a baby.\par \par \uc2 Through this entire discussion, Laura, the last couple of days since Roe v Wade was overturned