 Well, I think there's a lot of light out there and we're seeing some bad news, but that court decision was a great, great moment for this country.\par \par \uc2 PATRICK: It was a great day. It was a great day.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Gentlemen, great to see you both.\par \par \uc2 And things are so bad in New York City where we are with crime surging nearly 40 percent, that Mayor Eric Adams was forced to admit he was shocked at how bad this place is. But New York Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  is taking a different tact, not just ignoring the plight of her constituents but getting angry when they are afforded new rights.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GOV. \uc2 KATHY HOCHUL\uc2 , (D) NEW YORK: I'm sorry this dark day has come, that we're supposed to go back to what was in place since 1788 when the Constitution of the United States of America was ratified. And I would like to point out to the Supreme Court justices that they only weapons at that time were muskets. I'm prepared to go back to muskets.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Gosh, she is so smart. Joining me now is New York congressman and gubernatorial candidate \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 . Congressman, greats to see you. Big primary tomorrow. Everybody get out and vote. If you like what is happening in this city and across the state, definitely vote for Hochul. But I think a lot of people hear stuff like that and say this women is just not serious.\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 LEE ZELDIN\uc2 , (R-NY): Totally out of touch with reality. And you talk about muskets 18th century, then she was talking about weapons of war and fully automatic weapons, as if people who want concealed carry are looking to put one of those fully automatic scary looking weapons of war on their hip pocket. She was, by the way, firmly A-rated \uc2 NRA\uc2  endorsed member of Congress, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , just like Kirsten Gillibrand. They're moderates in the House, and then they're statewide in a liberal 