nel are currently working to secure the scene. The train had approximately 207 passengers, as well as crew members, all injured and uninjured occupants of the train had been transported from the scene.\par \par \uc2 Multiple law enforcement agencies, ambulance districts, first responders, fire departments, and medical helicopter -- helicopters responded to assist. Agencies involved including are the Sheridan County, Linn County, Macon County, Randolph County sheriff's offices, the Brookfield and Macon police departments, the Missouri State Highway Patrol, the \uc2 Missouri Department of Conservation\uc2 . The Missouri State Park Rangers, the Missouri State Fire Marshal's, the state emergency management.\par \par \uc2 Ambulance from the Sheridan County, Linn County, Randolph County, Livingston County, Macon County, Howard County, Carroll County and Caldwell County, also transported with medical helicopters, transport the medical services, provided respond -- responded to the scene. Each agency transported multiple victims. Officials from \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  are responding to the scene and the \uc2 NTSB\uc2  has been advised.\par \par \uc2 The investigation is in its preliminary stages. And as more information becomes available, we will be releasing it at that time. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 LT. ERIC F. BROWN, MISSOURI STATE HIGHWAY PATROL: As we stress, so, this is the beginning of a lengthier investigation. We have a lot more information we were seeking the need to obtain.\par \par \uc2 Also with me are a members of the Sheridan County commission. We will provide updates as they're available. They can be found on our patrols \uc2 Twitter\uc2  page @MSHPTrooperB.\par \par \uc2 Updated information be there as quickly as we can. And we will address more questions as we get more information. Thank you all for your time. I appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Can you just any questions here?\par \par \uc2 BROWN: We'll take some afterwards.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFI