acist, sexist, homophobic, blah, blah, blah.\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: Yeah, they can't run on saying to people that abortion is still tragically, there are still abortions today. Tragically, there will be abortions tomorrow because abortion is not banned. They can't run on that.\par \par \uc2 So they have to lie to people and say, it was just a ruling that bans it -- almost bans it. That's what they're telling people, when in fact, the ruling today -- and this is what they can't run on -- is to tell the people that the Supreme Court ruled that you through your elected representatives in the state you live will get to decide the state law about abortion. They can't run on that. So, they have to lie and tell people to go out and take to the streets --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What is the law in the state of Florida, Senator?\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: Well, the legislature in Florida passed a 15-week ban.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: Meaning, after the first 15 weeks -- and, by the way, that is consistent and in line with much of the country's -- if you're a path (ph), that -- poll after poll, these guys love talking about polls. Poll after poll show the overwhelming majority of Americans support a ban after 15 weeks. That's the Florida law and now --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: By the way, \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  actually put out specifics that fully 55 percent of abortions today are done by pills in people's homes. I found that number to be very high. I looked elsewhere and it seems to be consistent with other estimates.\par \par \uc2 RUBIO: Yeah, and all of these are tragic, okay? But the point being that that's what the law is in Florida, that's what the law -- that's what this case was about, was a Mississippi law that was being challenged and worked its way over to the court.\par \par \uc2 But what these people don't want you to know and why they don't want to have these debates, what they don't want