ring in White House Press Secretary \uc2 Ari Fleischer\uc2 , Civil Rights Attorney Leo Terrell, and Democrat Strategist and Co-Host of "THE FIVE" Jessica Tarlov, all Fox News Contributors, --and we have not heard from you today. So, I want to start with just the headline question. And let me start with you Ari, did you ever think that you would see this day? And what do you, what's your reaction to this decision?\par \par \uc2 ARI FLEISCHER\uc2 , FORMER WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: You know, Martha, for 50 years, conservatives and the pro-life community had to live with a rule that they disagreed with. And now, the shoe is going to on the other foot. And that is the way our system works. And our system does work. The fact of the matter is all these things happen because the sovereignty of the people, the people elected the President, the President made the appointments.\par \par \uc2 And \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  are right on what they said today, they made it political. They say, if you don't like this, you need to turn out November. Let them try. This is the way our system works. And it is the proper ruling. It's an accurate ruling. It is a right ruling, there is no abortion in the Constitution. It should be left up to the people of the States. Our system had a good day to day. It all works.\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Yes. And Jessica, when I listened to the people in the crowd there, and when I listened to other people who've reacted to this since the leak of this document, you hear a lot of people say, you know, I can't believe people just you know, the justices just wake up one morning and decide they're going to overturn Roe v. Wade, which has been the law of land for 50 years. That is not how this works. A case came before the court.\par \par \uc2 It was a Mississippi ban on abortions past 15 weeks, nearly four months into a pregnancy. And when they looked at this decision, these particular justices who now make up the court said, you know 