eral government are reserved to the states under the 10th Amendment or the people. So this is the way our Constitution is supposed to work.\par \par \uc2 And the decision that was made 50 years ago was a bad decision. Even Ginsburg said, even she agreed women ought to have the right to control their body, the decision, Roe was decided wrong from a Constitution standpoint.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: As you know, Senator, Democrats have seized on this all the way up to the president himself as sort of galvanizing their party, the base of their party, I assume, to vote Democrat in the November elections.\par \par \uc2 Do you worry about that?\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: I don`t worry about it from the standpoint of the politics, because I keep in touch with my constituents through my 99 county meetings every year.\par \par \uc2 And Iowans are concerned about inflation, about gas prices, and about the border and the Rio Grande not being controlled. That`s what I have heard all year. And those are still the top items that we hear. I think this is going to elevate abortion a little bit for a while, but people are -- pocketbook in November 8.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right.\par \par \uc2 Senator, very quickly on other news that shows the two parties can work together on something, this bipartisan gun measure that had 15 Republican votes in the Senate got passage today in the House.\par \par \uc2 So it does show, I guess regardless of what your personal views are on that legislation, that the two parties can still work together. Are you confident they can continue to after this?\par \par \uc2 GRASSLEY: I can give you three bills right now, Klobuchar-Grassley to take on big tech`s anti-discrimination thing, Grassley-Tester on cattle bill, and Grassley-Wyden on prescription drug prices, just to name three that I have been working on for two years.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, got it. I see that Grassley name in all of them, so they must be a good thing.\par \par \uc2 So, Senator, thank you very, very much. We appreciate your time on this crazy day.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, Inc.  Copyright CQ-2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All materials herein are  protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced,  distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the  prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You may not alter  or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the  content. \par \par \uc2 Document CAVU000020220624ei6o0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Interview With Fmr. Sen. Joe Lieberman (I-CT)\b0\par\par\uc2 Neil Cavuto \par \uc2 878 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Your World w/ Neil Cavuto\par \uc2 CAVU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 NEIL CAVUTO, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: To Joe Lieberman right now.\par \par \uc2 You hope cooler, calmer heads prevail, Senator, but that`s the big worry. This is a very polarizing issue. And emotions run extreme on both sides.\par \par \uc2 What do you tell people?\par \par \uc2 FMR. SEN. JOE LIEBERMAN (I-CT): Well the first thing is that it is -- this is an enormously significant decision.\par \par \uc2 I mean, it`s one of the big days in Supreme Court history. Justice Alito himself compared it in defending the overturning of a previous decision to the Brown vs. Board of Education decision, which overturned Plessy vs. Ferguson on the basic idea that our principle that separate but equal is not equal.\par \par \uc2 So there`s a lot of emotions out there. But I appreciate what President Biden said today. Obviously, he`s against the decision. He`s disappointed by it. But he`s the president, and he sets the tone. And he`s saying to people who are -- agree with him the decision was wrong, you have got to keep it peaceful. That`s the way we are in America.\par \par \uc2 We try to -- we accept the judgment of courts, even if we disagree with them. And I would add this note. If you disagree with this decision, but you are also horrified by what happened at the U.S. Capitol on January 6 because of this attempt to violently interrupt the constitutional border of counting electoral votes, then you can`t tolerate violence in response to a Supreme Court decision.\par \par \uc2 You have got to go back to court. You have got to go back to the legislatures. As the president said, you got to get involved in the elections this fall and in 2024.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: But he didn`t say all of that. And I do appreciate what you`re saying, Senator, about his expressing his disappointment with this decision, and urging everyone to keep calm. I`m just paraphrasing.\par \par \uc2 But he went beyond just expressing his disappointment, right? He questioned the motives behind it and the way and the approval of the three conservative justices in their arrival on the court, more or less impinging the entire court and the system we all have to rally around, whether we will always agree with the decision that court makes or not.\par \par \uc2 Doesn`t that further incite anger, that someone hears that, says, the president`s right about this, this is a kangaroo court, and it was Trump that put all these guys in there, and that`s a mistake, and it was rigged from the beginning?\par \par \uc2 It feeds a beastly kind of behavior, doesn`t it?\par \par \uc2 LIEBERMAN: I don`t think so, Neil.\par \par \uc2 Look, the president really is disappointed, obviously, by this decision. He`s got a right of free speech, if you will, to say so.\par \par \uc2 If you read the decisions of Justice Alito, and the -- and Justice Thomas, and the three dissenting justices, they say some pretty tough things about each other and the opinions each side articulated. So that`s just part of our system.\par \par \uc2 But, again, when the Supreme Court decides, that`s the law of the land. And I thought you have to consider not only President Biden`s call for peaceful, peaceful, peaceful protests, no intimidation, but also the fact that he redirected people who are upset with this decision to the election process, to the campaigns, and, ultimately, I think probably back to the court.\par \par \uc2 There`s a lot of room. This isn`t over. I mean, the court today obviously removed the constitutional right to an abortion. But it did not, I don`t think, say that Congress has no role here. And I think in the days ahead, you`re going to find people in Congress trying to figure out how to, again, establish a national standard for abortion.\par \par \uc2 Whether they can do it or not depends on the election in November. If Congress is as closely divided as now, or if Republicans control both houses or one, it`s not going to happen.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 LIEBERMAN: So the activity will go back to the states. And that`s not such a bad thing overall.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right.\par \par \uc2 Well, and, again, commenting on that decision and the implications of it are one thing. More or less questioning the institution that created it, I don`t know, Senator. On this one, we might not be seeing eye to eye.\par \par \uc2 But it`s always good seeing you, my friend. Thank you very, very much.\par \par \uc2 LIEBERMAN: You too.\par \par \uc2 Take care, Neil.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: It happens, right? It happens.\par \par \uc2 Joseph Lieberman, the former U.S. senator.\par \par \uc2 LIEBERMAN: Every now and then, barely.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Now and then. Now and then, it does happen.\par \par \uc2 Of course, the former vice presidential candidate in 2000 for the Democratic Party.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, Inc.  Copyright CQ-2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All materials herein are  protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced,  distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the  prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You may not alter  or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the  content. \par \par \uc2 Document CAVU000020220624ei6o0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Interview With Sen. \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2  (R-UT)\b0\par\par\uc2 Neil Cavuto \par \uc2 978 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Your World w/ Neil Cavuto\par \uc2 CAVU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 NEIL CAVUTO, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: One of the things you have been hearing about the waiting for this decision from the Supreme Court was that at least two dozen states were ready to trigger their own anti-abortion laws and put them in effect virtually immediately.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2 , he sits on the Judiciary Committee. He joins us now, the senator, of course, from the beautiful state of Utah.\par \par \uc2 Senator, good to have you.\par \par \uc2 I don`t know if whether Utah is one of those states, sir, but what do you think of states that are going to implement these triggers?\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 MIKE LEE\uc2  (R-UT): Yes, Utah has a trigger law. It is written by one of our great state legislators, Karianne Lisonbee.\par \par \uc2 And Utah, like so many other laws, really does have an interest in making sure that it legislates. What we see is the democratic process unfolding now. That process has been taken off the table for 49 years. And this is what the Republican form of government looks like.\par \par \uc2 It allows people through their elected lawmakers to make laws, including laws regarding how best to protect unborn human life.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: So, Senator, do you think it just adds to the confusion, though? I understand that, bringing it back to the states, maybe 24 will have this position that they know abortions are allowed.\par \par \uc2 I don`t know whether they`re as strict as Texas` abortion law that from fertilization, almost to conception, that it would be illegal. What we do now separately, 16 states and the District of Columbia that are protecting access to abortion.\par \par \uc2 What do you think of the kind of confusion that`s been wrought here?\par \par \uc2 LEE: Well, that`s not really confusion. That`s what we call federalism. That`s not confusion. That`s the way our constitutional system works.\par \par \uc2 And when something isn`t taken off the table by the Constitution, it`s reserved to the people. And unless it`s made federal, then it`s reserved to the people to be exercised at the state level. There`s -- it is not unusual to have differences between one state and another on laws governing all sorts of things.\par \par \uc2 It`s not a horrific event to have different laws in one state than in another. And abortion is no exception to that.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: So, Senator, if there`s a doctor performing abortions now in your state or any other of these roughly two dozen states that have this so- called trigger provision, are they breaking the law? Can they be arrested?\par \par \uc2 LEE: It depends on the circumstances.\par \par \uc2 This trigger law that Utah has enacted, Representative Lisonbee`s bill, does allow for abortions to be conducted under certain limited, narrow circumstances, and it would depend on those circumstances.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: So, if you have a business, let`s say -- I spoke to the Rite Aid CEO earlier today, sir, and she was reminding me that, of course, Rite Aid is everywhere.\par \par \uc2 But if you`re filling out prescriptions for abortion-related drugs or treatments, it`s possible in those states that have these trigger laws Rite Aid could be violating the law, right?\par \par \uc2 LEE: Well, yes, that`s possible. They will have to seek counsel in their respective states from people who are familiar with the laws in question.\par \par \uc2 But here, again, it`s important to remember this is the nature of the system in which we operate. Different states are going to have different laws. And it`s not surprising that a state like Utah might have a different set of policy preferences when it comes to how we`re going to protect unborn human life than you might see in New York or Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 It`s neither surprising nor unusual.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: So, in Utah, if you could educate me, Senator, what is the -- is it similar to Texas, no abortions beyond fertilization, beyond conception?\par \par \uc2 LEE: In Utah, we have exceptions under our law to protect a woman`s right to access to an abortion in circumstances where the pregnancy resulted from rape or incest or certain rare medical conditions can be found either in the mother or in the baby. In the case of the baby, if it`s a certainly fatal, diagnosable ailment that won`t allow the child to live past birth, that`s one of them. Certain brain defects will also qualify.\par \par \uc2 And if the mother faces substantial impairment to major bodily functions, in some circumstances, she might be able to get one.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Senator, there are now pills for abortion. You can take pills, and they are across all state lines.\par \par \uc2 LEE: Yes.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: I`m just wondering, do you think, given what Utah has committed to do in this trigger provision, they should be outlawed in your state?\par \par \uc2 LEE: Well, I`d have to look at the law and figure -- again, the Utah law doesn`t allow -- doesn`t outlaw abortions in every circumstance.\par \par \uc2 And so, no, I wouldn`t say that the -- that that pill would be outlined in every circumstance, given that the law doesn`t outlaw abortion in every circumstance.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: Got it.\par \par \uc2 LEE: It will depend on the specifics of the abortion in question.\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, I just wanted to get some clarification in my thick skull to understand where this goes from here.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Mike Lee\uc2 , very good seeing you. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 LEE: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, Inc.  Copyright CQ-2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All materials herein are  protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced,  distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the  prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You may not alter  or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the  content. \par \par \uc2 Document CAVU000020220624ei6o00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 The Democrats' Green Energy Scam; Biden In Denial As President Suggest Inflation Is A Chance To Make "Fundamental Turn" To Renewables; Far-Left Abortion Group Threatens More Violence\b0\par\par\uc2 Sean Hannity, Geraldo Rivera, Leo Terrell, Bill Hemmer \par \uc2 7,761 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 June 2022\par \uc2 Fox News: Hannity\par \uc2 SHAN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 ASC Services II Media, LLC.  All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST: Sounds like a sci-fi movie. And I just hope they can't do political talk shows or we're dead. That wouldn't be --\par \par \uc2 TUCKER CARLSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS HOST, "TUCKER CARLSON TONIGHT": I bet they can. That's terrifying.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right, Tucker. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 And welcome to HANNITY.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, a HANNITY investigation into America's two-tier justice system and corrupt D.C. politicians who excuse riots that don't advance their political agenda now this includes the clear danger this country is now facing if Roe v. Wade is overturned. We have left wing groups now signaling direct threats to riot. We'll tell you about that.\par \par \uc2 But first, tonight, we begin with a major scam now ongoing inside the climate alarmist religious cult known as the new green deal Democratic Party, the socialist party. And as we speak, the Biden administration, they are knowingly and openly lying to you, the American people, including their own die-hard supporters about one of the Democratic Party's favorite causes, the transition to green renewable energy.\par \par \uc2 Remember they steadfastly refuse to drill and to frack and they want to import oil from Iran and Venezuela and Saudi Arabia and \uc2 OPEC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: We have a chance here to make a fundamental turn toward renewable energy, electric vehicles -- and not just electric vehicles but across the board.\par \par \uc2 REP. ALEXANDRIA OCASIO-CORTEZ (D-NY): Ultimately, we really do need to be investing in renewables.\par \par \uc2 PETE BUTTIGIEG, TRANSPORTATION SECRETARY: Until we achieve a form of energy independence that is based on clean energy created here at home, American citizens will still be vulnerable to wild price hikes like we're seeing right now during Putin's war.\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER GRANHOLM\uc2 , ENERGY SECRETARY: As Minister Ryan has said, this clean energy transition could be the peace project of our time.\par \par \uc2 JANET YELLEN\uc2 , TREASURY SECRETARY: The way in which we can ensure reasonable energy expenses for households is to move to renewables to address climate change.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Now, tonight, we'll do a deep dive we'll expose the truth about these lies because as it turns out, this push towards what they call renewables and green energy and electric cars is a massive fraud. We'll explain in detail. But in order to really understand this, it is important to first know where do we get our energy from? Ever ask yourself the question?\par \par \uc2 I know you come home, you flip on the lights -- electricity, that's great. Look at your screen. Seventy-nine percent of America's grid is now powered by, guess what, fossil fuels. What do I say about fossil fuels? The lifeblood of the world's economy. That includes petroleum, natural gas and you bet, coal.\par \par \uc2 Another 8 percent is derived from nuclear power plants. Liberals hate that, too. Now, currently only 12 percent of our energy by definition would be from renewables.\par \par \uc2 So if the administration truly wanted to transition away from fossil fuels, they would need to shut down 80 to 90 percent of our power grid and replace it with, what, windmills, solar power? Unfortunately, that type of so- called green energy is not very efficient. Let's take, for example, one wind turbine. It produces less than three megawatts of energy whereas one natural gas turbine produces 45.\par \par \uc2 And get this, a typical natural gas plant has three turbines, which means you could need what, 49 windmills to replace just one moderately sized natural gas plant.\par \par \uc2 Now, keep in mind, there are more than 3,400 fossil fuel power plants in operation within the U.S. Any transition to wind and to solar would take decades and decades and decades and it would not lower the cost at all in the interim and probably thereafter.\par \par \uc2 Now, each windmill costs more than $3.8 million dollars to build, not to mention the thousands upon thousands of acres of land that would be needed to be purchased. And as Energy Secretary \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2  declared, it will require a lot of new resources that you, we, the American people, will have to pay for. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GRANHOLM: With the president's goal of 100 percent clean electricity by 2035 and net zero by 2050, we are going to be able to do that kind of transition with all different kinds of technologies in all pockets of the country.\par \par \uc2 We're going to need workers to, yes, install wind turbines and solar panels. We're going to need workers to build those wind turbines and solar panels. We need steel workers. We need miners for the materials to build them. We're going to need truckers and dock workers and deck hands to transport them. We're going to need electricians. We're going to need laborers. We're going to need utility workers.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: In other words, a big transition to renewables is not going to happen under Biden and any incremental transition will do nothing but drive up the cost of energy all across the board.\par \par \uc2 The only actual way to bring down prices is to produce more gas and oil, the lifeblood of the world's economy. I'll say it again.\par \par \uc2 In order to appease the climate alarmist cult in his party and pull the wool over your eyes, the administration is now trying to outsource all energy needs overseas. That's why they're trying to do a deal with Iran. That's why they're sending emissaries over to Venezuela. That's why he will bow before the crown prince, the guy that he says is responsible for killing Jamal Khashoggi, the pariah nation of Saudi Arabia, in order to make another big show about shutting down oil and gas infrastructure like for example pipelines and refineries and exploration permits inside the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Now, that's why Biden is going to Saudi Arabia. In spite of what they say, I promise you, he will be begging that crown prince right there and kissing up to him and kissing his ass and begging for more oil production. Now, we saw the same thing in Russia, I'm sorry, Europe with Russia, far left Germany.\par \par \uc2 Well, guess what? They have their own climate alarmist religious cult. They were desperate to appease them. They shut down their fossil fuel facilities. They outsourced all of their energy needs and did billion- dollar deals with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . How's that working out?\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, it was all about optics, didn't actually improve the environment. I mean, Mother Earth doesn't matter if you get a barrel of oil from here or over here. Not really. It always was a huge scam.\par \par \uc2 And now with Putin's war raging, Germany -- well, the spigot's been shut off. Now, they have to restart their -- well, mothball, coal-powered plants. Whoopsy daisy. Now, this brings us to electric cars.\par \par \uc2 Now, pay close attention here. When the Biden administration isn't fantasizing about renewables and energy independence with renewables, they're begging Americans. They're lecturing us to buy electric cars. They tell us over and over again, buy an electric car.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BUTTIGIEG: Last month, we announced a billion investment to build out a nationwide electric vehicle charging network so the people from rural to suburban to urban communities can all benefit from the gas savings of driving an EV.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Under my plan, which is before the Congress now we can take advantage of the next generation of electric vehicles, that a typical driver will save about $80 a month from not having to pay gas at the pump.\par \par \uc2 SEN. DEBBIE STABENOW (D-MI): It's on the issue of gas prices after waiting for a long time to have enough trips in this country to finally get my electric vehicle, I got it and drove it from Michigan to here this last weekend, and went by every single gas station, didn't matter how high it was.\par \par \uc2 GRANHOLM: If you filled up your EV by charging and you filled up your gas tank with gasoline and you have the same size tank, you would save $60 per fill up by going electric rather than using gasoline.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Maybe they haven't noticed but Biden inflation has added an additional $6,000 to every American household unnecessarily. And as you can see, Democrats want you to believe you buy an electric vehicle, it will bring down the cost for you the American people and will save the environment at the same time. Both claims are totally false.\par \par \uc2 Let's tackle the cost, the obvious. The average price for a new electric vehicle is $64,000, compared to $44,000 for a full-size car. So from the purchase, you're already, well, 20 grand in the hole. Add in another $1,200 for an installation of an electric charging port and 55 bucks a month in additional energy costs, and you will most certainly not be saving any money over the entire life of the vehicle.\par \par \uc2 I'm not against them, but I'm just giving you the reality. Now, of course, any electric car is only as clean as its energy source. They don't -- never talk about this part.\par \par \uc2 Remember, 80 percent of our power comes from oil, gas and coal. But that's not the only thing to consider. Keep in mind the production of these electric vehicles not exactly environmentally friendly. You know the battery alone is typically comprised of nickel, cobalt, aluminum, manganese and all of these need to be mined from Mother Earth with heavy equipment that uses gas or diesel.\par \par \uc2 Many rechargeable batteries are derived from, oops, China where they use slave labor or child labor. And don't get me wrong, there are some pretty cool electric vehicles on the market including \uc2 Tesla\uc2 . By the way, I'd look at a \uc2 Tesla\uc2 . A friend of mine swears by his. He loves it.\par \par \uc2 But buying one doesn't make you Captain Planet as \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  who flies around in his private jets would have you believe.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, under Trump, the United States -- you may have never been told this by the climate alarmist cult. Under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the United States led the world in greenhouse gas reduction. Not because of electric cars or windmills, instead clean burning, affordable natural gas developed through the free market help the United States curb pollution.\par \par \uc2 By the way, we're the Middle East of natural gas. We have at least 200- plus-years worth of a supply of natural gas. And that's all we know about at this moment.\par \par \uc2 Now talking about a phantom transition to renewables is not going to save our economy or the planet. We are now barreling towards a recession, coupled with out of control inflation, the national gas tax holiday Biden is now proposing will not significantly bring down prices, I'll take it, 18.4 cents a gallon. But I'll take it.\par \par \uc2 But even Obama said that this is a gimmick, kind of like tapping into the Strategic Petroleum Reserve. It's a band-aid. It's a temporary fix. After the election, they'll put it back in place.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BARACK OBAMA\uc2 , FORMER PRESIDENT: Oil companies like \uc2 Shell\uc2  and \uc2 BP\uc2  just reported record profits for the quarter and we're arguing over a gimmick to save you half a tank of gas, over the course of the entire summer so that everyone in Washington can pat themselves on the back and say that they did something.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: I can't believe it. Obama for once is actually right.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Obama's former economic adviser \uc2 Larry Summers\uc2  is now not only predicting a recession, also warning that the U.S. would need five years or six percent unemployment or one year of 10 percent unemployment to ease inflation, Biden inflation.\par \par \uc2 Our economy is going into a very dark place. You see it with your 401k. You see it when you go to the gas pump and you see it in every store that you shop in.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, the White House press secretary wasn't exactly reassuring. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KARINE JEAN-PIERRE\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: The action that the president has taken with the American Rescue Plan, with what we have seen with the historical gains, that is going to help us deal with the recession right now, we don't see a recession right now. That is not -- we're not in a recession right now. Right now, we're in a transition where we will we are going to -- going to go into a place of stable and steady growth.\par \par \uc2 You know, the president has been very clear in making sure that he does everything that he can to elevate -- to alleviate the -- you know, the pain that American families are feeling when it comes to gas prices.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: America is not heading towards a recession. That's kind of like inflation is transitory.\par \par \uc2 We, the American people are not stupid. Now, the Americans now know that how supply and demand works. They know that lecturing oil and gas companies and restricting the domestic production of energy raising taxes is not going to bring down costs or save us from a recession.\par \par \uc2 And by the way now in a new poll, Biden's approval rating is at 32 percent, that's right, the lowest point in a presidency since 1948.\par \par \uc2 Here with reaction, Outkick founder Clay Travis, along with the co-host of "The Five", Geraldo Rivera.\par \par \uc2 Geraldo, I mean electric cars are fine. I once had an Escalade hybrid. It wasn't too bad.\par \par \uc2 By the way, I love the "let's go Brandon" t-shirt, clay.\par \par \uc2 Yeah, it was fine. But when you -- when you break down how you charge it, when you break down how you build it, when you break down the cost of it, it's a fantasy that they're peddling here. In the meantime, we're going to beg Iran, Saudi Arabia and Venezuela. Does that make sense to you?\par \par \uc2 GERALDO RIVERA, CO-HOST OF "THE FIVE": It doesn't, but if President Biden could put together a coherent narrative as you just did, laying it all out, I think it would be in a much better place.\par \par \uc2 What he is trying to say -- and here I am translating for the president of the United States --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Geraldo, stop, pause.\par \par \uc2 What he's trying to say because you know, I know and Clay Travis knows and this audience knows that he's weak and he's frail and he's a cognitive wreck.\par \par \uc2 But go ahead. You translate for him.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: But he is the president of the United States, and you know --\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And a cognitive wreck.\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: -- a gas tax holiday is a ridiculous idea. It is a very transitory, you know, feel-good fix for a day or two.\par \par \uc2 What we need to do and what he should do rather than promoting the future - - we'll get to the future. Rather than promoting a \uc2 Tesla\uc2  in every garage, what he should be saying is let's produce more domestic oil ourselves, let's get the supply up. That will reduce the price.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Why don't we ask Midland, Texas? Why don't we go to Oklahoma? For natural gas, why don't we go --\par \par \uc2 RIVERA: Yes.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: -- 