oadcast news networks, we've seen an almost complete blackout of the Colbert seven. If this was FOX, the fainting couch store would run out of fainting couches in this industry.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Wait a minute, let's take it a step further. Let's call it the Hannity seven. I sent seven people to work on my staff, they did it, what happens?\par \par \uc2 CONCHA: Well, then, you would need to add another hour and day to 24/7 cable news coverage, right?\par \par \uc2 But to Jason's point earlier, in terms of the sentence -- the sentencing here, it's going to be very interesting to see what happens because Chad Pergram reported earlier on this network, a court found Couy Griffin of the group Cowboys for Trump guilty of a misdemeanor of entering the Capitol grounds. Even though he never entered the Capitol itself, he was sentenced to two weeks in prison, you know?\par \par \uc2 But in the end, it's not surprising that Colbert staffers who were supposed to be in the comedy business, by the way, attempted to do this. That show, along with \uc2 Jimmy Kimmel\uc2  , Seth Meyers, they're merely extensions of your average MSNBC show at this point, and the kind of escapism that we used to get at the end of a long day is gone. Sorry, go ahead.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So, one once again, Jason, you get the last word, 30 seconds. We don't have equal justice and equal application of our laws, do we?\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: No, no, we don't. \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  treats it totally different and the Department of Justice is unwilling. Yet again, add this to the long, long list of things that they're willing to prosecute.\par \par \uc2 Lady Justice is supposed to have a blindfold but she doesn't. She's not going to do anything in this case because it's people that are favorable to the left.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Unbelievable. I think if it was the Concha brigade, they might have -- I don't know -- they'd get a pass. I'm -- it's possible.\par \par \uc2 All right. Appreciate it. And, Jason, thank you. And of course, Joe Concha, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned. More "Hannity" right after this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: All right. Unfortunately, that is all the time we have left this evening. As always, thank you for being with us. You make the show possible. We can't thank you enough.\par \par \uc2 Please set your DVR. Never miss an episode. You are never going to get this news from the media mob.\par \par \uc2 When you need news, foxnews.com, hannity.com, any minute, any hour of any given day.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, let not your heart be troubled. Laura Ingraham is standing by. She's got a great show. "The Ingraham Angle" takes over right now -- Laura.\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2022 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document SHAN000020220621ei6k00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; International\par \b \uc2 Biden Addresses Fall Of Bike During Delaware Trip; Economy's Impact On Midterms, 2024; Seven Colbert Staffers Arrested On Capitol Hill; Rep. Michael Waltz (R-FL), Is Interviewed About Biden Administration's Mixed Message On President Biden's Ongoing Meeting With The Saudi Crown Prince \uc2 Mohammed Bin Salman\uc2  Next Month; White House: Biden Took Khashoggi Report Very Seriously; Biden Slammed Over Trip To "Pariah" Saudi Arabia; Nicaragua Approves Russian Troop Access To Country; Texas Lawmakers Investigate Uvalde Shooting Response; Close Race For Ohio's Senate Seat; Six Hurt, Three Critical After NUC Taxi Crash; CA Mom Shares Story Of Son Killed By Fake Fentanyl Pill\b0\par\par\uc2 An