nt's best tool to bring prices down. But he's been doing it since last year and prices haven't come down, Shannon.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: We have noticed. OK, Peter Doocy at the White House. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Oh, by the way, let me ask you before you go, the president taking off for Delaware this weekend. Do we know who's going to celebrate Father's Day?\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: We know that he's going to be in his beach house in Rehoboth, Delaware with the first lady and the first cat Willow, we saw them boarding Marine One. Before lunchtime today, they left at about 11:00 and we don't expect them back until late on Monday as part of a four day weekend that is bookended by Juneteenth on Monday, which is a federal holiday and their 45th wedding anniversary which is today, Shannon.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Let's hope that Dr. Jill got him something really nice. All right, Peter, thank you.\par \par \uc2 All right, stocks were mixed, the Dow lost 38, the S&P 500 gained eight, NASDAQ rose 152.\par \par \uc2 For the week, the Dow and NASDAQ dropped 4-8/10 percentage points and the S&P 500 was off 5-8/10.\par \par \uc2 Fox Business Correspondent Jackie DeAngelis is in New York tonight with analysis. Good evening, Jackie.\par \par \uc2 JACKIE DEANGELIS, FOX BUSINESS NETWORK CORRESPONDENT: Good evening, Shannon. Well, Wall Street hit the sell button hard this week, the Dow, the S&P 500, the NASDAQ all dropping for the week when all was said and done.\par \par \uc2 The S&P suffered its worst week since March of 2020. And on Wednesday, officially gave back all of its gains during the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 It all coincided with the Feds decision to raise interest rates by an aggressive three quarters of a point on Wednesday, a bump up not seen since 1994. The Fed is raising rates to try to tame inflation which is at a 40- year high at 8.6 percent .\par \par \uc2 Now, inflation is created when there's too much money chasing too few goods, raising rates slows down spending but it's a double edged sword. The concern is that this hike and more hikes this year will put the U.S. into a recession.\par \par \uc2 Some economists argue that the answer to inflation isn't as much about raising rates as it is about increasing supply and that Wall Street would like to see a different approach, like a change in energy policy to tame oil prices or incentives for farmers to help with food prices.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Well, Jackie, you've got some potential \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  news for us too, reportedly firing \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  employees who criticized him in a letter?\par \par \uc2 DEANGELIS: Yes, so \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  hasn't talked publicly about this Shannon, but several \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  employees drafted and circulated a letter criticizing Musk and his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  habits and asking executives at the company for more inclusivity.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  says that the company's president addressed this in an e-mail saying the employees were fired for making other staff feel "uncomfortable, intimidated and bullied and/or angry because the letter pressured them to sign on to something that did not reflect their views".\par \par \uc2 Now, of course, the irony here is that the musk \uc2 Twitter\uc2  deal is all about free speech, but it seems that Elon may not feel as passionately about empowering his employees in that way, Shannon.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: All right, the controversy continues. Jackie, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 Up next, former President Trump talks to face centered voters about the midterm elections. We're going to go live to Nashville.\par \par \uc2 First, here's what some of our Fox affiliates around the country are covering tonight. WBRC in Birmingham where three people are dead after a gunman opens fire at a suburban church during a Thursday evening potluck dinner. The 71-year-old suspect is in custody.\par \par \uc2 Fox 5 in New York where police are searching for five men behind dozens of ATM robberies in stores across Brooklyn and Queens.\par \par \uc2 Police say since December, the suspects have stolen at least 37 ATMs and two vehicles totaling more than $60,000.\par \par \uc2 And this is a live look at the San Francisco Bay Area from Fox 2, one of the big stories there tonight. The \uc2 Golden State Warriors\uc2  are \uc2 NBA\uc2  champs for the fourth time in eight seasons.\par \par \uc2 They defeated the \uc2 Boston Celtics\uc2  last night in game six of the finals. Steph Curry was named Most Valuable Player.\par \par \uc2 Golden States returned to victory comes two seasons after having the league's worst record.\par \par \uc2 That is tonight's live look outside the Beltway from SPECIAL REPORT. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 SHANNON BREAM, FOX NEWS CHANNEL ANCHOR (on camera): Federal regulators have authorized the first COVID-19 shots for infants and preschoolers. That paves the way for vaccinations to begin next week.\par \par \uc2 The Food and Drug Administration's action follows its advisory panel's unanimous recommendation for the shots from \uc2 Moderna\uc2  and \uc2 Pfizer\uc2 . That means U.S. kids under 5 are eligible for the shots. That totals about 18 million youngsters.\par \par \uc2 Former Trump White House official \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , pleading not guilty to contempt of Congress. Navarro appeared in federal court in Washington to be arraigned on the two counts indictments.\par \par \uc2 The charges were filed after he refused to cooperate with the congressional investigation into last year's Capitol riot.\par \par \uc2 Navarro has argued the select committee investigating the attack is itself unlawful, and therefore, a subpoena issued to him in February is unenforceable under law.\par \par \uc2 Faith-based voters are in Nashville tonight for a conference that is drawing some of the prospective Republican presidential candidates for 2024. The headliner today