ding those in elementary school, will face disciplinary action, including seat changes and counseling sessions, all over gender identification issues.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH TISLER, FAIRFAX COUNTY, VIRGINIA, PARENT: It means that they're putting way too much focus on a political agenda.\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH: Virginia's Governor, Republican Glenn Youngkin, campaigned heavily on efforts to address political correctness in schools.\par \par \uc2 GOV. GLENN YOUNGKIN, (R) VIRGINIA: We have to harness our outrage as we take back control from self-interested politicians.\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH: Today, while speaking in nearby Maryland at the annual PTA convention, first lady Jill Biden said education is being exploited for political purposes.\par \par \uc2 JILL BIDEN, U.S. FIRST LADY: We are reopening schools to class curriculum. We have been told that parents and teachers are at odds. But as I visit schools and I meet with families, that's not what I have seen.\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH: But polling suggests parents are at odds with some school boards, FOX finding 55 percent of registered voters want most elementary teachers banned from discussing sex and gender identity.\par \par \uc2 TISLER: This is developmentally inappropriate. These children aren't even taught what a pronoun is at the age of five.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH: But supporters of expanding gender discussions in classrooms insist new policies protect against discrimination and allow for more inclusive learning environment for all. But Shannon, this debate just keeps raging on.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: And we will track it. Mark, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 There is new evidence tonight of China's push to even the playing field in the Pacific and in the world. Beijing is unveiling its new aircraft carrier as it is signaling new support for Russia and its invasion of Ukraine. National security correspondent Jennifer Griffin has the latest tonight from the Pentagon.\par \par \uc2 