tee says Mr. Trump raised $250 million to fuel election challenges, much of it in small dollar donations.\par \par \uc2 REP. ZOE LOFGREN (D-CA): So, not only was there the big lie, there was the big rip off.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (on camera): Two more hearings this week on Wednesday, the push to get the DOJ involved in the election. Thursday, the pressure campaign on former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Chad, meantime, a coalition of bipartisan senators now has this agreement on a plan to curb gun violence. What's in that?\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM: Well, this was a breakthrough, 10 GOP senators support the plan, that is key if all 50 Democrats stick together, they can hit the magic number of 60 yeas and break a filibuster.\par \par \uc2 Now, the bill helps states set up their own red flag laws. It also enhances background checks for those younger than 21. And it requires a review of juvenile mental health records.\par \par \uc2 Now, liberals wanted to raise the age from 18 to 21 to buy assault weapons, but the GOP rejected that, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: We'll follow it. Chad, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Let's bring in Fox News Senior Political Analyst Brit Hume. Brit, good evening. Let's talk about this January 6 committee and what the ultimate goal is here as you watch it.\par \par \uc2 BRIT HUME, FOX NEWS SENIOR POLITICAL ANALYST: Well, there -- so far what they've laid out is a set of facts with which we've been familiar for what? Nearly two years now.\par \par \uc2 And you know, if their case was that Trump whipped up the crowd that brought him to -- that brought him to Washington to protest the theft of the election from him, that would be compelling and it would also be not new.\par \par \uc2 But the committee has a larger ambition, as we know, and that is not only to prove that Trump was responsible, which many of us had been saying for a couple of years, myself included.\par \par \uc2 But that this